WITH incoming AS MATERIALIZED (
  SELECT * FROM jsonb_to_recordset($nfl_articles_fc9b12c2cf17dc51$[{"source":"Action Network","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.actionnetwork.com/nfl/carolina-panthers-vs-green-bay-packers-prediction-pick-odds-nfl-thursday-night-football-october-29","canonical_url":"https://www.actionnetwork.com/nfl/carolina-panthers-vs-green-bay-packers-prediction-pick-odds-nfl-thursday-night-football-october-29","url_hash":"eb2102d24d97402eb9e90744583c9b551f80ba37e485392a58c91c262f1b2f25","content_hash":"f342b318b9a7e11206532d12648106f6ec1a81f25b236cb4981d91497e675c4f","title":"Panthers vs Packers Prediction, Pick, Odds for NFL Thursday Night Football on October 29","summary":"If you want more Action Network content, be sure to add us as a preferred source on Google. The Carolina Panthers (3-3) and Green Bay Packers (4-3) get NFL Week","published_at":"2026-10-29T14:16:01.000Z","confidence":0.74,"author":"Sean Koerner","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Turn your sports knowledge into winning\npredictions\n21+ or 18+ in Certain Locations. 19+ in ON. Please Play Responsibly. Gambling Problem? Call 1-800-GAMBLER. Visit connexontario.ca or Call 1-866-531-2600 in ON.\nNo Code Needed\nHome NFL\nPanthers vs Packers Prediction, Pick, Odds for NFL Thursday Night Football on October 29\nSean Koerner\nDirector of Predictive Analytics\nDownload App\nUpdated:\nOct 29, 2026, 10:16 AM EDT\nUpdated:\nOct 29, 2026, 10:16 AM EDT\n9 min read\nCredit: Reuters/Imagn. Pictured: Bryce Young, Jordan Love.\nIf you want more Action Network content, be sure to add us as a preferred source on Google .\nThe Carolina Panthers (3-3) and Green Bay Packers (4-3) get NFL Week 8 going tonight on Thursday Night Football. Kickoff is set for 8:15 p.m. ET from Lambeau Field in Green Bay, Wis. The game will broadcast live on Prime Video.\nThe Packers are 3.5-point favorites on the spread, with the over/under set at 47.5. Green Bay is a -192 moneyline favorite while Carolina is a +160 underdog.\nLet's get into my Panthers vs Packers predictions for Thursday Night Football .\nPanthers vs Packers Prediction\nPanthers vs Packers pick: Panthers Team Total Over 20.5 (-125) OR Over 21.5 (-105 to -115)\nMy Panthers vs Packers best bet is the Panthers to go over their team total. Make sure to find the best odds by checking our live NFL odds page.\nDownload the Action Network app now for more NFL picks and analysis!\nPanthers vs Packers Odds\nThursday, Oct. 29\n8:15 p.m. ET\nPrime Video\nPanthers Odds\nSpread Total Moneyline\n+3.5\n-108\n47.5\n-108o / -112u\n+160\nPackers Odds\nSpread Total Moneyline\n-3.5\n-112\n47.5\n-108o / -112u\n-192\nOdds via  DraftKings . Get up-to-the-minute  NFL odds here .\nPanthers vs Packers Moneyline : Panthers +160, Packers -192\nPanthers vs Packers Spread : Panthers +3.5, Packers -3.5\nPanthers vs Packers Total : 47.5\nPanthers vs Packers Thursday Night Football Preview\nWhen the Panthers Have the Ball\nBryce Young is a former No. 1 overall pick who had a brutal start to his career, but he’s gotten better each season and is coming off a career year in 2025 when he led the Panthers to the playoffs, albeit by winning what was easily the league’s worst division.\nHe’s taken another step forward this season and currently ranks 16th in EPA/dropback, the first year of his career he’s actually been positive in that metric .\nPanthers head coach Dave Canales and offensive coordinator Brad Idzik have helped by leaning heavily into play action. Young is using it on a career-high 32% of his dropbacks and he is averaging a career-best 8.0 yards per attempt off play action.\nThe supporting cast is also probably the best he’s had.\nTetairoa McMillan and Jalen Coker are quickly becoming one of the better young wide receiver duos in the league. Darren Waller has essentially become the pass-catching TE Carolina has been trying to find for Young, while John Metchie has stepped into the Xavier Legette WR3/slot role and might honestly be a better fit for this offense.\nCanales also handed play-calling duties to Idzik this year, and he’s responded with the third-highest pass rate over expected (PROE) in the league, which tells you how much more confidence this staff has in Young compared to earlier in his career.\nLast week, however, we saw Young's first implosion of the season against the Buccaneers . Young threw for only 163 yards with one touchdown and two interceptions in a 30-point loss — and the bigger issue was the protection.\nYoung faced a season-high 52% pressure rate even though Tampa only blitzed on 24% of his dropbacks . That means the Bucs were consistently getting pressure while sending four or fewer rushers, which is basically the worst possible setup for any quarterback.\nAnd Carolina's offensive line concerns aren’t going away on this short week.\nLT Rasheed Walker has struggled this season, LG Damien Lewis has been ruled out (with Corey Bullock replacing him), and RT Taylor Moton is done for the year. That forces first-round rookie Monroe Freeling into a full-time role earlier than Carolina probably would have preferred for someone who was viewed as more of a developmental prospect.\nThe Panthers' left side is especially concerning because that’s where Lukas Van Ness should line up most often. He’s having a career year and has stepped up in a big way while Green Bay continues to play without Micah Parsons as he works back from last year’s ACL tear. Young could absolutely be facing elevated pressure again.\nBut Carolina also has a pretty obvious counter available: dial the pass rate back a little, lean more on running back Chuba Hubbard , and use the run game to create cleaner play-action opportunities for the passing game.\nThat’s where this matchup gets interesting.\nHubbard ranks sixth among qualified RBs with 3.8 yards after contact per carry . Green Bay has been excellent at initiating contact, allowing the third-fewest yards before contact, but once backs get through that first wave, the Packers are allowing the seventh-most yards after contact.\nTheir LB room has also taken some hits. Edgerrin Cooper is on IR, Zaire Franklin is out with a shin injury, and Ty’Ron Hopper will be asked to take on an every down role despite being shaky in run support.\nCarolina may get stuffed at times, but I think the better approach is to stay patient with Hubbard. If he gets through the first level, there should be opportunities for chunk gains.\nAnd if that gets Green Bay’s front playing the run honestly, it should make life much easier on Young through play action.\nThat’s probably the best path for this offense to bounce back from last week. Not asking Young to drop back 40 times behind a shaky offensive line, but using Hubbard to keep the Packers honest and creating more efficient passing opportunities for a QB who has been excellent off play action this year.\nSmart betting starts here\nKoerner's player prop & TD projections\nTail picks the sharps are betting\nMoney percentages, profitable systems & more\nTRY PRO NOW\nWhen the Packers Have the Ball\nThis is probably the most fascinating matchup in the game.\nGreen Bay has been completely inept running the football, while Carolina has been one of the easiest defenses in the\nleague to run against.\nAccording to Next Gen Stats, this is the first matchup after Week 8 since 2019 featuring the team averaging the fewest rushing yards per game against the defense allowing the most rushing yards per game.\nSo if the Packers are ever going to get their run game back on track, this would seemingly be the spot.\nJosh Jacobs averaged just 3.3 yards per carry last week in his season debut. But the bigger issue all season has been the offensive line.\nThe injury problems continue here. C Sean Rhyan and RG Travis Glover are both out on the short week. Kevin Zeitler could make his season debut after signing a few weeks ago, which might help, but there’s still enough instability up front that I’m not convinced Green Bay suddenly becomes an efficient rushing offense simply because Carolina is a favorable matchup.\nThat’s what makes this such an unusual setup for the Panthers defense.\nMost teams have been able to attack Carolina’s biggest weakness directly by running the ball. Green Bay might be one of the few teams that simply isn’t equipped to do that as effectively as everyone else.\nThat likely puts more of the game on Jordan Love and the passing attack.\nCarolina has quietly been solid against the pass, ranking 14th in pass defense DVOA, while allowing explosive passes at the second-lowest rate in the league and disguising coverage pre-snap at the second-highest rate .\nThat’s noteworthy against Love because he’s one of the more aggressive downfield passers in football and has seen his efficiency dip somewhat against disguised coverage.\nAt the same time, Love, Christian Watson , Matthew Golden and Tucker Kraft are all playing at a high level, and Green Bay is going to challenge downfield much more aggressively than some of the offenses the Panthers have faced.\nThat makes Green Bay’s offense a pretty unique matchup for Carolina.\nIf the Packers can’t rush efficiently and Carolina continues limiting explosives, Green Bay could end up in more obvious passing situations and 3rd-and-longs that lead to quicker possessions.\nIf Love does connect on those downfield shots, Green Bay can score quickly and get Carolina’s offense right back on the field anyway.\nSo whether Green Bay struggles to sustain drives or starts hitting explosives through the air, there’s a reasonable path to the Panthers getting more possessions than usual.\nAnd that becomes important when looking at Carolina’s team total.\nPanthers vs Packers Prediction, Betting Analysis\nI’m pretty much in line with the full-game side and total here, and there are sharp cases to be made on basically every angle in this game. That’s usually true, but even more than normal here — this was a tricky game to cap.\nThe side where I think the widest range of outcomes exists is the Packers' team total.\nMaybe their run game takes advantage of the matchup and Jordan Love stays efficient enough through the air to put up a big number. Or maybe the offensive line issues continue, the run game struggles, and Carolina’s ability to limit explosives keeps the Packers offense from taking off.\nThat part of the game feels much more volatile to me.\nInstead of trying to guess which version of the Packers offense shows up, I’d rather isolate the Panthers offense bouncing back.\nLast week was brutal, but it came in what has still been a breakout year for Bryce Young. He’s playing the best football of his career, the supporting cast is much better, and the play-action game has been a real strength.\nThe obvious concern is the offensive as Young could absolutely face another elevated pressure rate tonight. But I believe Carolina has a pretty clear adjustment available to them: lean on Chuba Hubbard, stay patient with the run game, and use that to create cleaner play-action opportunities for Young. That should also help keep the Packers' pass rush honest.\nI also think there’s a sneaky pace element here. Both teams play fast, and Green Bay’s offensive style could create more Carolina possessions whether the Packers are succeeding or failing.\nIf Green Bay still can’t run and gets stuck in 3rd-and-longs, that can lead to shorter possessions. If Love hits those aggressive downfield shots, the Packers can score quickly and get Carolina the ball back that way instead.\nI don’t necessarily need to be right about the Packers offense here. I just think Carolina is in a good spot to bounce back after last week, and I’d rather bet on that than try to predict the much wider range of outcomes on the Green Bay side.\nThere’s also the Ryan Fitzgerald factor. The Panthers kicker is somehow 12-for-17 on extra-point attempts this season, which is either the beginning of a terrifying case of the yips or just an absurdly unsustainable miss rate for an NFL kicker on what are essentially chip shots.\nI’m obviously not betting this because I expect him to suddenly become perfect, but simply converting extra points at something closer to a normal NFL rate going forward can only help Carolina’s scoring floor.\nI’m buying the point and taking Panthers Team Total Over 20.5 (-125) because 21 is a key number for team totals. I’m also completely fine with Over 21.5 if the adjusted price is somewhere around -105 to -115.\nIn a game where I’m basically in line with the side and total, this is the market where I think I can avoid the biggest uncertainty and isolate the part of the matchup I trust more.\nPick: Panthers Team Total Over 20.5 (-125) OR Over 21.5 (-105 to -115)\nPanthers vs Packers Betting Trends\nPanthers vs Packers Weather\nGet the latest coverage on NFL Weather .\nFree Guide: 10 Tips to Hit Bigger Same Game Parlays More Often\n10 real, data-backed strategies for SGP bettors. Just enter your email and we'll send it.\nAbout the Author\nSean Koerner leads predictive analytics at Action Network, specializing in sports projections and fantasy rankings. With over 20 years of experience, he's a top expert in the field, consistently ranking first in the FantasyPros Accuracy standings multiple times. Known for his in-depth content on NFL betting and fantasy football, Sean also co-hosts popular podcasts and can do projections for all sports, making him a go-to source for accurate sports predictions.\nFollow @ The_Oddsmaker on X\nThis site contains commercial content . We may be compensated for the links provided on this page. The content on this page is for informational purposes only. Action Network makes no representation or warranty as to the accuracy of the information given or the outcome of any game or event.\nTop Stories\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Anytime Touchdown Props for NFL Thursday Night Football\nGilles Gallant\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Player Props for Josh Jacobs and Savion Wil