t luck factor.\nIn Version 3.1, if the Luck Score is 1.9 or higher, we'll consider that a luck-based side. A 1.5-1.9 is considered a lean and won't count toward official Luck Rankings statistics.\nLast weekend, the unlucky team for the luck-based sides went 1-0 ATS, moving these to a 5-2 (71.4%) record on the season and 87-45 overall (65.9%)\nFor totals, a Luck Total above +1.5 (over) or below -1.5 (under) is considered official for Luck Rankings record keeping, but as in years past this doesn't start until Week 3.\nBased on our  Week 8 NFL Luck Rankings , we have the first (post-Week 1) luck-free slate since we introduced the Luck Rankings in 2022. Amazingly enough, there aren't even any \"leans\" this week for games that get close to our thresholds.\nThe closest things to a lean for a side would be the Jets as the unlucky side against Raiders, and the Ravens as the unlucky side against the Bills a close second. For a total, the Cardinals-Cowboys under is the only one close.\nSo, no breakdown of any games this week from me from the luck perspective. But here's the full slate listed below in case you are interested anyway!\nNFL Luck Rankings Week 8 Games\nTop Stories\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Prediction, Pick, Odds for NFL Thursday Night Football on October 29\nSean Koerner\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Anytime Touchdown Props for NFL Thursday Night Football\nGilles Gallant\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Player Props for Josh Jacobs and Savion Williams\nSam Farley\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Spread Prediction: Pros Betting This 57% ATS System\nPJ Walsh\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Playoff Picture: Week 8 AFC Division Odds & Futures Reset\nBrandon Anderson\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Week 8 Pick’em, Confidence Pool Picks, Projections, Ratings\nSean Koerner\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Betting Primer: Trends, Stats, Systems for Every Game\nEvan Abrams\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Power Rankings Week 8: Dolphins Mo