e NFL\nNFL Week 8 Pick’em, Confidence Pool Picks, Projections, Ratings\nSean Koerner\nDirector of Predictive Analytics\nDownload App\nUpdated:\nOct 28, 2026, 03:32 PM EDT\nUpdated:\nOct 28, 2026, 03:32 PM EDT\n1 min read\nPRO\nCredit: USA TODAY Network via Reuters Connect. Pictured: Joe Burrow.\nTo help you make NFL Week 8 pick'em picks, I've ranked straight-up (SU) and against-the-spread (ATS) options by confidence below.\nThese rankings are based on my power ratings, which help power our NFL PRO Projections . They account for various factors, such as injuries and travel.\nThese NFL Week 8 rankings will be constantly updated throughout the week — be sure to bookmark this story and check it again, especially since I’ll be able to better grasp what spreads I like.\nFollow me in the Action App for notifications when I lock in my NFL betting picks for Week 8.\nNFL Week 8 Pick'em, Confidence Ratings\nTop Stories\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Prediction, Pick, Odds for NFL Thursday Night Football on October 29\nSean Koerner\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Anytime Touchdown Props for NFL Thursday Night Football\nGilles Gallant\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Player Props for Josh Jacobs and Savion Williams\nSam Farley\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Spread Prediction: Pros Betting This 57% ATS System\nPJ Walsh\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Playoff Picture: Week 8 AFC Division Odds & Futures Reset\nBrandon Anderson\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Betting Primer: Trends, Stats, Systems for Every Game\nEvan Abrams\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Power Rankings Week 8: Dolphins Move Up in Luck Rankings\nNick Giffen\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Week 8 Luck Rankings Picks: The First Luck-Free Slate In 5 Years\nNick Giffen\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\n2026 Live NFL Quarterback Power Rankings: Every QB’s Value Against the Spread\nEvan Abrams\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nBookBias: The NFL Public Betting Database for QBs, Coaches & Teams\nEvan Abrams\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Anytime Touchdown Machine: Live TD Odds, Trends and More\nEvan Abrams\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nFree Guide: 10 Tips to Hit Bigger Same Game Parlays More Often\n10 real, data-backed strategies for SGP bettors. Just enter your email and we'll send it.\nFollow Us On Social","revision_hash":"a313e3b58c1a2be03a7f51b1e48e06da3ea6af74e55cccbfed7505ad229df269"},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-betting-primer-panthers-vs-packers-picks/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-betting-primer-panthers-vs-packers-picks/","url_hash":"0dd7dfd35328e278413cae399f5be944266536df4416b8eec74d2cbcf308f0c5","content_hash":"949be288503e4995b33c49e934e175c5679830ba669261529e29a7279e56197c","title":"NFL Thursday Night Football Betting Primer: Panthers vs Packers Picks","summary":"Welcome back to another edition of our NFL Thursday Night Football Betting Primer. NFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet Expert NFL Game Picks NFL Betting Strategy Best +EV NFL Picks Can the Cardiac Cats bounce back versus the Pack? Let&#8217;s break down the sides and totals to see what&#8217;s the best angle to bet on for [&#8230;] The post NFL Thursday Night Football Betting Primer: Panthers vs Packers Picks appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:56:58.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Andrew Erickson","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Welcome back to another edition of our NFL Thursday Night Football Betting Primer .\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nCan the Cardiac Cats bounce back versus the Pack?\nLet's break down the sides and totals to see what's the best angle to bet on for TNF.\nLFG.\nPrime-Time Highlight (Through Week 7)\nLeague-wide in 2026, Thursday-night underdogs are 5-2 ATS (seven games, including the Melbourne opener) and favorites are 2-5; the O/U is 4-3 toward the Over. Across all 22 prime-time games (Wednesday opener, TNF, SNF and MNF), underdogs are 14-7-1 ATS and favorites 7-14-1, with the O/U split 11-11.\nGreen Bay's one TNF game this season was a 35-14 home loss to Atlanta as a 4.5-point favorite; Carolina's one prime-time game was the Week 4 Sunday-night win over Detroit as a 3.5-point underdog.\nNFL Thursday Night Football Betting Primer: Carolina Panthers vs. Green Bay Packers\nBetting Lines & Odds\nErickson's Pick: Panthers +3.5\nTrends\nCarolina has covered the spread in 12 straight games following a loss, dating back to last season. So far, that trend has continued in 2026. The Panthers are 2-0 ATS after a loss: a 34-3 win at Atlanta in Week 2 (as a 2.5-point road favorite, after the Week 1 loss to Chicago) and a 32-26 win over Detroit in Week 4 (as a 3.5-point home underdog, after the Week 3 loss at Cleveland). Thursday's game is their next after-a-loss test, following a 43-13 home loss to Tampa Bay in Week 7 (where they failed to cover the -2.5 spread by more than 30 points).\nLeague-wide, teams coming off a loss by 20 or more points are 12-3-1 ATS in 2026 (16 games, through Week 7). That includes Carolina's own Week 2 cover after its 59-37 loss to Chicago. Green Bay is the lone push in that group (Week 4 at Tampa Bay, after the 35-14 home loss to Atlanta). Again, Carolina lost by 30 on Sunday.\nAs a road team, Carolina is 2-1 ATS and 0-3 O/U in 2026 (a cover at Atlanta, a non-cover at Cleveland, and a cover at Philadelphia, all as a road favorite; all three went Under). The Panthers have not been a road underdog yet this season (0 games). As an underdog overall, they are 1-1 ATS and 2-0 O/U (both at home: a non-cover against Chicago and a cover against Detroit).\nAcross all 2026 games, Carolina is 3-3 ATS and 3-3 O/U.\nAs a home favorite (the role it plays here), Green Bay is 1-1 ATS and 1-1 O/U in 2026 (2 games: a Week 3 non-cover against Atlanta and a Week 6 cover against Dallas as a 1.5-point favorite). Overall: across all home games, 2-1 ATS and 1-2 O/U (the Week 5 win over Chicago came as a 1.5-point underdog); across all games as a favorite, 1-2-1 ATS and 1-3 O/U; across all 2026 games, 3-3-1 ATS and 2-5 O/U.\nCarolina's road games have stayed Under the total four straight (2025 Week 18 at Tampa Bay, then 2026 Weeks 2, 3 and 6 at closing totals of 44.5, 42.5 and 39.5). This game's total of roughly 47.5 is higher than any Carolina road game this season.\nGreen Bay has also stayed Under in four straight (Weeks 4 through 7). On the other side, the Panthers are Over-leaning after a loss (16-7 O/U since 2024) and have gone Over in all three home games in 2026.\nStreaks through Week 7. CAR: 3-3 straight up (1-game losing streak), 3-3 against the spread (1-game non-cover streak), 3-3 toward the total (1-game Over streak). GB: 4-3 straight up (1-game losing streak), 3-3-1 against the spread (3-game cover streak across Weeks 5-7, with the Week 4 push before it), 2-5 toward the total (4-game Under streak).\nGreen Bay has covered three straight, but before that they were riding a GB 0-9-1 record ATS since they lost Micah Parsons. Officially 3-9-1 ATS in last 13 games.\nBoth teams are on a short week after playing Sunday. Carolina lost 43-13 at home to Tampa Bay as a 3-point favorite; Green Bay lost 20-17 at Detroit but covered as a 3.5-point road underdog.\nHome favorites have struggled across the league this season: 25-32-2 ATS in 2026 (neutral-site games excluded), and 11-10-1 ATS when laying between 3 and 4 points.\nInjuries\nCAR OLB Jaelan Phillips (hamstring): did not practice Monday or Tuesday; he missed Week 7, and he will be out another week.\nCAR RT Taylor Moton (fractured fibula): hurt in the Week 7 loss and placed on injured reserve Monday.\nCAR G Damien Lewis (knee) and G Torricelli Simpkins III (ankle): did not practice Monday or Tuesday. Both are out.\nGB WR Matthew Golden (shoulder/foot): did not practice Monday or Tuesday. Zach Kruse of Packers Wire wrote that Golden and G/T Travis Glover are in danger of missing Thursday; Matt LaFleur said he hopes Golden plays.\nGB C Sean Rhyan (high ankle sprain): did not practice Monday or Tuesday; LaFleur does not expect him back Thursday, and earlier reports say he may miss multiple weeks. Backup C Jacob Monk (quad) was placed on injured reserve. John Williams (second-year tackle) filled in at center in Week 7 and may start there again; Green Bay signed OL Mekhi Becton from the practice squad as they continue to deal with offensive line injuries.\nGB LG Aaron Banks (knee/toe): limited Monday and Tuesday (full on Wednesday).\nGB LB Zaire Franklin (shin): hairline fracture; did not practice Monday or Tuesday and is out. He has not been placed on injured reserve.\nGB DT Devonte Wyatt (ankle): did not practice Monday, limited Tuesday; he left the Week 7 game in the first half but returned.\nPanthers added K Ryan Fitzgerald to the injury report with an illness. He does not have a game designation, so is expected to play.\n- Joe Person (@josephperson) October 28, 2026\nThe full report shows Matthew Golden went from estimated DNP to limited, which is a good indicator that he's trending towards playing. https://t.co/lVvxPIKRYa pic.twitter.com/5lKlaQdQOy\n- Rob Demovsky (@RobDemovsky) October 28, 2026\nBetting Preview\nCarolina is 7-0 ATS on the road following a loss, and underdogs have won four straight games at Lambeau Field. The Panthers have been one of the marquee teams to bet on after big losses, and Green Bay is just 6-11 ATS as a favorite since the start of last season (1-2-1 ATS as a favorite this season).\nTherefore, my best bet in this game is the Panthers catching the 3.5.\nThey have covered 12 straight following a loss, and both after-loss games this season were covers, including the 34-3 win at Atlanta after the Week 1 blowout by Chicago. Now they come off a 43-13 home loss to Tampa Bay, and teams coming off a loss of 20 or more points are 12-3-1 ATS this season.\nAdd in Thursday-night underdogs at 5-2 ATS and prime-time underdogs at 14-7-1, and getting more than a field goal is a number I want to take. Shop for the +4.\nUnderstandably, I get some reservations about Carolina given they are missing so many key pieces on their offensive line, at edge, and at cornerback. But this has been the case for most of the season. Meanwhile, it's not like Green Bay is far up in the trust tree given their own offensive line woes.\nThe total is a push-and-pull at 47.5. It is higher than any Carolina road game this season, and the Panthers have stayed Under in all three road games, and Green Bay has gone Under four straight. But Carolina is Over-leaning after a loss, and both offenses will be working through offensive line injuries on a short week.\nSavion Williams caught 3 of 3 for 47 yards and ran twice for 4 (6.4% adjusted, from 11.4%) in Week 7. Snap share: 40 of 67 (60%), from 40 of 75 (53%).\nThe Packers No. 3 WR has been operating in the \"Jayden Reed\" role as the third receiver on 60% of the snaps, with two big catches that were conversions on 3 total targets. He has at least 3 catches in both games this season (7 total targets) while seeing both designed targets near the line of scrimmage (1.5 air yards per target in Week 6) and downfield looks (2 10-plus air yard targets in Week 7). With Matthew Golden banged up, we could see more of Williams. The second-year WR is already seeing his role expand over the last two games.\nI think that continues in Week 8. Williams had 2 catches for 12 yards when GB played Carolina last year on just a 30% snap share (his 2025 season high).\nChuba Hubbard has hit over 85.5 rushing + receiving yards in 4 of his 6 games played this season (including 3 of last 4), and gone over in all three non-blowout games for Carolina in 2026.\nAnd even though he fell short last week, it was a tougher matchup versus Tampa Bay (still totaled 11 touches for 60 yards in three quarters, and actually had 90 yards from scrimmage in total but had a gain wiped away on a flag).\nPer Next Gen Stats,  Hubbard has been contacted at or behind the line of scrimmage on 45.8% of his carries this season but has gained positive yardage on 79.5% of those carries, the highest rate among running backs (min. 40 carries). 92.0% of the rushing yards GB has allowed have come after contact, the highest rate. Green Bay has allowed 224 yards on designed runs contacted at or behind the line of scrimmage this season, the most in the NFL and 64 more than any other defense.\nGiven Hubbard's bell-cow status as both a rusher/receiver, I think he piles up yardage. It's a 5-star bet on the Prop Bet Cheat Sheet this week for Thursday Night Football. Through 6 games played this season, Hubbard has found the end zone in 4 of them. GB is allowing 1.3 rushing TDs/game to opposing RBs.\nFor a long-shot first TD play…Jalen Coker at 13-1 odds. Bryce Young missed him on a deep target last week that would have been an easy TD score. Highest-rated 1st TD bet on the BettingPros First Touchdown Scorer Report .\nPlayer Props\nSavion Williams OVER 2.5 receptions\nChuba Hubbard OVER 85.5 rushing+receiving yards\nChuba Hubbard anytime TD (-104)","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/best-nfl-player-props-thursday-night-football-panthers-vs-packers-week-8-2026/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/best-nfl-player-props-thursday-night-football-panthers-vs-packers-week-8-2026/","url_hash":"99268afad36bfce6bafdb5b12dabf2a9c849e0d519770e7d1f3cbb7059069a64","content_hash":"6f261c1e7296744bc055e3031e8b0cb11eb066878a2886b1503a0e68b17a124b","title":"Best NFL Player Props: Thursday Night Football (Panthers vs. Packers)","summary":"The Carolina Panthers visit the Green Bay Packers at Lambeau Field for Thursday Night Football on October 29, kicking off Week 8 with Green Bay favored by 3.5 points and the total set at 47.5. Our best Panthers vs. Packers player props draw on the BettingPros Prop Bet Cheat Sheet, which has generated +31 units [&#8230;] The post Best NFL Player Props: Thursday Night Football (Panthers vs. Packers) appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:56:45.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"BettingPros Staff","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"The Carolina Panthers visit the Green Bay Packers at Lambeau Field for Thursday Night Football on October 29, kicking off Week 8 with Green Bay favored by 3.5 points and the total set at 47.5. Our best Panthers vs. Packers player props draw on the BettingPros Prop Bet Cheat Sheet, which has generated +31 units and a 3.6% ROI across 872 NFL picks this season, with four consecutive winning weeks. Passing yards props have led the way with a 59.4% win rate and +38.2 units, while anytime touchdown picks have delivered +14.3 units and a 15.7% ROI. Below, we break down our favorite Thursday Night Football player props using the cheat sheet's projections to identify potential betting value.\nTop NFL Picks\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nNFL Player Props Rankings & Predictions: Panthers vs. Packers (Thursday Night Football)\nWe compiled several projection sources to come up with consensus projections . We then compared these projections to the NFL player prop bet odds from the sportsbooks to give you the best NFL player prop bet picks . View the best player prop bets for this week's slate with our NFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet .\nBest NFL Player Props for Thursday Night Football: Panthers vs. Packers\nThrough Week 6, the Packers had a 7.8% pass rate over expected (PROE). In Josh Jacobs' Week 7 return, Green Bay had a 6.4% PROE. It was a small step back, but it was something. Meanwhile, Carolina's defense ranks 29th in PROE against (-2.6%) this season, and they were just curbstomped by Tampa Bay's rushing attack. Tampa Bay's trio of Bucky Irving, Kenneth Gainwell and Sean Tucker rumbled for 246 yards and 5.47 yards per carry.\nIt was the second time a team's backfield exceeded 200 rushing yards against the Panthers this season. Carolina has allowed the most rushing yards per game (126.8) and yards per carry (5.21) to running backs this season. D'Andre Swift (124 rushing yards), Irving (106 rushing yards), Kyle Monangai (100 rushing yards), Gainwell (88 rushing yards), Bijan Robinson (72 rushing yards) and Quinshon Judkins (70 rushing yards) each surpassed 59.5 rushing yards against the Panthers this season.\nJacobs is once again the Packers' lead back. In his first game of the season, he handled 11 of Green Bay's backfield's 17 rush attempts (64.7%). Jacobs managed only 36 rushing yards on 11 carries for 3.27 yards per carry. Nevertheless, his workload was rock-solid, and if he shook off some rust, he could be more efficient and take a larger piece of the pie against Carolina's pitiful run defense. Jacobs topped 59.5 rushing yards in nine of 16 games last season, and he should clear the over on Thursday for the first time this season.\nOur NFL Player Prop Bet Cheat Sheet assists bettors by comparing lines from leading sportsbooks with our daily NFL projections.\nJosh Jacobs Over 59.5 Rushing Yards ( -114 )\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet Picks & Predictions: Panthers vs. Packers\nWhat is an NFL player prop bet?\nAn NFL player prop bet is a type of wager where you're betting on the performance of a specific player in a game rather than the overall outcome. For example, you might place a bet on how many passing yards a quarterback will throw for, or how many touchdowns a running back will score. It's a fun way to get more invested in the action, especially if you're confident in how a particular player will perform, regardless of who wins or loses the game. It's like focusing on one slice of the pie instead of the whole thing.\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nSubscribe:  Apple Podcasts  |  Spotify  |  Google Podcasts | RadioPublic  |  Breaker  |  Castbox  |  Pocket Casts\nWhether you're new to sports betting or a betting pro, our   Sports Betting Strategy and Advice  page is for you. You can get started with our 101 section - including   10 Sports Betting Tips for Beginners  - or head to more advanced strategy - like   Key Numbers When Betting Against the Spread  - to learn more.","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-player-props-bets-panthers-vs-packers/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-player-props-bets-panthers-vs-packers/","url_hash":"9dc415ae07b123f2dcc969e88a11bc8f5c2c08f8c5fc149975c238d392beedea","content_hash":"39754c8f43a4a2f4a82c3c94518b1ed0df749201e58ce51f48b713fc01b0c4d3","title":"NFL Thursday Night Football Player Props &#038; Bets: Panthers vs. Packers","summary":"Week 8 kicks off tonight. The first seven weeks have certainly been entertaining. With the trade deadline looming, one or two moves will likely increase the season&#8217;s excitement. Let’s jump right into our favorite NFL Thursday Night Football player props for Panthers vs. Bears. More NFL Betting Advice NFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet Expert NFL [&#8230;] The post NFL Thursday Night Football Player Props &#038; Bets: Panthers vs. Packers appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:19:40.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Steve Krebs","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Week 8 kicks off tonight. The first seven weeks have certainly been entertaining. With the trade deadline looming, one or two moves will likely increase the season's excitement. Let's jump right into our favorite NFL Thursday Night Football player props for Panthers vs. Bears.\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nNFL Thursday Night Football Player Props: Panthers vs. Packers\n(Odds courtesy of FanDuel Sportsbook ) \nJordan Love 2+ Passing Touchdowns ( -154 )\nThe juice on this selection is getting a bit out of control. If you want to add this prop to your bets this evening, get it in early. At this rate, Jordan Love's total touchdowns could climb to three. You can also consider Love to pass for 100+ yards ( -125 ) in each half if the juice on the touchdowns isn't your speed.\nLove has thrown for at least two touchdowns in six out of seven games this season. Given the high tax on the success rate, oddsmakers are clearly expecting the young quarterback to sling two touchdowns against Carolina. Love has thrown at least two touchdowns in three out of four home games dating back to last season.\nChuba Hubbard Anytime Touchdown Scorer ( -115 )\nYou can throw away Chuba Hubbard's performance last week in what was a complete nightmare for the Carolina Panthers. Hubbard rushed for a season-low seven attempts. Before Sunday, Hubbard scored three touchdowns in two games. The Panthers running back has scored in four out of six games.\nCarolina had made a strong effort to get the running game going over the last three weeks - before playing Tampa on Sunday. Hubbard rushed for 67 carries over three contests, with at least 19 attempts per contest. Jalen Coker and Tetairoa McMillan have combined for four touchdowns this season and haven't crossed the goal line since Week 4. If Carolina wants to meet its expectation of 22+ points, we expect Hubbard to account for at least one touchdown.\nJosh Jacobs 3+ Receptions ( -135 )\nOur next selection is somewhat surprising given the immediate role Josh Jacobs played in the passing game on Sunday. In his first game back, Jacobs was targeted on seven passes and caught five. His receiving yardage prop is highly tempting at 20+ for a +105 return. Ultimately, we are going to play it safe and back Jacobs' receptions.\nSince last season, Jacobs has finished with three or more receptions in six out of the last 10 games. The Green Bay running back caught four passes in the Packers' loss to the Panthers last season. Jordan Love has attempted 86 passes over the previous two contests. With that volume, Jacobs is a strong candidate to reach the three-reception threshold.\nSavion Williams 25+ Receiving Yards   ( -114 )\nWe close out the night with our sweatiest selection of all. Savion Williams has cleared 25 yards in two consecutive games. With limited options at wide receiver for Green Bay, Williams is being asked to take on a bigger role. He has responded with 69 yards in the last two games.\nWilliams has caught every target thrown his way, showing his reliability. With most coverage focused on Christian Watson and Matthew Golden, Williams should find some open looks downfield. He has cleared 30+ yards in each game this season, so 25+ yards seems reasonable at almost even money.","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-same-game-parlay-panthers-vs-packers/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-same-game-parlay-panthers-vs-packers/","url_hash":"02aaf8efe57ac9124028039aab4b5c5ee0f4ab578ab192fe58da01dd944975e5","content_hash":"f31d46f1fe59d2189aeb4f60449e7ea13ddfb478ae0b63c27c3e31b32ff7dafb","title":"NFL Thursday Night Football Same Game Parlay: Panthers vs. Packers","summary":"We&#8217;re heading into Week 8 of the 2026-2027 NFL season, and the Green Bay Packers kick things off by hosting the Carolina Panthers. The Packers are coming off a 20-17 road loss to the Detroit Lions, while the Panthers are coming off a 43-13 home loss to the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. The Packers are 4-3, [&#8230;] The post NFL Thursday Night Football Same Game Parlay: Panthers vs. Packers appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-29T09:29:19.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Richard Janvrin","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"We're heading into Week 8 of the 2026-2027 NFL season, and the Green Bay Packers kick things off by hosting the Carolina Panthers. The Packers are coming off a 20-17 road loss to the Detroit Lions, while the Panthers are coming off a 43-13 home loss to the Tampa Bay Buccaneers. The Packers are 4-3, while the Panthers are 3-3. The Packers are last in the NFC North, while the Panthers cling to first in the NFC South. This game could have major implications for playoff spots down the line, whether it's a division title or a Wild Card spot. Below is our best NFL Thursday Night Football same game parlay (SGP ) for Panthers vs. Packers.\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nNFL Thursday Night Football Same Game Parlay: Panthers vs. Packers\n(Odds Courtesy of DraftKings Sportsbook )\nCarolina Panthers at Green Bay Packers\nLeg 1: Carolina Panthers Moneyline ( +160 )\nFor the first leg of this parlay, I'm swinging big with a Panthers outright win.\nThe Packers play varied coverages, but they play Cover 2 more than any other team. Against Cover 2, Panthers quarterback Bryce Young has been excellent. He's completed 18-of-26 passes for 328 yards (12.6 yards per attempt) and one touchdown. On the flip side, the Panthers mostly play Cover 3. Packers quarterback Jordan Love has completed fewer than 60% of his passes for 630 yards (7.2 yards per attempt), three touchdowns and three interceptions against Cover 3.\nThe Panthers are dreadful against the run, and the Packers' running game has been, too, averaging fewer than 60 yards per game.\nAs for the Panthers' running game, they'll have a chance to beat up on the Packers, who allow 95.1 rushing yards and 1.3 rushing touchdowns per game. Panthers running back Chuba Hubbard has run for 120+ yards in two of the last three games.\nI expect a close game here, and would be totally content if you pivoted to Panthers +3.5 ( -108 ).\nLeg 2: Chuba Hubbard Anytime Touchdown Scorer ( -120 )\nOver the last three games, Chuba Hubbard has handled 78.6% of the Panthers' running back carries. In that span, he's recorded 61 touches (20.3 per game) and three touchdowns. A whopping 41.8% of his carries have gone for at least five yards.\nNow, Hubbard faces a Packers defense that allows running backs 23.71 carries for 95.1 yards and 1.3 rushing touchdowns per game. In the passing game, they allow running backs 4.4 catches for 33 yards per game. Hubbard has an 8.5% target share, catching 15 passes for 112 yards and two touchdowns.\nHubbard is in a fantastic spot to score.\nLeg 3: Tucker Kraft Anytime Touchdown Scorer ( +165 )\nTucker Kraft enters Week 8 with two touchdowns this season, including one last week. Now, he faces a Panthers defense that has allowed four touchdowns to tight ends this season.\nAs mentioned, the Panthers primarily play Cover 3. Against this coverage, Kraft has caught 11 passes for 95 yards and a touchdown. His reception percentage is the highest on the team among players with at least 10 targets against Cover 3.\nGiven the Panthers' recent coverage against tight ends, including allowing seven receptions for 65 yards to Eagles tight ends and nine catches for 92 yards and a touchdown to Lions tight ends, I'll roll the dice on Kraft.\nParlay Odds: +1000","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-td-scorers-picks-panthers-vs-packers/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-td-scorers-picks-panthers-vs-packers/","url_hash":"f86ae81a95685f426a50ca96ad43fc7218842d911f95d4f701388579c0db2de7","content_hash":"21ae1c8611515b4b5236fb6431cbf4a3b111ed76225dd736e381222ba6fd3be5","title":"NFL Thursday Night Football TD Scorers Picks: Panthers vs. Packers","summary":"We&#8217;ve had six consecutive profitable weeks on our NFL Thursday Night Football TD scorers picks after cashing in on D&#8217;Andre Swift&#8217;s first touchdown scorer odds (+600) in Week 7. This week&#8217;s Panthers-Packers tilt features a Carolina team that just allowed 43 points to Tampa Bay, while Green Bay boasts one of the league&#8217;s most lethal [&#8230;] The post NFL Thursday Night Football TD Scorers Picks: Panthers vs. Packers appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-29T09:29:13.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Mike Spector","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"We've had six consecutive profitable weeks on our NFL Thursday Night Football TD scorers picks after cashing in on D'Andre Swift's first touchdown scorer odds (+600) in Week 7.\nThis week's Panthers-Packers tilt features a Carolina team that just allowed 43 points to Tampa Bay, while Green Bay boasts one of the league's most lethal wide receiver duos. Will either of them be in my first touchdown or anytime touchdown predictions?\nHere are the best touchdown scorer picks for Week 8's Thursday Night Football contest between the Panthers and Packers.\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nNFL Thursday Night Football TD Scorers Picks: Panthers vs. Packers\n(Odds courtesy of DraftKings Sportsbook )\nChristian Watson First Touchdown Scorer ( +850 )\nGreen Bay leads the NFL with over 80% of its offensive yardage coming via the pass. So while the Carolina defense is coming off a game where it allowed the second-most rushing yards of any team this season, it's wise to start stockpiling your touchdown scorer portfolios for this game with Packers pass-catchers.\nGreen Bay averages more than four explosive pass plays per game, the league's highest rate. That is why I'm higher on Christian Watson as the game's first touchdown scorer rather than going with a safer running back play, not to mention how often Jordan Love has looked his way.\nWatson ranks in the top 24 among wide receivers in target share (21.3%) and his team's air yards share (31.4%), and in the top 10 in yards per route run.\nLove averaged 7.8 yards per attempt and threw two touchdowns the last time he faced Panthers defensive coordinator Ejiro Evero. All but three of Green Bay's touchdowns have come via the pass.\nTetairoa McMillan Anytime Touchdown Scorer ( +180 )\nFellow Panthers wide receiver Jalen Coker was nicked up with a shoulder injury last week. That has me looking to Tetairoa McMillan as Carolina's top pass-catching option.\nCarolina has scored 23.25 more points than its implied totals, the third-highest in the league. A lot of that is due to quarterback Bryce Young's improvement in several key areas. Over seven weeks, Young is on pace for a single-season high in air yards per attempt (seventh). He is also in the top 12 in explosive pass rate and first down/touchdown per dropback rate.\nMcMillan looks to take advantage of a Packers secondary that ranks in the bottom five in points allowed to perimeter receivers, where he lines up more than three-quarters of the time. He received only six targets last week, but Green Bay's 5% touchdown rate to perimeter receivers (22nd) makes McMillan a great anytime touchdown buy-low option in Week 8.\nMike Spector is a featured writer at BettingPros. For more from Mike, check out his  archive   and follow him  @MikeSpector01 .","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-picks-panthers-vs-packers-week-8/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-thursday-night-football-picks-panthers-vs-packers-week-8/","url_hash":"610a9b246835dbc3a874802de6c59d2953e9be02662adb4fc6516d6174324e1a","content_hash":"f8e5d3cbf7947276cafd792cd43566707e12e61b10acda814fbd43002f73cfaf","title":"NFL Thursday Night Football Picks: Panthers vs. Packers (Week 8)","summary":"The Packers lost a nail-biter against NFC North rival Detroit in Week 7, and the Panthers were steamrolled by NFC South rival Tampa Bay. Still, the Packers are modest 3.5-point favorites on Thursday Night Football, and the game total is 47.5 points. It projects to be a competitive contest, something to consider when making NFL [&#8230;] The post NFL Thursday Night Football Picks: Panthers vs. Packers (Week 8) appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-29T09:29:04.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Josh Shepardson","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"The Packers lost a nail-biter against NFC North rival Detroit in Week 7, and the Panthers were steamrolled by NFC South rival Tampa Bay. Still, the Packers are modest 3.5-point favorites on Thursday Night Football, and the game total is 47.5 points . It projects to be a competitive contest, something to consider when making NFL Thursday Night Football picks.\nA blossoming speedy young wideout for the Packers should have a big play up his sleeve in a plus matchup on Thursday Night Football. That said, Green Bay got a key offensive cog back last week, and he could be heavily featured this week. Finally, an ancillary piece for the Panthers has a brutal matchup and might have a quiet effort.\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nBest Week 8 NFL Thursday Night Football Picks\n(Odds courtesy of DraftKings Sportsbook )\nMatthew Golden Longest Reception Over 24.5 Yards ( -109 )\nMatthew Golden is having a sensational sophomore season. According to the Fantasy Points Data Suite 2.0, among eight Packers with at least 50 routes this season, Golden is first in target share (24.7%), targets per route run (0.28 TPRR), first-read rate (28.1%) and air yard share (39.6%). The second-year speedster has a 14.04-yard average depth of target (aDOT).\nGolden's vertical usage has produced, too. The sophomore wideout has five receptions for over 24.5 yards, reeling in at least one in four games. Conversely, the Panthers can be burned for a big reception.\nThey've allowed at least one 25-yard reception to Isaac TeSlaa, Jameson Williams, Rome Odunze, Kalif Raymond, Denzel Boston and Sam LaPorta. Golden should be the next player to log at least a 25-yard reception against the Panthers.\nJosh Jacobs Over 59.5 Rushing Yards ( -114 )\nThrough Week 6, the Packers had a 7.8% pass rate over expected (PROE). In Josh Jacobs' Week 7 return, Green Bay had a 6.4% PROE. It was a small step back, but it was something. Meanwhile, Carolina's defense ranks 29th in PROE against (-2.6%) this season, and they were just curbstomped by Tampa Bay's rushing attack. Tampa Bay's trio of Bucky Irving, Kenneth Gainwell and Sean Tucker rumbled for 246 yards and 5.47 yards per carry.\nIt was the second time a team's backfield exceeded 200 rushing yards against the Panthers this season. Carolina has allowed the most rushing yards per game (126.8) and yards per carry (5.21) to running backs this season. D'Andre Swift (124 rushing yards), Irving (106 rushing yards), Kyle Monangai (100 rushing yards), Gainwell (88 rushing yards), Bijan Robinson (72 rushing yards) and Quinshon Judkins (70 rushing yards) each surpassed 59.5 rushing yards against the Panthers this season.\nJacobs is once again the Packers' lead back. In his first game of the season, he handled 11 of Green Bay's backfield's 17 rush attempts (64.7%). Jacobs managed only 36 rushing yards on 11 carries for 3.27 yards per carry. Nevertheless, his workload was rock-solid, and if he shook off some rust, he could be more efficient and take a larger piece of the pie against Carolina's pitiful run defense. Jacobs topped 59.5 rushing yards in nine of 16 games last season, and he should clear the over on Thursday for the first time this season.\nDarren Waller Under 20.5 Receiving Yards ( -116 )\nDarren Waller was the only bright spot for the Panthers in their Week 7 beatdown. He secured a 50-yard touchdown reception on one of his two targets. It was his only reception.\nIn the five games Jalen Coker was healthy this season, Waller recorded the following numbers:\n43.2% snap share\n48.4% route participation rate\n7.8% target share\n0.15 TPRR\n8.8% first-read rate\n10.7% air yard share\n2.2 receptions per game\n32.4 receiving yards per game\n1.57 yards per route run (YPRR)\nWaller went over 20.5 receiving yards in four of those five games. However, he posted a bagel in a challenging Week 6 matchup against the Eagles.\nThe veteran tight end has another challenging matchup this week. The Packers have allowed the fewest receiving yards per game (32.9) and the seventh-fewest yards per target (5.90) to tight ends this season. T.J. Hockenson (36 receiving yards) and Josh Oliver (22 receiving yards) went over 20.5 receiving yards against the Packers in Week 1, but Cade Otton (37 receiving yards) and Brevyn Spann-Ford (35 receiving yards) are the only tight ends to clear that threshold since.\nFurthermore, Green Bay's coverage tendencies are suboptimal for Waller's receiving outlook. The Packers have played zone 79.3% of the time (73.3% league average) and two-high coverage 66.3% of the time (50.6% league average) this season. In the five games Coker played, Waller had 0.15 TPRR and 1.61 YPRR on 66 routes against zone coverage but only 0.09 TPRR and 1.29 YPRR on 45 routes against two-high coverage. Thus, Waller should fall short of 20.5 receiving yards on Thursday Night Football.\nJosh Shepardson is a featured writer at BettingPros. For more from Josh, check out his archive   and follow him  @BChad50 .","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-week-8-confidence-pool-picks-predictions-2026/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-week-8-confidence-pool-picks-predictions-2026/","url_hash":"31c0c0b57f4aa34a57f065606fb7b2362c9a385bd0d875cd2c4d409bff124bcf","content_hash":"f64e570e7e239dda94365a57293320c22fd44d4dd09ce628e4865984ee77353e","title":"NFL Week 8 Confidence Pool Picks &#038; Predictions (2026)","summary":"After a couple of solid weeks, we struggled in Week 7. We&#8217;re now 33,268th with a 56-48 record overall. It&#8217;s time to lock in. Here are my NFL Week 8 confidence pool picks. More NFL Betting Advice NFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet Expert NFL Game Picks NFL Betting Strategy Best +EV NFL Picks Get instant [&#8230;] The post NFL Week 8 Confidence Pool Picks &amp; Predictions (2026) appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-28T16:15:56.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Jason Radowitz","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"After a couple of solid weeks, we struggled in Week 7. We're now 33,268th with a 56-48 record overall. It's time to lock in. Here are my NFL Week 8 confidence pool picks .\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nNFL Week 8 Confidence Pool Picks\n(1) Cardinals | Cardinals vs. Cowboys\nAt the end of the day, these teams are pretty similar on paper. Dallas has the better passing game, but Arizona can run the ball better. I'll take my chances with the Cardinals to pull off an upset.\n(2) Browns | Browns vs. Steelers\nExpect this divisional game to be tight and close throughout. I'll take the underdog.\n(3) Bills | Ravens vs. Bills\nThe Ravens desperately need Lamar Jackson back. But even then, I'm not sure he'll be enough to get past the Bills.\n(4) Eagles | Eagles vs. Commanders\nI love taking the road underdog in divisional games. Philadelphia was competitive last week against Dallas. So there's that.\n(5) Chiefs | Chiefs vs. Broncos\nIf you think the Chiefs are going to put together back-to-back poor performances, you're out of your mind!\n(6) Seahawks | Bears vs. Seahawks\nThe defending champs looked much better last week. The defense is electric, and the offense just got a new piece from the Colts!\n(7) Lions | Vikings vs. Lions\nA 6-0 team looks worse on paper analytically than a 4-2 squad. Detroit's defense has improved, so I'll go with the Lions.\n(8) Jets   | Raiders vs. Jets\nI'm not sure why I do this to myself, but give me the Jets at home. Geno Smith should have fun throwing against the Las Vegas secondary.\n(9) Buccaneers | Falcons vs. Buccaneers\nBaker Mayfield's energy lifted the Bucs last weekend. It'll be the same this weekend.\n(10) Rams | Chargers vs. Rams\nThe Chargers should be competitive, but I still like the Rams in the Los Angeles battle.\n(11) Patriots | Patriots vs. Dolphins\nOne divisional win is enough for the Dolphins this season.\n(12) Jaguars | Colts vs. Jaguars\nThat historic selloff for the Colts this week tells the whole story. I'm on the Jaguars.\n(13) Packers | Panthers vs. Packers\nComing off a dreadful performance on Sunday and having to play on Thursday isn't ideal. Good luck, Panthers.\n(14) Bengals   | Titans vs. Bengals\nThe Bengals scored 35 unanswered points in the second half last week. That's what they can do against the Titans.","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-week-8-picks-predictions-best-early-parlays-2026/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-week-8-picks-predictions-best-early-parlays-2026/","url_hash":"ef03c6d7dbe7a3eb46b24066da09b42f06b86fc7adbc065fb0f80871763ad651","content_hash":"920b8683e74f40f7e44b206f32e3931bb64bfa8971e40b6e739b9e225eede38f","title":"NFL Week 8 Picks &#038; Predictions: Best Early Parlays (2026)","summary":"Week 8 kicks off soon, and it’s hard to believe how quickly the season is flying by. Getting to the lines early gives you an advantage, and we&#8217;ve found a few that stand out from the rest. Let’s dive into our top NFL Week 8 picks and our favorite parlays More NFL Betting Advice NFL [&#8230;] The post NFL Week 8 Picks &#038; Predictions: Best Early Parlays (2026) appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-28T10:58:28.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Steve Krebs","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Week 8 kicks off soon, and it's hard to believe how quickly the season is flying by. Getting to the lines early gives you an advantage, and we've found a few that stand out from the rest. Let's dive into our top NFL Week 8 picks and our favorite parlays\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nBest Early NFL Week 8 Picks & Parlays\n(Odds Courtesy of DraftKings Sportsbook )\nBoost your NFL betting strategy with our   Same-Game Parlay (SGP) Tool . Get expert correlations, projections and bet ratings.\nEarly NFL Week 8 Parlay #1\nLeg 1: Jordan Love 2+ Passing Touchdowns ( -166 )\nWe open the week with a safe parlay that starts on Thursday with the Carolina Panthers versus the Green Bay Packers. Jordan Love wasn't anywhere near his best on Sunday against the Lions. The Green Bay quarterback connected on 27-of-45 attempts. Yet, he still finished with 274 yards and two touchdowns. Love gets the benefit of home-field advantage this week, where he has thrown for at least two touchdowns in two out of three games.\nLove has recorded two touchdown passes in all but one game this season. The total is currently set at 48 points. That means oddsmakers expect a ton of scoring. Given the high total, we expect Love to throw at least two touchdowns against the Panthers.\nLeg 2: Carolina Panthers-Green Bay Packers Over 39.5 Points ( -350 )\nAs noted earlier, we expect a high-scoring game. We shaved a few points off the standard total of 48, just in case something unforeseen happens. The Panthers and Packers average 46.5 combined points this season. The Packers average 2.1 more points at home, while Carolina scores fewer than 26 points on the road.\nCarolina has covered 40+ combined points in five out of six games. Green Bay has reached 40 total points in two out of three home games this season. If this culminates in the shootout sportsbooks expect, the Packers and Panthers should clear the 40-point threshold in Thursday's matchup.\nLeg 3: Los Angeles Rams Moneyline ( -290 )\nWe close out our first parlay with a very straightforward selection. The Chargers are winless and now face a Rams team that, despite multiple injuries, is a solid favorite going into this contest (-6.5). We considered taking the points while it's still less than a touchdown. Ultimately, taking the Rams to win outright is the more logical play.\nIf you're feeling ambitious and want to increase the profit on this parlay, you can certainly add Rams -6.5. For our purposes, we will take the Moneyline. The Rams took it to the Raiders on Sunday and held a commanding lead for most of the game. Matthew Stafford should lead his team to another win over the Chargers, their fourth of the season. The Chargers are averaging 15 points through six games - the lowest in the NFL.\nParlay Odds: +140\nEarly NFL Week 8 Parlay #2\nLeg 1: Detroit Lions Team Total Under 31 Points ( -340 )\nOur second parlay has one Moneyline bet and two legs focused on totals. As with the first parlay, we're taking a more cautious approach, hoping to bring back a +200 profit. The Vikings are allowing just 10.6 points per game on the road this season. This should be a sweat-free option.\nMinnesota is 6-0 and comes off an unexpected close battle against Indianapolis on Sunday. The Vikings remain one of the NFL's most dominant defensive units. The task is tough this week, as they face one of the league's highest-scoring teams. Minnesota has allowed just over 12 points per game through six games and has not given up more than 22 points in any contest this season.\nLeg 2: New England Patriots Moneyline ( -370 )\nThe Miami Dolphins won their first game of the season on Sunday against the Jets. The Dolphins have had a rough start to the season. However, it was good to see the team finally get a win. Two wins in a row may be a lot to ask of Miami, and New England has won three of its last four games. The Patriots are 2-0 in the previous matchups against the Dolphins, dating back to last season.\nSunday marked Miami's second 20+ point game. Drake Maye and New England have been flourishing offensively. Maye has thrown for 12 touchdowns and two interceptions over the last four games. A divisional matchup always comes with a narrative that the game will be close. That said, we don't think Miami can keep up with New England's offense, which gives us confidence in the Patriots on the Moneyline.\nLeg 3: Tennessee Titans-Cincinnati Bengals Under 47 Points ( -110 )\nThis will more than likely be the sweatiest leg of the entire parlay. And we are OK with that. At first glance, this doesn't look like a high-scoring affair. The stats reinforce that notion, as the total for this contest is largely predicted on only one team, the Cincinnati Bengals. The Bengals rank fourth in the NFL in scoring, averaging 27.2 points per game.\nThe Titans rank 31st in scoring, putting up only 15.4 points per game. Tennessee has scored 20+ points in two out of six games but has failed to cover 47 points in all but one. The Titans are averaging 17 points in three road contests.\nParlay Odds: +213","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-survivor-pool-advice-for-week-8-odds-picks-predictions-2026/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-survivor-pool-advice-for-week-8-odds-picks-predictions-2026/","url_hash":"df905bc6f225d3b629aecc123a5b84022909854029e26ca697c68a0480404ebd","content_hash":"5b4e7a9c13b9ac9cf7c51b64ef7e494b8747c5e55ef4e88a2d264407c29afca4","title":"NFL Survivor Pool Advice for Week 8: Odds, Picks &#038; Predictions (2026)","summary":"For the third straight week, the top Moneyline favorite on the board (Texans) lost outright. But last week&#8217;s NFL survivor pool advice got through two of our safest picks (Rams and Cowboys), and two of our three risky plays (Vikings and Broncos) won outright. This week looks like one of the toughest for survivor pools [&#8230;] The post NFL Survivor Pool Advice for Week 8: Odds, Picks &#038; Predictions (2026) appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-27T13:21:13.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Mike Spector","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"For the third straight week, the top Moneyline favorite on the board (Texans) lost outright. But last week's NFL survivor pool advice got through two of our safest picks (Rams and Cowboys), and two of our three risky plays (Vikings and Broncos) won outright.\nThis week looks like one of the toughest for survivor pools yet, with nine of the 14 games having spreads of 3.5 points or fewer. On a positive note, we're advising you to use several teams that likely weren't under consideration at any point this season.\nRead on for our best NFL survivor pool advice for Week 8.\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nNFL Survivor Pool Advice for Week 8: Picks & Predictions (2026)\n(Odds courtesy of DraftKings Sportsbook )\nHere are the odds for the top 10 favorites to win their Week 8 matchups.\nWeek 8 NFL Moneyline Odds\nTEAM\nODDS\nCincinnati Bengals\n-600\nJacksonville Jaguars\n-400\nNew England Patriots\n-375\nLos Angeles Rams\n-325\nDallas Cowboys\n-285\nGreen Bay Packers\n-210\nPittsburgh Steelers\n-200\nBuffalo Bills\n-190\nWashington Commanders\n-190\nDetroit Lions\n-175\nSafest Picks\nCincinnati Bengals\nIf Cincinnati loses, it would be the third straight team to lose outright as the biggest favorite of the week, and it would be a gargantuan upset over a Titans team that has scored 10 or fewer points in three of its seven games.\nThe Bengals impressively outscored the Ravens 35-0 in the second half last week. They haven't started this well through the first six games (4-2) since the last time they made the Super Bowl in 2021. \nJoe Burrow now has 11 games with four or more touchdown passes since that 2021 season (the most in the league). Tennessee's offense has looked better in back-to-back weeks, with 129 rushing yards and three touchdowns from Tony Pollard last week. But its defense is now the bigger concern after allowing a 53.6% rushing success rate to a Browns offense that entered the week with a bottom-five rate in that metric (34.2%).\nJacksonville Jaguars\nJacksonville snapped its three-game winning streak in its last game before a bye week. I ts defense is also struggling, allowing 400 yards twice in the last three games. But I'm giving the Jaguars a pass for a loss to the Texans, as Houston head coach DeMeco Ryans is 16-5 in division games, the best record by a head coach in the NFL since 2023.\nI don't expect Jacksonville to drop a second straight division game to a Colts team that has lost three straight and is 2-12 in its last 14.\nDallas Cowboys\nMany would classify Dallas as the team to avoid in survivor pools this week, as Arizona is responsible for two of the five upsets this season by teams with +350 Moneyline odds or longer. While both upsets came in a domed environment at SoFi Stadium, we may be overvaluing those wins against Chargers and Rams teams that are a combined 3-10.\nArizona's league-worst scoring defense (29.7 points per game) couldn't limit a struggling Denver offense. The Broncos still managed 30 points even though Bo Nix was just 1-for-7 passing on throws downfield.\nThe Cardinals should have no answer for the elite wide receiver duo of CeeDee Lamb and George Pickens. This is a smart spot to use the Cowboys, even off a short week. Most of their schedule down the stretch is littered with divisional games or games against the 49ers, Seahawks, Rams and Jaguars.\nRisky Popular Plays\nNew England Patriots\nThe Dolphins are coming off their first win under new head coach Jeff Hafley - a 28-25 road win over the Jets. Miami was the more disciplined and physical team from the get-go. It jumped to a 14-0 lead (its first lead at any point this season) on two long drives that combined for 21 plays and chewed up almost 12 minutes of clock.\nI understand that a win against the lowly Jets doesn't indicate that Miami is \"back\" by any means. But I'm avoiding New England simply because weird things tend to happen when it travels to Florida's heat and humidity. The Dolphins have a winning record against the Patriots over the last 19 matchups (11-8), including winning four of the previous five at home.\nNew England is on a 16-game winning streak as favorites. But there are better spots to use the Patriots in survivor pools down the stretch, like its home rematch against Miami or in Week 16 against the Jets.\nGreen Bay Packers\nGreen Bay will be a popular pick against Carolina, who just allowed 40 points to a Tampa Bay team that had just 64 passing yards. While the Buccaneers had the second-best rushing output of any team this season in that win, Green Bay's rushing attack isn't built to exploit the Panthers' weakness.\nThe Packers are undisciplined and have committed the most penalties in the league (65). They also have the most dropped passes by a wide margin (18).\nIf you haven't used Green Bay in survivor pools yet, I'd much rather save them for a Week 15 home matchup against the Dolphins.\nPittsburgh Steelers\nPittsburgh has won three straight games after starting 2-2. Plenty of survivor pool contestants will want to use the Steelers against the Browns, not believing in Cleveland's best seven-game start since 2020. \nYes, the Browns have played with fire, with Deshaun Watson leading a game-winning drive in the fourth quarter or overtime in all five wins. But Pittsburgh could be weary the week after playing in Paris, and I'm not doubting Cleveland's hot start.\nContrarian Play to Beat a Large Pool\nWashington Commanders\nSurvivor pool strategy picks are meant to be contrarian, not only to avoid the popular plays others use each week, but to save the more elite teams for later in the season when the pickings are much slimmer. Thus, backing a Washington team playing its first full game without Terry McLaurin (torn patellar tendon) and led by Jayden Daniels (0-7-1 in his last eight starts) is certainly an outside-the-box play.\nWashington has the ultimate scheduling advantage coming off a bye week and facing an Eagles team that played on Monday night. The Commanders lost to Philadelphia by two points in Week 1 (they were a two-point conversion away from sending the game into overtime). But that game featured a healthy Jalen Hurts, and Washington still overcame allowing 5.4 yards per carry in that road contest.\nMike Spector is a featured writer at BettingPros. For more from Mike, check out his  archive   and follow him  @MikeSpector01 .","revision_hash":null},{"source":"BettingPros","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-week-8-picks-predictions-best-early-bets-2026/","canonical_url":"https://www.bettingpros.com/articles/nfl-week-8-picks-predictions-best-early-bets-2026/","url_hash":"8f6ae447438b8e7a67d47585455293072e315856c79c828c5033fa6137202755","content_hash":"d43b7fdc238d5516e7d5538cca9c018528a3fea2d91733c59f8d9357dd50a328","title":"NFL Week 8 Picks &#038; Predictions: Best Early Bets (2026)","summary":"I&#8217;m eyeing a couple of bets for this week&#8217;s NFL games. One team is 6-0, and another is 0-6 heading into Week 8. We&#8217;re betting on both of those games this weekend. Here are our top early Week 8 NFL picks. More NFL Betting Advice NFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet Expert NFL Game Picks NFL [&#8230;] The post NFL Week 8 Picks &#038; Predictions: Best Early Bets (2026) appeared first on BettingPros .","published_at":"2026-10-27T13:21:11.000Z","confidence":0.72,"author":"Jason Radowitz","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"I'm eyeing a couple of bets for this week's NFL games. One team is 6-0, and another is 0-6 heading into Week 8. We're betting on both of those games this weekend. Here are our top early Week 8 NFL picks .\nMore NFL Betting Advice\nNFL Prop Bet Cheat Sheet\nExpert NFL Game Picks\nNFL Betting Strategy\nBest +EV NFL Picks\nGet instant alerts when a line reaches your target via the BettingPros App\nEarly NFL Week 8 Picks \n(Odds courtesy of  DraftKings Sportsbook )\nMinnesota Vikings vs. Detroit Lions\nThe Minnesota Vikings are the 6-0 squad in Week 8. However, PFF grades the Vikings 77.8, which isn't elite or deserving of a 6-0 record. The Vikings have scored 20.8 points per game, including under three points in the third quarter.\nIt might be hard for the Vikings to keep up with the Detroit Lions, who are home and have scored 30.7 points per game this year.\nThe Vikings have struggled in the tackling department, holding a 55.9 grade via PFF. Meanwhile, the Lions have performed poorly defensively most of the year but have an 88.1 tackling grade.\nThat said, the defense has only allowed 99.2 yards per game on the ground this season. The Vikings have Jordan Mason back from injury, but now Aaron Jones is dealing with an injury that could keep him out. Minnesota hasn't had that two-headed monster in the running game this season.\nDon't be shocked if the Vikings take the lead early and into the half. But I've got the Lions storming back in the second half to pull off a win against an undefeated Minnesota squad. Give me the Lions at -3 (-112).\nPick: Lions -3 ( -112 )\nLos Angeles Chargers vs. Los Angeles Rams\nThere hasn't been great football in Los Angeles this season. That said, someone's got to win this weekend (unless there's a tie).\nThese two teams are 3-10 combined this season. Before the season began, both teams were playoff contenders.\nAnyway, the Chargers have scored just 15 points per game this season and have averaged only 168.2 yards in the air behind Justin Herbert. The entire team has struggled on offense, but Herbert is still at fault. For example, PFF has the Chargers' pass grade at 41.9 this season. Pass protection hasn't held up, and the receivers haven't been great, especially with Ladd McConkey dealing with an injury at the start of the season.\nOn the other hand, the Rams are good offensively. They've just lacked consistency. Puka Nacua looks healthy, and Kyren Williams, along with Blake Corum, have found a groove in the running game. Still, look for the Rams to exploit the Chargers' secondary, which is easily the weakest part of their defense.\nThe tight ends will continue to perform, along with Nacua, even with Davante Adams out with injury.\nLet's back the Rams at -6.5 at home.\nPick: Rams -6.5 ( -112 )","revision_hash":null},{"source":"ESPN NFL","source_type":"news","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50313890/nfl-week-8-odds-betting-tips-panthers-packers-preview","canonical_url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50313890/nfl-week-8-odds-betting-tips-panthers-packers-preview","url_hash":"9f846b3b3c06d7aa9627867e5ebcfd46c1a160441ed3b1bb058fc52fea034822","content_hash":"a63583f10cc2204a9618dda6eae5b14553f6b3730d73869f74b4513764f07f4f","title":"How to bet Panthers-Packers: Analysis, tips and top prop plays","summary":"Odds, bets and analysis to help you bet the Carolina Panthers-Green Bay Packers game on Thursday night.","published_at":"2026-10-29T14:50:17.000Z","confidence":0.67,"author":"Eric Moody","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"ESPN NFL","source_type":"news","url":"https://www.espn.com/video/clip/_/id/50318514/