ter would not reveal Lamar Jackson’s participation level at Wednesday’s practice. The injury report, though, shows the quarterback was a full participant.\nIt is Jackson’s first full practice since Oct. 2, when he was a full participant with a back injury.\nHe has not played since Oct. 4, missing the past three games with a high ankle sprain.\nJackson was trending toward playing last week, with limited practices in all three on-field days. The Ravens initially listed him as questionable to play, but he was inactive for Sunday’s 35-13 loss to the Bengals.\nThe Ravens went 1-2 without Jackson, who is 3-1 with six passing touchdowns, one interception and one rushing touchdown.\nDefensive lineman Calais Campbell (rest), safety Kyle Hamilton (knee), safety Jaylinn Hawkins (knee), offensive guard Vega Ioane (knee), and linebacker Roquan Smith (knee) did not practice Wednesday.\nNose takcle John Jenkins (knee), offensive guard John Simpson (groin), offensive tackle Ronnie Stanley (rest/toe/ankle), cornerbcak T.J. Tampa Jr. (knee) and defensive tackle Broderick Washington (ankle) were limited.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/mike-mcdaniel-will-remain-the-chargers-offensive-playcaller","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/mike-mcdaniel-will-remain-the-chargers-offensive-playcaller","url_hash":"3451d657d8c79b6bb3a231b03d1d926c19e460c9ede28d297d4037e320e5f042","content_hash":"043da1718ccee20ec6032475b442e4c5c4b41e85687888999d8d083a994356c9","title":"Mike McDaniel will remain the Chargers' offensive playcaller","summary":"Chargers head coach Jim Harbaugh said that the team would spend their bye week \"looking into everything\" when it came to improving their offense and did not rule out a change involving offensive coordinator Mike 