ew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nJakobi Meyers limited in Jaguars practice, Antonio Johnson out\nBy\nJosh Alper ,\nBy\nJosh Alper\nPublished October 28, 2026 04:25 PM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nThe Jaguars are coming off a bye week and their return to practice featured a few limited participants.\nThe group included wide receiver Jakobi Meyers, who is dealing with a hamstring injury but has not missed any game action this season. Meyers has 20 catches for 285 yards and two touchdowns.\nSafety Antonio Johnson has not missed any games either, but he appears to be likelier to miss this week than Meyers. Johnson did not practice on Wednesday due to an ankle injury.\nLong snapper Ross Matiscik (shoulder), defensive lineman Ruhe Orhorhoro (ankle), and linebacker Jahlani Tavai (hamstring) joined Meyers as limited participants. Cornerback Montaric Brown (hamstring) was a full participant after missing the team’s two London games and tight end Brenton Strange (eye) also landed in that category.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/brian-thomas-on-rough-stretch-just-want-to-flush-it","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/brian-thomas-on-rough-stretch-just-want-to-flush-it","url_hash":"7c362e58873441f9a1b2b154fd410239f42a44a65090e1e3482e35a6cd057436","content_hash":"8509b20efac98778e5cab22012f727b98743f11981abf7fe58ee12ad22daaf04","title":"Brian Thomas on rough stretch: Just want to flush it","summary":"Jaguars wide receiver Brian Thomas is coming off two straight games without a catch and he didn't play at all in the second half of the team's Week 6 loss to the Texans.","published_at":"2026-10-29T12:23:23.000Z","c