eattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nBrian Thomas on rough stretch: Just want to flush it\nBy\nJosh Alper ,\nBy\nJosh Alper\nPublished October 29, 2026 08:23 AM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nJaguars wide receiver Brian Thomas is coming off two straight games without a catch and he didn’t play at all in the second half of the team’s Week 6 loss to the Texans.\nThomas had a drop in the first half of that game and his ongoing role on a team with several other receiving options has been the subject of conversation with the trade deadline less than two weeks away. Head coach Liam Coen said this week that he expects Thomas to make plays for the team in this week’s game against the Colts and Thomas said on Wednesday that his approach coming out of the bye week has been to let go of what happened in the past.\n“I really just wanted to flush it , come back ready with a different mindset and come back ready to go,” Thomas said, via the team’s website. “That was the biggest thing for me. . . . I feel I still know what I can do. I just have to go out and do it and go out there and show everybody what I can do.”\nThomas had 87 catches for 1,282 yards as a rookie, but had 57 catches for 812 yards since Coen became the coach ahead of the 2025 season. That hasn’t stopped the Jags from winning games — the Jags are 17-5 in the regular season with Coen — and those differing fortunes are a big reason why Thomas’s name frequently comes up in trade rumors. Such talk has been rebuffed thus far, but Thomas will likely have to show more in the next couple of weeks to put them to bed for good.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/shane-steichen-jonathan-taylors-on-our-football-team-hasnt-asked-for-a-trade","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/shane-steichen-jonathan-taylors-on-our-football-team-hasnt-asked-for-a-trade","url_hash":"b0320e87f738fd6d60fdbe61138ed2de2c51c09b093fad223632eac7054d09c7","content_hash":"f5b65ca19aa4f047e3c6463467ad0e08d29afe3c6fae75ea4d4517746c301063","title":"Shane Steichen: Jonathan Taylor's on our football team, hasn't asked for a trade","summary":"Colts running back Jonathan Taylor's future in Indianapolis is the subject of much scrutiny right now, but head coach Shane Steichen said on Wednesday that Taylor isn't looking for an immediate exit.","published_at":"2026-10-28T18:14:55.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Josh Alper","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Shane Steichen: Jonathan Taylor's on our football team, hasn't asked for a trade - NBC Sports\nSkip navigation\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nProfile\nLogin or Create Profile\nFavorites\nMenu\nFavorites\nSign up to follow your favorites on all your devices.\nSign up\nTeams\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nShane Steichen: Jonathan Taylor’s on our football team, hasn’t asked for a trade\nBy\nJosh Alper ,\nBy\nJosh Alper\nPublished October 28, 2026 02:14 PM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nColts running back Jonathan Taylor’s future in Indianapolis is the subject of much scrutiny right now, but head coach Shane Steichen said on Wednesday that Taylor isn’t looking for an immediate exit.\nSteichen told reporters at a Wednesday press conference that Taylor has not asked for a trade in the wake of the team’s decision to trade defensive tackle DeForest Buckner and guard Quenton Nelson. Wide receiver Josh Downs reportedly requested a trade on Wednesday and Taylor would likely net the team a rich return to use as part of a rebuilding effort that kicked off with last week’s firing of General Manager Chris Ballard.\nSteichen acknowledged all of that chatter, but said that he is moving forward with Taylor until told otherwise.\n“Those are hypothetical things right now,” Steichen said, via Stephen Holder of ESPN.com. “I know there’s stuff floating around out there, but JT’s on our football team.”\nSteichen said that it is going to be tough to keep moving forward through the upheaval, but that’s “what we signed up for” and the next two weeks will determine just how sweeping the in-season changes are in Indianapolis.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/cam-heyward-jared-verse-calling-steelers-dirty-will-be-addressed-sunday","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/cam-heyward-jared-verse-calling-steelers-dirty-will-be-addressed-sunday","url_hash":"781defce188eac09e047ff5d42d342b3fa537e97001e0be75de0be1c4b096838","content_hash":"5d45a3282b1de909354b75e30104b387c1243227d69d8679cf7465cf7b616d24","title":"Cam Heyward: Jared Verse calling Steelers \"dirty\" will be addressed Sunday","summary":"Dislike between the Browns and Steelers has been brewing for decades, so there isn't much need for any one player to fan the flames of the bad feelings between the two AFC North teams.","published_at":"2026-10-29T11:07:55.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Josh Alper","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Cam Heyward: Jared Verse calling Steelers \"dirty\" will be addressed Sunday - NBC Sports\nSkip navigation\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nProfile\nLogin or Create Profile\nFavorites\nMenu\nFavorites\nSign up to follow your favorites on all your devices.\nSign up\nTeams\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nCam Heyward: Jared Verse calling Steelers “dirty” will be addressed Sunday\nBy\nJosh Alper ,\nBy\nJosh Alper\nPublished October 29, 2026 07:07 AM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nDislike between the Browns and Steelers has been brewing for decades, so there isn’t much need for any one player to fan the flames of the bad feelings between the two AFC North teams.\nBrowns defensive end Jared Verse did that after the two teams played in Week 4, however. Verse explained that he doesn’t “have any respect for anybody that plays too dirty and does too much extra s—t after the game” and mentioned double-teaming and sliding while calling his opponents “garbage.”\nThe two teams meet again in Pittsburgh this Sunday and Steelers defensive end Cam Heyward made it clear that Verse’s comments haven’t been forgotten during an appearance on The Rich Eisen Show this week.\n“Double teaming, sliding, chipping, are those not allowed in our game? Yeah, I got the bruises to prove it . But we don’t whine about it, baby. It’s part of the game,” Heyward said Tuesday. “So, I’m looking forward to this game. It’s gonna be a fun game. Both teams are in position to do a lot of work in this division, as they say. The AFC North is on fire, and I’m glad I’m in the kitchen because I like it that way. But those were words that were said, and they will be addressed.”\nThe distaste between the two teams is nothing new, but having both of them playing well at the same time is fairly uncommon. With both teams at 5-2 coming into this week, there will be more than bragging rights at stake for the winner.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/justin-herbert-blame-for-chargers-offense-is-on-the-players-not-mike-mcdaniels-fault","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/justin-herbert-blame-for-chargers-offense-is-on-the-players-not-mike-mcdaniels-fault","url_hash":"1a11a9927de2680c15b7bd2f210598134c9e9c61c176a5968ba41bf8f56fd012","content_hash":"6851fd39cde349e1d3e57615d26bf1bb738420bd039c922a08dda2c7c015be3d","title":"Justin Herbert: Blame for Chargers' offense is on the players, not Mike McDaniel's fault","summary":"The Chargers' starting quarterback says the new offensive coordinator does not deserve the blame.","published_at":"2026-10-29T08:59:41.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Michael David Smith","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Justin Herbert: Blame for Chargers' offense is on the players, not Mike McDaniel's fault - NBC Sports\nSkip navigation\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nProfile\nLogin or Create Profile\nFavorites\nMenu\nFavorites\nSign up to follow your favorites on all your devices.\nSign up\nTeams\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nJustin Herbert: Blame for Chargers’ offense is on the players, not Mike McDaniel’s fault\nBy\nMichael David Smith ,\nBy\nMichael David Smith\nPublished October 29, 2026 04:59 AM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nBefore the season, Chargers coach Jim Harbaugh predicted that Justin Herbert would be the greatest quarterback ever . During the season, Herbert has been by some measures the worst quarterback in the NFL. That has led to plenty of talk that new offensive coordinator Mike McDaniel is to blame.\nBut Herbert says that isn’t the case.\n“It’s not his fault, it’s our fault as an offense,” Herbert said when asked about McDaniel. “We have to do our job. It’s not Mike’s fault. The guys are open, plays are being made. It’s on us to run, to block, to catch, to throw. It’s on us as an offense.”\nHerbert said that he’s learning a lot from McDaniel, even if the results aren’t showing up on the field.\n“Mike has been very helpful. He’s such a great coach and such a great leader, to have the experience and expertise has, it’s been very helpful,” Herbert said.\nAccording to Herbert, the Chargers’ winless season is 100 percent on the players and not at all on McDaniel.\n“Mike has done an incredible job of getting people open and it’s on us to execute and make plays,” Herbert said. “As an offense we have to come together, execute our stuff, and understand that it’s on us to fix it.”\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/new-study-estimates-75-percent-of-former-nfl-players-who-died-from-2008-to-2023-had-cte","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/new-study-estimates-75-percent-of-former-nfl-players-who-died-from-2008-to-2023-had-cte","url_hash":"50cc9311b80c001b2b88c0831e7753dd1ec76d8d90f66f993adc14d9c4540492","content_hash":"1ca1999b94ab4cee739ece06717f1e78d9a3aace36eb443f79690496c2f40a7f","title":"New study estimates 75 percent of former NFL players who died from 2008 to 2023 had CTE","summary":"A new study from JAMA Network Open by researchers at Boston University, Mass General Brigham, and the Concussion &amp; CTE Foundation has found that an estimated 75 percent of former NFL players who died between 2008 and 2023 had CTE.","published_at":"2026-10-29T02:22:00.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Mike Florio","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"New study estimates 75 percent of former NFL players who died from 2008 to 2023 had CTE - NBC Sports\nSkip navigation\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nProfile\nLogin or Create Profile\nFavorites\nMenu\nFavorites\nSign up to follow your favorites on all your devices.\nSign up\nTeams\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nNew study estimates 75 percent of former NFL players who died from 2008 to 2023 had CTE\nBy\nMike Florio ,\nBy\nMike Florio\nPublished October 28, 2026 10:22 PM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nA new study from JAMA Network Open by researchers at Boston University, Mass General Brigham, and the Concussion & CTE Foundation has found that an estimated 75 percent of former NFL players who died between 2008 and 2023 had CTE.\n“Many cases may have been early stage at the time of death and possibly symptom free,” the paper said, via Shwetha Surendran of ESPN.\nThat observation speaks to one of the basic realities of CTE. It’s unknown how many people have it. And it’s no surprise that the vast majority of former NFL players who die with CTE symptoms are later determined to have had CTE.\nThere’s a balance to strike. On one hand, it’s obvious that long-term, repetitive head trauma isn’t good for the brain. On the other hand, it can be problematic to have hundreds, if not thousands, of former NFL players believing they already have — and constantly fearing the inevitable development of symptoms.\nEven now, years after CTE became a commonly-known term, there’s much work to be done in order to understand who gets it, how it develops, and what it means to have it. Hopefully, the research will continue with the goal of better clarifying the risks that current players are assuming without making those whose careers have ended unduly anxious about the possibility that a ticking time bomb has been embedded in their brains.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/sean-mcvay-davante-adams-closer-to-the-shorter-term-of-the-6-10-week-timeline","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/sean-mcvay-davante-adams-closer-to-the-shorter-term-of-the-6-10-week-timeline","url_hash":"3f5a25b2d1bb824a92f63c4eae80a35523ec64b2a685648b09f598086a85b179","content_hash":"2b1932cb04d577170d69b894a2bcabcfd1e3b0d3eeed76265afffc5b0b1dd761","title":"Sean McVay: Davante Adams \"closer to the shorter term\" of the 6-10 week timeline","summary":"Rams wide receiver Davante Adams injured his hamstring in an Oct. 18 game against the Cardinals.","published_at":"2026-10-29T01:45:39.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Charean Williams","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z",