olphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nSean McVay: Davante Adams “closer to the shorter term” of the 6-10 week timeline\nBy\nCharean Williams ,\nBy\nCharean Williams\nPublished October 28, 2026 09:45 PM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nRams wide receiver Davante Adams injured his hamstring in an Oct. 18 game against the Cardinals.\nHe recently underwent a procedure on the ruptured hamstring.\n“Everything’s good. It went really well,” Rams coach Sean McVay said Wednesday. “He’s feeling good in the process of recovering and doing really well.”\nThe prognosis for Adams was 6-10 weeks, but McVay said that Adams will return probably “closer to the shorter term” of the timeline. That could mean Adams returns sometime after the team’s Week 11 off week.\n“He tells me, which I believe, [that] he’s Wolverine,” McVay said. “He’ll heal quick and be ready to go. He’s in good spirits. [He] sent me a picture the other day [of him] being able to walk already. He’s doing really well, and I think based on how everything went, on the shorter end is what is projected.”\nAdams, who is on injured reserve, has 30 receptions for 480 yards and four touchdowns in six games.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/for-pfts-25th-anniversary-completely-re-written-quarterback-of-the-future-is-coming","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/for-pfts-25th-anniversary-completely-re-written-quarterback-of-the-future-is-coming","url_hash":"5d31bbcecc88a9ab42770292c793690654f6f69a1fd91f19810c05f4a5f8ab93","content_hash":"76631f865ae730ba2e0dfda690c8099ef132438503d5e054a95e1aa51f7046ea","title":"For PFT's 25th anniversary, completely re-written Quarterback of the Future is coming","summary":"The 25th anniversary of the launch of PFT happens on Sunday, November 1.","published_at":"2026-10-29T00:14:08.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Mike Florio","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"For PFT's 25th anniversary, completely re-written Quarterback of the Future is coming - NBC Sports\nSkip navigation\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nProfile\nLogin or Create Profile\nFavorites\nMenu\nFavorites\nSign up to follow your favorites on all your devices.\nSign up\nTeams\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nFor PFT’s 25th anniversary, completely re-written Quarterback of the Future is coming\nBy\nMike Florio ,\nBy\nMike Florio\nPublished October 28, 2026 08:14 PM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nThe 25th anniversary of the launch of PFT happens on Sunday, November 1. And for those of you who have been here since the early days of the site’s existence, I’ve made you something.\nI’ve completely re-written Quarterback of the Future , the long-forgotten football/sci-fi novel that helped lead me into this business in the first place.\nI won’t bore you with the details of how it all happened here. (I’ll bore you with the details of how it all happened here , in the official introduction to the book I’ll post one chapter at a time free of charge.)\nAlso, here’s the landing page for the various chapters. The plan is to post one per day. (They’re relatively short.) Depending on the response, my mood at any given moment, and whether time permits, I may accelerate the process.\nRegardless, it’s a brand-new version of a solid story that was, frankly, not very well written. After years of writing thousands of words per day (and writing eight or nine novels — I’ve lost track — along with Playmakers), the second try is better.\nAs I’m reminded whenever I flip through a copy of the original QBF , it can’t be much worse.\nTake it for whatever it is. It should be fun. It should be enjoyable. Each chapter should make you interested in reading the next one.\nGive it a try. Chapter One arrives Sunday, the official 25th anniversary of the moment we first went live.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/troy-aikman-says-theres-a-50-50-chance-he-wont-be-working-in-tv-next-year","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/troy-aikman-says-theres-a-50-50-chance-he-wont-be-working-in-tv-next-year","url_hash":"eca7c315e044f7a62bfac22bc02008ef492abbb78cbbd355b4d861a944b1ee1a","content_hash":"522ec0951c85e599b8ea7da5e8debdc7cb1d7ac09008e536e9c8eee8f83ad675","title":"Troy Aikman says there's a \"50-50 chance\" he won't be working in TV next year","summary":"Hall of Fame quarterback Troy Aikman appeared at a Dallas event on Wednesday night with Peter King, in connection with Peter's new book, The Game.","published_at":"2026-10-29T00:46:47.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Mike Florio","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Troy Aikman says there's a \"50-50 chance\" he won't be working in TV next year - NBC Sports\nSkip navigation\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nProfile\nLogin or Create Profile\nFavorites\nMenu\nFavorites\nSign up to follow your favorites on all your devices.\nSign up\nTeams\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nTroy Aikman says there’s a “50-50 chance” he won’t be working in TV next year\nBy\nMike Florio ,\nBy\nMike Florio\nPublished October 28, 2026 08:46 PM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nHall of Fame quarterback Troy Aikman appeared at a Dallas event on Wednesday night with Peter King, in connection with Peter’s new book, The Game . During the session, Aikman addressed whether he’d be calling NFL games in 2027. Along the way, Aikman addressed the Babar in the bookstore.\nVia veteran sports journalist Tim Cowlishaw, Aikman said there’s a “ 50-50 chance ” that Aikman won’t be working in TV next year.\nGiven the circumstances, that seems accurate. Aikman’s contract expires after the Super Bowl, and he has not been bashful when it comes to expressing concern (and exasperation) with ESPN’s lack of interest in negotiating an extension.\nIf he leaves ESPN, where else will he go? With CBS already deciding to make J.J. Watt the replacement for Tony Romo, a prime seat will be available for Aikman only if Prime Video opts to exercise its ability to buy out Kirk Herbstreit and pivot to Aikman.\nIt’s no surprise, then, that Aikman has been talking about possibly working for the Cowboys. He has spoken about wanting to work in a front office, and his consulting gig with the Dolphins may have been the first step toward a Matt Millen/John Lynch-style pivot.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Pro Football Talk","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/caleb-williams-hasnt-been-fined-for-week-7-despite-wearing-unauthorized-shoes","canonical_url":"https://www.nbcsports.com/nfl/profootballtalk/rumor-mill/news/caleb-williams-hasnt-been-fined-for-week-7-despite-wearing-unauthorized-shoes","url_hash":"045d96a205121cd81501a972ef774c839ce81065af11d4a9d619231be010bae9","content_hash":"f121dcad28d2f7d4148f52a2b712d8505689ebc63772fddda845885ac0310190","title":"Caleb Williams hasn't been fined for Week 7, despite wearing unauthorized shoes","summary":"Bears QB vows to keep wearing Caddix cleats.","published_at":"2026-10-28T23:40:30.000Z","confidence":0.66,"author":"Mike Florio","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Caleb Williams hasn't been fined for Week 7, despite wearing unauthorized shoes - NBC Sports\nSkip navigation\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nPro Football Talk\nRumor Mill\nPFT Video\nPFT PM\nPFT Live\nPFT Clips\nPFT Draft: Best matchups of Week 8\nWhy questions swirl around Lamar’s health\nCoen trying to keep Jaguars focused vs. Colts\nOther PFT Content\nChristian Watson, Matthew Golden are delivering for the Packers\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nKirk Cousins is having a rare debut run with the Raiders\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nDeion Sanders dismisses “a few guys” from the team after blowout loss in Northwestern\nMike Florio ,\nMike Florio ,\nProfile\nLogin or Create Profile\nFavorites\nMenu\nFavorites\nSign up to follow your favorites on all your devices.\nSign up\nTeams\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nAFC East\nBuffalo Bills\nMiami Dolphins\nNew England Patriots\nNew York Jets\nAFC North\nBaltimore Ravens\nCincinnati Bengals\nCleveland Browns\nPittsburgh Steelers\nAFC South\nHouston Texans\nIndianapolis Colts\nJacksonville Jaguars\nTennessee Titans\nAFC West\nDenver Broncos\nKansas City Chiefs\nLas Vegas Raiders\nLos Angeles Chargers\nNFC East\nDallas Cowboys\nNew York Giants\nPhiladelphia Eagles\nWashington Commanders\nNFC North\nChicago Bears\nDetroit Lions\nGreen Bay Packers\nMinnesota Vikings\nNFC South\nAtlanta Falcons\nCarolina Panthers\nNew Orleans Saints\nTampa Bay Buccaneers\nNFC West\nArizona Cardinals\nLos Angeles Rams\nSan Francisco 49ers\nSeattle Seahawks\nRumor Mill\nPeacock\nPFT Shop\nCaleb Williams hasn’t been fined for Week 7, despite wearing unauthorized shoes\nBy\nMike Florio ,\nBy\nMike Florio\nPublished October 28, 2026 07:40 PM\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\nThe NFL fined Bears quarterback Caleb Williams $11,941 for wearing an “ unauthorized logo ” on his shoes in Week 6, at Atlanta. In Week 7, he wore the same brand of shoe — Caddix, which doesn’t have a licensing deal with the NFL.\nPer a source with knowledge of the situation, Williams has not yet been fined. (For Week 6, the fine was issued on the following Tuesday.)\nWilliams explained on Wednesday his reasons for wearing shoes made by a company that doesn’t have a money-for-nothing deal with the NFL.\n“As we’ve known for the past couple of years now, I’m huge into my body ,” Williams said, via Courtney Cronin of ESPN. “I’m huge into trying to stay on the field. I’m huge into trying to be healthy. It’s a rough game and things like that. So the cleats, they’ve been great. They’ve been super comfy and they’ve worked. They are a science-type of cleat. It’s something that focuses on when you plant on the hard plants on turf or grass, they call them SmartStuds, and they move when you move in these hard plants. They take tension off of your tendons, your joints and all of that. So over the course of a long career or over the course of a long year, when you can take some percentage -- it could be one, it could be 50, it could be 12, it could be whatever, you know. When you take that percentage off consistently over a period of time, you know, you get to have the chance, a higher chance of being healthy. And so that’s what I focus on.\n“I try to be healthy. They’re smart cleats. They’re science cleats, and they’ve been working for me. A bunch of other guys wear them in the league, and they’re forward-focused on making sure players stay on the field, and that’s what I’m always focused on.”\nThe NFL didn’t fine Williams for wearing the Caddix cleats in the preseason or in Week 1 or Week 2 of the regular season. (He didn’t play in Week 3, Week 4, or Week 5 due to a hamstring injury.)\nAlthough Caddix plans to pay Williams’s fine, league rules generally prohibit the payment of fines by anyone other than the person fined. Caddix could easily tiptoe around that technicality with an endorsement deal with Williams. (Then again, he’s already giving the team a strong endorsement for free.)\nThe situation has put the league in an awkward spot. On one hand, it needs to protect the shoe companies that pay the league good money for the right to outfit its players. On the other hand, if the Caddix shoes are safer, the league risks creating the perception (yet again) that supposed concerns about health and safety take a backseat to the ongoing pursuit of the almighty dollar.\nClose Ad\nAdd favorite players, teams, and leagues with an NBCUniversal Profile\nContinue","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Rotowire NFL","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/jeffery-simmons-13465","canonical_url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/jeffery-simmons-13465","url_hash":"c6d2d16e126ffea1b19d3772858a8a22672d6f2defd887d2e5bc07b04efa3d82","content_hash":"14936970241fa6d9938bec98c53f6378603fb263a6e265f5ab902b5c316589d6","title":"Jeffery Simmons: Traded to Chicago","summary":"Simmons was traded to the Bears on Thursday, along with a 2028 fifth-round pick, in exchange for first-round picks in 2027 and 2028, as well as a 2027 fourth-round pick, Adam Schefter of ESPN reports. Visit RotoWire.com for more analysis on this update.","published_at":"2026-10-29T14:39:00.000Z","confidence":0.65,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Rotowire NFL","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/jamarr-chase-15183","canonical_url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/jamarr-chase-15183","url_hash":"e9a08789c9e4e8ab9346ed45266e65251c113d3db8f28ecc3cf6bdead3d23b32","content_hash":"2823e627f0a2dc3b72d83eab71c24f721a1822a48312eb4a4a1373cdd35e4db0","title":"Ja'Marr Chase: Expected to play against Titans","summary":"Chase (ankle) isn't believed to be dealing with a serious injury, and he's expected to suit up Sunday against the Titans, Ian Rapoport of NFL Network reports. Visit RotoWire.com for more analysis on this update.","published_at":"2026-10-29T14:15:00.000Z","confidence":0.65,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Rotowire NFL","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/matthew-golden-18500","canonical_url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/matthew-golden-18500","url_hash":"a748120408e66a8066e2935c6a3b433f01a03736b61af0868eb56f3563dfa00e","content_hash":"8392b7142596f1211a3dc7585086de1f6cde33d49accad19bf70c44c9c04420c","title":"Matthew Golden: Optimism for Thursday availability","summary":"The Packers expect Golden (shoulder/foot), who is listed as questionable for Thursday night's game against the Panthers, to suit up, James Palmer of NFL on Prime Video reports. Visit RotoWire.com for more analysis on this update.","published_at":"2026-10-29T14:10:00.000Z","confidence":0.65,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Rotowire NFL","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/lamar-jackson-12561","canonical_url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/lamar-jackson-12561","url_hash":"690fff07317da113b7066bafc12fa3a042765a70293e255d44c3a8313ffd1f49","content_hash":"ca26e9d33df40eaf849eca4335b81ca026436fb191ae5607231a4cf7316b4017","title":"Lamar Jackson: On track to play Sunday","summary":"Jackson (ankle) handled all of the first-team work during Wednesday's practice and is on track to play Sunday against the Bills, Matt Zenitz of CBS Sports reports. Visit RotoWire.com for more analysis on this update.","published_at":"2026-10-29T14:02:00.000Z","confidence":0.65,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Rotowire NFL","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/tyler-allgeier-15976","canonical_url":"https://www.rotowire.com//football/player/tyler-allgeier-15976","url_hash":"39b2a5eb1c428617c34cfcec8b61a1e117f899a7ac2085e4fec2695fd92bb4ab","content_hash":"799570d15144d2eb3102d5faa97ee043a312504d4e426beed1f5bbeff3259f97","title":"Tyler Allgeier: DNP on Wednesday","summary":"Allgeier (toe) didn't practice Wednesday, Darren Urban of the Cardinals' official site reports. Visit RotoWire.com for more analysis on this update.","published_at":"2026-10-29T00:16:00.000Z","confidence":0.65,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Sharp Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.sharpfootballanalysis.com/fantasy/bears-seahawks-week-8-fantasy-football-preview-nfl-worksheet-rich-hribar-2026/","canonical_url":"https://www.sharpfootballanalysis.com/fantasy/bears-seahawks-week-8-fantasy-football-preview-nfl-worksheet-rich-hribar-2026/","url_hash":"76f097d0e7cbdbef21e041015232ad2f6da919d603b6bd14e05a9b9b4db89022","content_hash":"4d42a781fd8269d5a136d3d8429564416d6c6c6e747a51b3314d8475745407c3","title":"Bears vs. Seahawks Fantasy Football Worksheet, Week 8","summary":"The Worksheet, a comprehensive fantasy football preview by Rich Hribar, breaks down everything you need to know about the Bears vs. Seahawks Week 8 matchup on Monday Night Football. Find a breakdown of every Week 8 NFL game in our Worksheet Hub. The Seahawks average 109.4 more yards per game than their [...]","published_at":"2026-10-29T14:29:53.000Z","confidence":0.69,"author":"Rich Hribar","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Bears vs. Seahawks Fantasy Football Worksheet, Week 8\nBy Rich Hribar | 2026-10-29T10:45:48-04:00 Oct 29, 2026 |\nView Larger Image\nThe Worksheet, a comprehensive fantasy football preview by Rich Hribar, breaks down everything you need to know about the Bears vs. Seahawks Week 8 matchup on Monday Night Football.\nFind a breakdown of every Week 8 NFL game in our Worksheet Hub.\n[[[\"Chicago\",\"Rank\",\"@\",\"Seattle\",\"Rank\"],[\"3.5\",\" \",\"Spread\",\"-3.5\",\" \"],[\"21.5\",\" \",\"Implied Total\",\"25.0\",\" \"],[\"25.7\",\"8\",\"