\nJakorian Bennett CB Knee FP No designation\nJalyx Hunt OLB Knee/Ankle LP No designation\nJihaad Campbell LB Hamstring/Quad DNP No designation\nJonathan Greenard OLB Ankle LP No designation\nJonathan Jones CB Hamstring DNP No designation\nLandon Dickerson G Pectoral FP No designation\nMichael Carter II DB Abdomen LP No designation\nMoro Ojomo DT Neck LP No designation\nNolan Smith OLB Concussion LP No designation\nSaquon Barkley RB Hamstring/Back DNP No designation\nSmael Mondon Jr. LB Knee LP No designation\nTyler Steen G Shoulder FP No designation\nZack Baun LB Shoulder FP No designation\nWashington Commanders (WAS) Injury Report\nPlayer Pos Injury Wed Game Status\nCharles Omenihu DE LP No designation\nColson Yankoff TE FP No designation\nFabian Moreau CB FP No designation\nJavon Kinlaw DT DNP No designation\nJayden Daniels QB FP No designation\nJer'Zhan Newton DT LP No designation\nJohn Bates TE DNP No designation\nMarcus Mariota QB FP No designation\nStefon Diggs WR DNP No designation\nTreylon Burks WR LP No designation\nNFL Injury Report: Practice Reports for Every Team\nLoading report…\nAll games\nAll teams\nLoading the latest report…\nNFL Injury Designations Explained\nEvery team is required to release a weekly injury report during the season, and those reports can designate an injured player as questionable, doubtful, or out.\nWhat do those designations mean?\nQuestionable: Player is uncertain to play\nDoubtful: Player is unlikely to play\nOut: Player will not play\n[[[\"Sharp NFL Betting Picks\"],[\"Best Bets: ATS & Game Total Picks (Thursday)\"],[\"Player Props & Predictions (Friday)\"],[\"Referee Assignments & Penalty Trends (Thursday)\"],[\"Key NFL Injuries: Betting Impact & Picks (Saturday)\"],[\"Passing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\"],[\"Receiving Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\"],[\"Rushing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\"],[\" First & Anytime Touchdown Picks \"],[\" Parlay Picks & Same Game Parlays \"],[\" Weather Betting Impact \"],[\" Odds & Picks \"],[\" Prop Odds & Picks \"],[\" Implied Totals \"],[\" Matchups Tool \"],[\" Fantasy Cheat Sheet \"]],[{\"row\":0,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":0,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0},{\"row\":1,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":1,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":2,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":2,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":3,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":3,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":4,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":4,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":5,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":5,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":6,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":6,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":7,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":7,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":8,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":8,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":9,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":9,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":10,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":10,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":11,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":11,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":12,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":13,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":13,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":14,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":14,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":15,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":15,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}}],[],[]] []\nSharp NFL Betting Picks\nBest Bets: ATS & Game Total Picks (Thursday)\nPlayer Props & Predictions (Friday)\nReferee Assignments & Penalty Trends (Thursday)\nKey NFL Injuries: Betting Impact & Picks (Saturday)\nPassing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\nReceiving Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\nRushing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\nFirst & Anytime Touchdown Picks\nParlay Picks & Same Game Parlays\nWeather Betting Impact\nOdds & Picks\nProp Odds & Picks\nImplied Totals\nMatchups Tool\nFantasy Cheat Sheet","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Sharp Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.sharpfootballanalysis.com/betting/nfl-first-touchdown-scorer-bet-picks-prediction/","canonical_url":"https://www.sharpfootballanalysis.com/betting/nfl-first-touchdown-scorer-bet-picks-prediction/","url_hash":"a8fc2919a0f29cac23808d52216adacdc29ab4ef027d048e22217de4da415680","content_hash":"9ffb44bb32ed5878f8524e088f264c1004e188a16ae44d5ac8de4e6ee00766af","title":"First &#038; Anytime Touchdown Scorer Bets: Week 8","summary":"Two of the most popular NFL bets this season are First Touchdown Scorer and Anytime Touchdown Scorer. Every week during the NFL season, our experts will give you their prediction on which player they think will score the first TD in every game. These prop bets can be difficult to predict, but they are a [...]","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:15:57.000Z","confidence":0.69,"author":"Josh Shepardson","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"First & Anytime Touchdown Scorer Bets: Week 8\nBy Josh Shepardson | 2026-10-29T10:52:38-04:00 Oct 29, 2026 |\nView Larger Image\nTwo of the most popular NFL bets this season are First Touchdown Scorer and Anytime Touchdown Scorer.\nEvery week during the NFL season, our experts will give you their prediction on which player they think will score the first TD in every game.\nThese prop bets can be difficult to predict, but they are a fan favorite among many NFL bettors.\nWhat is a first touchdown scorer bet?\nTo win this bet, you must correctly pick the player to score the first touchdown in the game - the first player who receives a touchdown pass or crosses the goal line with the ball.\nA touchdown scorer is defined as the player in possession of the ball in the end zone and not the player who throws the TD.\nWhat is an anytime touchdown scorer bet?\nTo win this NFL bet, you must correctly pick a player who will score a touchdown . Similar to first touchdown bets, the player is the one who crosses the end zone himself, not the QB who throws to that player.\nBefore placing your anytime TD or first TD bet, be sure to check out our DraftKings Sportsbook bonus code\nFirst & Anytime Touchdown Scorer Predictions & Bets for Week 8\nFind Anytime Touchdown Odds on Our NFL Player Props Odds Page\nPanthers @ Packers 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nJosh Jacobs (RB, Packers) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+550)\nThe Panthers have allowed the most rushing yards per game (126.8), the most yards per carry (5.2), and the second-most rushing touchdowns per game (1.5) to running backs this season. Tampa Bay's trio of Bucky Irving , Kenneth Gainwell , and Sean Tucker truck-sticked them for 246 rushing yards and 3 rushing touchdowns. Jacobs handled 11 of Green Bay's backfield's 17 rush attempts (64.7%) in his return from the NFL Commissioner's Exempt List. Jacobs logged the team's only run inside the five-yard line. Last season, he had 22 of Green Bay's 29 rush attempts inside the five-yard line (75.9%).\n»  Bet it now +550\nPanthers @ Packers Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nMatthew Golden (WR, Packers) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+145)\nThe Panthers have allowed only 1 receiving touchdown to outside wide receivers in three games since putting starting cornerbacks Mike Jackson and Jaycee Horn on injured reserve after Week 3. However, they've allowed the eighth-most yards per target (9.02) to outside wideouts since Week 4, and Golden is tailor-made to burn them. The second-year wideout leads the Packers in air yard share (39.6%) and red-zone targets (13) and has a 14.04-yard average depth of target (aDOT) through seven games. Golden is also tied for team lead in end-zone targets (8), with 3 receiving touchdowns and 5.4 expected receiving touchdowns .\n»  Bet it now +145\nColts @ Jaguars 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nBhayshul Tuten (RB, Jaguars) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+550)\nThe Colts traded DeForest Buckner, removing a quality defensive lineman from a defense that's already unimposing against the run. Indianapolis ranks 27th in yards allowed per carry (4.49) to running backs, and they've permitted 5 rushing touchdowns to them. Tuten has scored 2 rushing touchdowns and 2 receiving touchdowns this season. He's also handled 65.3% of Jacksonville's backfield's rush attempts. Unfortunately, he's shared work with Chris Rodriguez around the goal line, but the split is 4 carries inside the five-yard line for Rodriguez to 3 for Tuten. So, the sample is still small, and Tuten has converted 2 of his tries into touchdowns versus 1 for Rodriguez.\n»  Bet it now +550\nColts @ Jaguars Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nBrenton Strange (TE, Jaguars) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+210)\nStrange has 3 red-zone targets this year, but he's turned his only end-zone target into a touchdown. Strange is also an expected-touchdown underachiever, with 1.7 expected touchdowns this season. He has a decent matchup this week, as the Colts have allowed 5 receiving touchdowns to tight ends this year. Travis Kelce, Foster Moreau, Pat Freiermuth, and T.J. Hockenson have reached the end zone against the Colts.\n»  Bet it now +210\nTitans @ Bengals 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nTee Higgins (WR, Bengals) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+650)\nAmong Bengals with at least 15 routes this season, Higgins is first in route participation rate (81.8%), target share (22.8%), target rate per route (26%), air yard share (43.9%), receptions per game (5.5), receiving yards per game (95.2), and yards per route run (2.96). He trails Ja'Marr Chase (5 receiving touchdowns and 6 end-zone targets) and Mike Gesicki (5 receiving touchdowns and 4 end-zone targets) in touchdowns and end-zone targets but has scored 2 touchdowns on his only 2 end-zone targets this year. However, Higgins and Chase are tied for the team lead in end-zone targets (14) and receiving touchdowns (13) since last season.\n»  Bet it now +650\nTitans @ Bengals Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nSamaje Perine (RB, Bengals) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+235)\nChase Brown is Cincinnati's lead running back, but it's uncertain if he's the team's preferred option in scoring territory. He's handled 4 of the team's rush attempts inside the five-yard line this year, posting a 50% success rate and scoring 1 touchdown. However, after their Week 6 bye, Perine was subbed in for the team's only goal-line attempt and punched in a 1-yard rushing touchdown. Perine's Anytime Touchdown line is a value if he's the goal-line back, but he also has backdoor touchdown potential if the 10.5-point favored Bengals handle their business and use Perine to salt the game away in garbage time.\n»  Bet it now +235\nBrowns @ Steelers 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nDarnell Washington (TE, Steelers) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+1300)\nWashington has scored a touchdown in back-to-back games, and three of his last four, reaching paydirt against the Browns in Week 4. The Browns have played man coverage at the highest rate (45.5%) and single-high coverage at the highest rate (75.2%) this year. Washington has a 24% target rate per route and 1.76 Y/RR on 42 routes against man and a 23% target rate per route and 1.78 Y/RR on 74 routes against single-high this year. The gigantic tight end is second on the Steelers in receiving touchdowns (3) but first in expected receiving touchdowns (2.9) and end-zone targets (6) and tied for first in red-zone targets (6). Washington is a very inviting target for Aaron Rodgers in the end zone.\n»  Bet it now +1300\nBrowns @ Steelers Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nKC Concepcion (WR, Browns) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+270)\nConcepcion is coming off a breakout performance, running circles around the Titans for 8 receptions and 129 receiving yards. He hasn't reached the end zone yet. Nevertheless, among Browns with at least 20 routes this year, Concepcion is first in target share (20.5%), first in first-read share (27.1%, second in target rate per route (24%), and first in receptions per game (4.3). Concepcion is too dynamic to be kept out of the end zone much longer with as many opportunities as the Browns are feeding him.\n»  Bet it now +270\nVikings @ Lions 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nAmon-Ra St. Brown (WR, Lions) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+700)\nThe Sun God has had his way with Brian Flores. In six games against Flores, ARSB has had a 32.1% target share, 35% target rate per route, 41.4% first-read rate, 47.1% air yard share, 8.3 receptions per game, 100.7 receiving yards per game, 3.34 yards per route run (Y/RR), 7 red-zone targets, 3 end-zone targets, 3 receiving touchdowns, and 3.3 expected receiving touchdowns.\n»  Bet it now +700\nVikings @ Lions Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nT.J. Hockenson (TE, Vikings) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+260)\nHockenson has played in only three games with Kyler Murray in which neither left early with a concussion. Still, in those games, Hockenson had a 24.4% target share, 31% target rate per route, 28.1% first-read rate, 25.9% air yard share, 6.3 receptions per game, 55.0 receiving yards per game, 2.32 Y/RR, 5 red-zone targets, 1 end-zone target, 1 receiving touchdown, and 1.6 expected receiving touchdowns. Hockenson has a drool-inducing matchup in a revenge game against a Detroit defense that has allowed the seventh-most yards per target (8.6) and the most receiving touchdowns (10) to tight ends this season. The Panthers were the only team that played the Lions and didn't have a tight end splash paydirt, and the Saints, Bills, Jets, and Cardinals had multiple tight ends score touchdowns against them.\n»  Bet it now +260\nFalcons @ Buccaneers 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nJahan Dotson (WR, Falcons) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+2500)\nDotson has a 31.0% air yard share, 4 red-zone targets, 4 end-zone targets, 2 receiving touchdowns (both on end-zone targets), and 1.5 expected receiving touchdowns in five games with Michael Penix starting for the Falcons this year. The Penn State legend should also benefit from Tampa Bay's blitzing tendencies. The Bucs have blitzed at the fourth-highest rate (41.5%) this season, and Dotson has a 20% target rate per route and 3.20 Y/RR on 46 routes against the blitz in Penix's starts.\n»  Bet it now +2500\nFalcons @ Buccaneers Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nEmeka Egbuka (WR, Buccaneers) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+210)\nEgbuka hasn't been efficient, but his 83.4% route participation rate, 25.3% target share, 31.7% first-read rate, 34.8% air yard share, 6 red-zone targets, 4 end-zone targets, 2 receiving touchdowns, and 2.6 expected receiving touchdowns lead the Bucs this season. Volume, even inefficient volume, is king and can lead to touchdowns.\n»  Bet it now +210\nCardinals @ Cowboys 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nCeeDee Lamb (WR, Cowboys) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+625)\nLamb leads the Cowboys in target share (29.3%), target rate per route (34%), first-read rate (39.2%), air yard share (40.2%), receptions per game (7.6), receiving yards per game (93.0), yards per route run (2.74), red-zone targets (13), end-zone targets (9), receiving touchdowns (6), and expected receiving touchdowns (6.4). His matchup is dreamy. Arizona has allowed the second-most receiving touchdowns (10) to wide receivers in 2026.\n»  Bet it now +625\nCardinals @ Cowboys Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nRyan Flournoy (WR, Cowboys) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+265)\nFlournoy will enjoy the same favorable matchup as Lamb. Additionally, Arizona's coverage tendencies are a plus for Flournoy. The Cardinals rank fifth in zone coverage rate (82.1%) and two-high coverage (70.5%) this year. Among Cowboys with at least 30 routes, Flournoy is third on the team in target rate per route (20%) against two-high coverage this year. Furthermore, the Cardinals have played Cover 6 at the second-highest rate (25.9%), and Flournoy's 29% target rate per route is second only to Lamb's 34% among Cowboys with at least 10 routes against Cover 6 since last season.\n»  Bet it now +265\n[[[\"Sharp NFL Betting Picks\"],[\"Best Bets: ATS & Game Total Picks (Thursday)\"],[\"Player Props & Predictions (Friday)\"],[\"Referee Assignments & Penalty Trends (Thursday)\"],[\"Key NFL Injuries: Betting Impact & Picks (Saturday)\"],[\"Passing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\"],[\"Receiving Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\"],[\"Rushing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\"],[\" First & Anytime Touchdown Picks \"],[\" Parlay Picks & Same Game Parlays \"],[\" Weather Betting Impact \"],[\" Odds & Picks \"],[\" Prop Odds & Picks \"],[\" Implied Totals \"],[\" Matchups Tool \"],[\" Fantasy Cheat Sheet \"]],[{\"row\":0,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":0,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0},{\"row\":1,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":1,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":2,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":2,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":3,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":3,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":4,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":4,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":5,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":5,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":6,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":6,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":7,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":7,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":8,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":8,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":9,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":9,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":10,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":10,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":11,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":11,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":12,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":13,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":13,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":14,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":14,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":15,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":15,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}}],[],[]] []\nSharp NFL Betting Picks\nBest Bets: ATS & Game Total Picks (Thursday)\nPlayer Props & Predictions (Friday)\nReferee Assignments & Penalty Trends (Thursday)\nKey NFL Injuries: Betting Impact & Picks (Saturday)\nPassing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\nReceiving Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\nRushing Yards Leader Odds (Friday)\nFirst & Anytime Touchdown Picks\nParlay Picks & Same Game Parlays\nWeather Betting Impact\nOdds & Picks\nProp Odds & Picks\nImplied Totals\nMatchups Tool\nFantasy Cheat Sheet\nRaiders @ Jets 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nBrock Bowers (TE, Raiders) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+800)\nBowers is a total alpha. He's pacing the Raiders in target share (23.2%), first-read rate (31.3%), air yard share (32.5%), receptions per game (6.8), and receiving yards per game (91.0). Despite missing the first two games of the year, his 3 receiving touchdowns trail only Tre Tucker's 4 for the team lead, and he's amassed 7 red-zone targets and 4 end-zone targets in five games. The Jets have allowed only 1 receiving touchdown to a tight end this year, but Bowers has aligned inline only 12.7% of the time. He's aligned in the slot 50.8% of the time and wide 35.4%. So, Gang Green's 8 receiving touchdowns allowed to wideouts are more applicable for the matchup with Bowers.\n»  Bet it now +800\nRaiders @ Jets Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nOmar Cooper (WR, Jets) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+280)\nCooper had a 30-yard reception on his only route before getting injured in Week 1, and he's made up for lost time since returning from the IR in Week 6. In the past two weeks, he has a 74.2% route participation rate, 20.0% target share, 24% target rate per route, 29.3% first-read rate, 32.5% air yard share, 11 receptions, 218 receiving yards, 4.45 Y/RR, 2 red-zone targets, one end-zone target resulting in a touchdown, and 2 receiving touchdowns overall. The rookie wideout scored a touchdown in both contests. On the other side, the Raiders have allowed 8 receiving touchdowns to wide receivers this year, all scored since Week 4.\n»  Bet it now +280\nRavens @ Bills 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nJosh Allen (QB, Bills) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+500)\nAllen has gone full beast mode in 14 games the Bills have played with an over/under total of 50 points or higher since 2023. In those games, excluding kneel-downs, Allen has toted the rock 97 times (6.9 per game) for 600 rushing yards (42.9 per game) and 18 touchdowns.\n»  Bet it now +500\nRavens @ Bills Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nZay Flowers (WR, Ravens) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+155)\nThe Bills have been completely lost in the secondary, permitting an NFL-high 11 receiving touchdowns to wide receivers (11), despite having their bye last week. The Chargers are the only team that faced the Bills and didn't have a wideout score a touchdown. Flowers is balling this year, but his numbers in the limited sample of only 63 plays with Lamar Jackson are otherworldly. Flowers has a 47.4% target share, 41% target rate per route, and 8.02 Y/RR on those 63 plays. He's scored 3 touchdowns this season and should get in on the scoring fun in a probable shootout.\n»  Bet it now +155\nChargers @ Rams 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nPuka Nacua (WR, Rams) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+575)\nNacua has dominated the receiving work without Davante Adams. In four games without his fellow stud teammate since last year, Nacua has recorded a 29.5% target share, 34% target rate per route, 8.8 receptions per game, 104.0 receiving yards per game, 3.08 Y/RR, 5 touchdowns, 9 red-zone targets, and 2 end-zone targets.\n»  Bet it now +575\nChargers @ Rams Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nBlake Corum (RB, Rams) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+180)\nKyren Williams has a 61.3% snap share versus 36.3% for Corum in the last two weeks, but they have an identical 26 rush attempts and 1 rushing touchdown. They each have 1 carry inside the five-yard line since Week 6, too. Corum has also added a receiving touchdown in that span. Corum will get his drives and opportunities to cash in a touchdown against a defense that's allowed 6 rushing touchdowns and 1 receiving touchdown to running backs in 6 games this year.\n»  Bet it now +180\nPatriots @ Dolphins 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nRhamondre Stevenson (RB, Patriots) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+475)\nStevenson isn't a workhorse, but he's New England's top running back. He's handled 77 of New England's backfield's 164 rush attempts (47%) this season, including all 3 of the backfield's carries inside the five-yard line. Stevenson turned 2 of those 3 attempts into touchdowns. He's also scored 1 receiving touchdown, when the Bears comically forgot how to tackle on the final play of the first half on Thursday Night Football last week.\n»  Bet it now +475\nPatriots @ Dolphins Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nEli Raridon (TE, Patriots) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+425)\nRaridon scored a touchdown on his only reception in Week 1, but he also ran just 8 routes and had a 19.0% route participation rate. The rookie tight end ran 5 routes and had an 18.5% route participation rate in Week 2, but he's settled into a bigger role since. Since Week 4, Raridon has had a 56.8% snap share, a 37.7% route participation rate, a 23% target rate per route, 10 receptions, 136 receiving yards, 2.39 Y/RR, 3 red-zone targets, 2 end-zone targets, and 1 touchdown. He got in the paint last week against the Bears and can do so again this week. The Dolphins have allowed 6 receiving touchdowns to five different tight ends in six games, and they coughed up 2 receiving touchdowns to Mason Taylor last week.\n»  Bet it now +425\nChiefs @ Broncos 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nKenneth Walker (RB, Chiefs) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+400)\nThe Broncos might be better served selling out to stop Walker and force Patrick Mahomes to beat them with his lackluster pass-catching corps, but that's easier said than done. Walker piled up 173 rushing yards and 1 rushing touchdown and 18 receiving yards and 1 receiving touchdown against them in Week 1. Walker has scored 8 touchdowns in six games this year, getting in the end zone in four of those contests.\n»  Bet it now +400\nChiefs @ Broncos Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nJ.K. Dobbins (RB, Broncos) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+240)\nSince Sean Payton snatched the play-calling duties from Davis Webb in Week 5, the Broncos rank 23rd in pass rate over expected (-2.0% PROE). Payton's unlikely to change his play-calling tendencies against the Chiefs, as they rank 31st in PROE faced (-3.5%). Payton has given lip service to getting Jonah Coleman earning more opportunities, but it was Dobbins who punched in a 1-yard touchdown run on a drive the rookie played the majority of last week. Dobbins has scored a rushing touchdown in three straight contests.\n»  Bet it now +240\nEagles @ Commanders 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nDallas Goedert (TE, Eagles) is our pick for the first TD scorer bet (+1300)\nIn Tanner McKee's two starts this season, Goedert has an 18.8% target share, a 25% target rate per route, a 25.0% first-read rate, 11 receptions, 109 receiving yards, 1.85 Y/RR, and 1 red-zone target. Goedert has a tantalizing matchup against his NFC East foe. The Commanders are tied for the ninth-most yards allowed per target (9.00) to tight ends and have coughed up 8 touchdowns to them in six games. Goedert even victimized them, scoring 2 touchdowns against them in Week 1.\n»  Bet it now +1300\nEagles @ Commanders Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nAntonio Williams (WR, Commanders) is our pick for the anytime TD scorer bet (+310)\nTerry McLaurin is out for the season, and while Stefon Diggs might seem like the natural primary beneficiary of a bigger role, Dan Quinn mentioned Williams \"getting more targets.\" The rookie hasn't been a world-beater, but his 19% target rate per route on a 55.4% route participation rate is rock-solid. Williams has scored 1 touchdown on 2 red-zone targets and 2 end-zone targets, with 1.4 expected touchdowns. Furthermore, Williams has inside-outside versatility, with a 50.4% wide alignment rate and 48.9% slot rate. His versatility could help him escape Quinyon Mitchell's sticky coverage and allow him to cook the Eagles from the slot. Philadelphia has allowed only 2 receiving touchdowns to outside wideouts this year but 7 to those aligned in the slot.\n»  Bet it now +310\nBears @ Seahawks 1st TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nComing Soon!\nBears @ Seahawks Anytime TD Scorer Bet Prediction:\nComing Soon!","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Sharp Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"https://www.sharpfootballanalysis.com/fantasy/fantasy-football-rankings-weekly/","canonical_url":"https://www.sharpfootballanalysis.com/fantasy/fantasy-football-rankings-weekly/","url_hash":"d4d88dfa53570d95b8678a040fef39d2b1f00076a2fdc9556a6f728dfeaf0423","content_hash":"1a30505ee96d12f7371cb2705233c23b224a43f4483d0c6ab446e357b8c24b5f","title":"Week 8 Fantasy Football Rankings, 2026","summary":"One of the premier fantasy football analysts, Rich Hribar ranks all q