lCol\":0,\"prop\":0},{\"row\":11,\"col\":1,\"visualRow\":11,\"visualCol\":1,\"prop\":1},{\"row\":11,\"col\":2,\"visualRow\":11,\"visualCol\":2,\"prop\":2},{\"row\":11,\"col\":3,\"visualRow\":11,\"visualCol\":3,\"prop\":3},{\"row\":11,\"col\":4,\"visualRow\":11,\"visualCol\":4,\"prop\":4},{\"row\":12,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0},{\"row\":12,\"col\":1,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":1,\"prop\":1},{\"row\":12,\"col\":2,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":2,\"prop\":2},{\"row\":12,\"col\":3,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":3,\"prop\":3},{\"row\":12,\"col\":4,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":4,\"prop\":4}],[],[]] []\nArizona Rank @ Dallas Rank\n6.5 Spread -6.5\n24.0 Implied Total 30.5\n20.3 26 Points/Gm 27.0 5\n29.7 32 Points All./Gm 25.7 23\n68.4 2 Plays/Gm 62.9 13\n58.0 3 Opp. Plays/Gm 63.1 18\n4.6 29 Off. Yards/Play 5.6 11\n5.0 31 Def. Yards/Play 6.0 29\n37.8% 26 Rush% 36.4% 30\n62.2% 7 Pass% 63.6% 3\n46.8% 27 Opp. Rush % 48.9% 31\n53.2% 6 Opp. Pass % 51.1% 2\nThe Cowboys average 6.9 plays per possession, the most in the league.\nArizona averages 6.2 plays per possession, 4th in the league.\nArizona leads the NFL in drives of 10 or more plays (21).\nDallas has scored on 53.1% of its possessions, 2nd in the league.\nDallas has allowed opponents to score on 46.4% of their drives, 27th\nArizona has allowed opponents to score on 46.7% of their drives, 28th.\nArizona has allowed a league-high 9 touchdowns from outside of the red zone.\nThe Cowboys have converted 74.1% (20 of 27) of their red-zone trips into touchdowns, 3rd in the league.\nThe Cardinals have converted 42.9% (12 of 28) of their red zone trips into touchdowns, the lowest rate in the league.\n3.3% of Arizona's offensive plays have gained 20 or more yards, the lowest rate in the league.\nThe Cardinals average 2.3 fewer yards per passing play than their opponent, the worst margin in the league.\nTrust = spike production for that player\nCardinals vs. Cowboys Fantasy Quarterback Preview\nDak Prescott (TRUST)\nPrescott completed a season-low 55.6% of his passes (15 of 27) on Monday night for 212 yards (his fewest since Week 1), but he delivered his second-best fantasy outing (23.3 points) of the year on the back of throwing 3 touchdown passes and running in a two-point conversion.\nThis week, Prescott is at home with a massive team total against an Arizona defense that has been hemorrhaging points to opposing quarterbacks.\nThe Cardinals allow 18.6 passing points per game (29th), rank 31st in yards allowed per pass attempt (8.5), and surrender a league-high 8.5% touchdown rate.\nThe Cardinals have allowed six consecutive QB1 scorers.\nPrescott has played 18 career home games with an implied team total of 30-plus points .\nIn those games, he averages 24.3 fantasy points per game with 15 QB1 scoring weeks.\nHe has thrown multiple passing touchdowns in 16 of those games.\nJacoby Brissett\nBrissett had another down week in Week 7, completing 56.2% of his passes (27 of 48) for 5.7 yards per pass attempt.\nBrissett has not thrown for 7.0 yards per pass attempt in a game since Week 1.\nOnly Cam Ward (by decimals at 5.7 Y/A) and Jalon Daniels (5.1 Y/A) have fewer yards per pass attempt than Brissett (5.7 Y/A).\nIt feels like we are closing on Brissett losing the job, but Carson Beck isn't ready, and Arizona may see no real point in turning to Gardner Minshew as a \"kicking the can\" move.\nBrissett could be shelved, but the Week 8 outlook is solid for matchup-based 2QB gamers and DFS if he stays on the field.\nIf you are thin at quarterback and were starting Brock Purdy, Tyler Shough, or CJ Stroud, Brissett is in the streaming conversation.\nArizona has a 24-point team total, and they've shown they'll throw a lot when chasing points.\nBrissett has 53 dropbacks against Denver on Sunday (13.8 second-half fantasy points).\nTwo weeks ago, against Detroit, Brissett had 52 dropbacks (17.9 second-half fantasy points).\nIn Week 3 against the 49ers, Brissett had 53 dropbacks (20.0 second-half fantasy points).\nYou may not want to watch the first half, but Brissett has volume-based potential to score points in a loss.\nHe also gets a favorable matchup.\nDallas ranks 25th in passing points allowed (15.6 per game), allowing a 68.2% completion rate (30th), 7.7 yards per pass attempt (27th), and a 5.6% touchdown rate (24th).\nThey have been better the past two weeks, keeping us honest.\nThey held Jordan Love to 6.7 yards per pass attempt (though his teammates left many plays on the field) and Tanner McKee to 6.0 Y/A on Monday night (with Philly beaten up).\nBrissett was QB10 (24.8 points) in Dallas a year ago, completing 21 of 31 passes for 261 yards and 2 touchdowns and adding a rushing score to his line.\nCardinals vs. Cowboys Fantasy Running Back Preview\nTo continue reading this article\nselect one of the packages below\nAll-Access : Unlocks all fantasy content & Warren Sharp's betting recommendations for 2026.\n- 2025 Record: 500-374 (57%) +70.77 Units -\n- 2025 Best Bet Record: 17-3 (85%) -\n- Computer Totals Record Last 5 Years: 144-65 (69%) -\nLEARN ABOUT ALL-ACCESS\nFantasy Packages : Unlocks all of Rich Hribar's industry-leading fantasy content for 2026.\nLEARN ABOUT FANTASY\nAlready a Subscriber? Log In\nMore Week 8 Fantasy Breakdowns From The Worksheet:\n[[[\"Week 8 NFL Games\",\"Time\"],[\" Panthers @ Packers \",\"Thursday Night Football\"],[\" Ravens @ Bills \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Vikings @ Lions \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Falcons @ Buccaneers \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Colts @ Jaguars \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Titans @ Bengals \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Cardinals @ Cowboys \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Raiders @ Jets \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Browns @ Steelers \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Chargers @ Rams \",\"Sunday -- 4:05 p.m. ET\"],[\" Chiefs @ Broncos \",\"Sunday -- 4:25 p.m. ET\"],[\" Patriots @ Dolphins \",\"Sunday -- 4:25 p.m. ET\"],[\" Eagles @ Commanders \",\"Sunday Night Footb