\n19.5 Implied Total 27.0\n22.0 20 Points/Gm 25.7 9\n25.7 23 Points All./Gm 17.3 3\n65.6 7 Plays/Gm 60.2 23\n58.4 4 Opp. Plays/Gm 59.5 10\n4.5 31 Off. Yards/Play 5.8 8\n5.8 28 Def. Yards/Play 5.8 27\n43.6% 16 Rush% 46.3% 10\n56.4% 17 Pass% 53.7% 23\n44.7% 20 Opp. Rush % 37.5% 4\n55.3% 13 Opp. Pass % 62.5% 29\nThe Colts have lost 11 straight road games against Jacksonville (10 in Jacksonville).\nThe Colts are 0-4 against teams with a winning record this season.\nThe Colts are the only team in the league to lead and trail in every game this season.\nJacksonville has outscored opponents 82-40 (+42) in the first half, 3rd in the league.\nThe Jaguars lead the league in points-off-turnover margin (+31).\nThe Colts are last in the league in turnover margin (-9).\n32% of Jacksonville's passing plays gain 10 or more yards, 3rd in the league.\n21.2% of Indianapolis' passing plays gain 10 or more yards, 28th.\nThe Colts have a 44.5% success rate on rushing plays (8th) compared to 40.5% on passing plays (23rd).\nThe Jaguars have the highest success rate against the run (67.2%) compared to 52.9% against the pass (27th).\nTrust = spike production for that player\nColts vs. Jaguars Fantasy Quarterback Preview\nTrevor Lawrence\nLawrence comes out of the bye completing 65.2% of his passes (QB14) for 8.0 yards per pass attempt (QB5), 12.3 yards per completion (QB4), and a league-high 7.6% touchdown rate.\nHe leads all quarterbacks in passing points per dropback (0.53).\nThe only thing slowing Lawrence down is Jacksonville's success, since he is the QB20 in dropbacks per game (33.5).\nHe is the QB23 in fourth-quarter scoring (3.5 points per game) and last in fourth-quarter dropbacks per game (6.0).\nThe Jaguars could get into cruise control here, but if they do, Lawrence will surely be part of any lead-building as a QB1.\nThe Colts rank 21st in passing points allowed per game (14.8), 21st in yards per pass attempt (7.5), 30th in yards per completion (12.3), and 23rd in touchdown rate (5.2%).\nLawrence has thrived this season with play-action passing.\nOn play-action passes, Lawrence is second in the league in rating (121.6), completing 67.3% of his passes (33 of 49) for 8.7 Y/A (5th) with an 8.2% touchdown rate (4th).\nThe Colts have allowed 8.7 yards per pass attempt (27th) and a 9.2% touchdown rate (31st) on play-action passes.\nDaniel Jones\nJones is completing 59.6% of his passes (27th) for 5.8 yards per pass attempt (30th), 9.8 yards per completion (29th), a league-low 1.7% touchdown rate, and a 2.9% touchdown rate (28th).\nHis 0.19 passing points per dropback is ahead of only Jalon Daniels (0.18) for qualifying passers.\nIt is hard to trust Jones as more than a back-end QB2.\nHe has already had good matchups against Washington (7.9 points) and Tennessee (13.8 points) with no fantasy production to lean on.\nIf you have to go back to Jones in 2QB formats, he gets another matchup that has some upside on paper.\nJacksonville allows only 13.6 passing points per game (13th), but they allow 7.9 yards per pass attempt (28th) and 12.1 yards per completion (29th).\nWhat has saved them is their 3.3% touchdown rate (7th) and 3.3% interception rate (29th).\nColts vs. Jaguars Fantasy Running Back Preview\nTo continue reading this article\nselect one of the packages below\nAll-Access : Unlocks all fantasy content & Warren Sharp's betting recommendations for 2026.\n- 2025 Record: 500-374 (57%) +70.77 Units -\n- 2025 Best Bet Record: 17-3 (85%) -\n- Computer Totals Record Last 5 Years: 144-65 (69%) -\nLEARN ABOUT ALL-ACCESS\nFantasy Packages : Unlocks all of Rich Hribar's industry-leading fantasy content for 2026.\nLEARN ABOUT FANTASY\nAlready a Subscriber? Log In\nMore Week 8 Fantasy Breakdowns From The Worksheet:\n[[[\"Week 8 NFL Games\",\"Time\"],[\" Panthers @ Packers \",\"Thursday Night Football\"],[\" Ravens @ Bills \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Vikings @ Lions \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Falcons @ Buccaneers \",\"Sunday -- 1 p.m. ET\"],[\" Col