hash":"d9633d144d9f816dd72dcbda52d41be97c7583cc61fd79a50e3163df4be90cd0","title":"Week 8 Fantasy Football Waiver Wire: Top Pickups &#038; Adds","summary":"Week 8 Fantasy Football Waiver Wire: Top Targets Jonah Coleman Makai Lemon Omar Cooper Jr. Antonio Williams Mike Washington Jr. Welcome to Week 8 of the waiver wire. Recommended adds are available in at least 60% of ESPN leagues, and the watch list consists of players worth monitoring. The deep cuts section for running backs [...]","published_at":"2026-10-27T19:20:12.000Z","confidence":0.69,"author":"Raymond Summerlin","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Week 8 Fantasy Football Waiver Wire: Top Pickups & Adds\nBy Raymond Summerlin | 2026-10-27T15:50:12-04:00 Oct 27, 2026 |\nView Larger Image\nWeek 8 Fantasy Football Waiver Wire: Top Targets\nJonah Coleman\nMakai Lemon\nOmar Cooper Jr.\nAntonio Williams\nMike Washington Jr.\nWelcome to Week 8 of the waiver wire.\nRecommended adds are available in at least 60% of ESPN leagues, and the watch list consists of players worth monitoring.\nThe deep cuts section for running backs and receivers highlights players who are rostered in fewer than 5% of ESPN leagues, for all you \"not in my league\" degens.\nI do not list recommended FAAB percentages for every player because a much better resource for researching what you need to bid is available, thanks to our friends at FAABLab.\nFinally, I do not rank kickers and defenses because, frankly, I don't care about them and would like to see them disappear from the game.\nWith those caveats out of the way, let's get to it.\nContents\n1 Week 8 Fantasy Football Waiver Wire: Top Targets\n2 Week 8 Quarterback Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\n3 Week 8 Running Back Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\n4 Week 8 Wide Receiver Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\n5 Week 8 Tight End Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\nWeek 8 Quarterback Waiver Wire Targets\nSam Darnold\nJacoby Brissett\nWeek 8 Running Back Waiver Wire Targets\nJonah Coleman\nMike Washington Jr.\nKaelon Black\nSeth McGowan\nWeek 8 Wide Receiver Waiver Wire Targets\nMakai Lemon\nOmar Cooper Jr.\nAntonio Williams\nTroy Franklin\nJordyn Tyson\nWeek 8 Tight End Waiver Wire Targets\nChig Okonkwo\nAJ Barner\nMason Taylor\n[[[\"Sharp Football Fantasy Articles\"],[\" Fantasy Cheat Sheet \"],[\" The Worksheet Game Previews \"],[\" Fantasy Football Rankings \"],[\" Waiver Wire Pickups \"],[\" DFS Picks: DraftKings & FanDuel \"],[\" Live Fantasy Football Q&A With Rich Hribar \"],[\" Implied Team Totals \"],[\" Expected Fantasy Points Tool \"],[\" Expected Fantasy Points Allowed \"],[\" Red Zone Usage \"],[\" IR Tracker \"],[\" NFL Odds & Picks \"],[\" NFL Prop Odds & Picks \"]],[{\"row\":0,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":0,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0},{\"row\":1,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":1,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":2,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":2,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":3,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":3,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":4,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":4,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":5,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":5,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":6,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":6,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":7,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":7,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":8,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":8,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":9,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":9,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":10,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":10,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":11,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":11,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":12,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":12,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}},{\"row\":13,\"col\":0,\"visualRow\":13,\"visualCol\":0,\"prop\":0,\"jtcellstyle\":{\"font-weight\":\"bold\"}}],[],[]] []\nSharp Football Fantasy Articles\nFantasy Cheat Sheet\nThe Worksheet Game Previews\nFantasy Football Rankings\nWaiver Wire Pickups\nDFS Picks: DraftKings & FanDuel\nLive Fantasy Football Q&A With Rich Hribar\nImplied Team Totals\nExpected Fantasy Points Tool\nExpected Fantasy Points Allowed\nRed Zone Usage\nIR Tracker\nNFL Odds & Picks\nNFL Prop Odds & Picks\nWeek 8 Quarterback Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\n1. Sam Darnold, Seahawks – Available in 69% of ESPN leagues\nThis one is pretty simple. If Darnold is forced to throw more because Chicago can score against the Seahawks, he should have a good fantasy game. The Bears are dead last in yards per attempt allowed, 25th in touchdown rate allowed, and 26th in explosive pass rate allowed. We need the Bears to push the scoreboard and get the Seahawks into more passing situations, but if that happens, Darnold will find success.\n2. Jacoby Brissett, Cardinals – Available in 80.3% of ESPN leagues\nBrissett should probably top this list, as this looks like a prime matchup and game-script combo for him to hit his fantasy ceiling. My main concern is an in-game benching given Brissett's struggles, but the fact that Carson Beck is dealing with back spasms could mean those fears are unwarranted.\nWatch List\nIt was relative to their pre-bye performance, but the Dolphins were impressive on offense against the Jets, and Malik Willis had a good fantasy game. I would like to see the offense function well again before chasing it…The Bucs are a pass funnel, but they have not been a great target for fantasy quarterbacks. Michael Penix does have 3 touchdowns in back-to-back games… Geno Smith threw 3 touchdowns last week and has a good matchup against the Raiders, but the Jets simply have not been throwing enough to really trust him as a streaming option.\nWeek 8 Running Back Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\n1. Jonah Coleman, Broncos – Available in 75.8% of ESPN leagues\nI hope you got him last week, because I would imagine the FAAB price has gone up. As a word of caution from a Coleman truther, we need him to completely send J.K. Dobbins to the bench to be a real fantasy factor. Getting 50% of the running back carries in his first game back is positive, but he built a lot of that lead in the fourth quarter (4 carries to Dobbins' 0). Also, 50% was still only 9 carries. Sure, Sean Payton said he wants to get Coleman more work, but he has said that about Marvin Mims roughly 1,000 times, and it has never happened. Coleman is an add in every league. That is not in question. But he is still more of a stash than a fantasy starter, even in the bye weeks.\n2. Mike Washington Jr, Raiders – Available in 82.3% of ESPN leagues\nAnother week. Another game where Washington looks much better than Ashton Jeanty when given opportunities. For the season, Washington is averaging 4.9 yards per carry with an explosive run on 15% of his attempts. Jeanty is at 3.1 yards per carry with an explosive run on 4.7% of his attempts. At some point, this usage has to flip, though I still am not sure what Washington's ceiling ultimately is unless Jeanty is shut down and given a chance to get healthy. Assuming Jeanty remains active, even if Washington gets more carries, Jeanty would seemingly still be a factor in the passing game.\n3. Kaelon Black, 49ers – Available in 78.1% of ESPN leagues\nIt does not seem like Christian McCaffrey 's injury is serious (he came back to play through it in the second half), and the 49ers are on bye this week. Still, Black is someone to stash in an open roster spot just to see what happens.\n4. Seth McGowan, Colts – Available in 96% of ESPN leagues\nThe Colts started their fire sale by trading Quenton Nelson on Tuesday, and it would not be a shock if Jonathan Taylor joins him out the door ahead of the trade deadline. That alone makes McGowan worth stashing, especially after he set a new season-high with 12 touches against the Vikings. That said, it is not a given that McGowan would be a locked-in fantasy starter even if Taylor is moved. Indy's offense is bad and would be worse without Taylor. We also don't know how the Colts view McGowan. Is he just a good complement to Taylor, or do they think he can start if something happens to Taylor? Either way, McGowan is worth stashing, but keep expectations in check.\nWatch List\nJeremiyah Love is supposed to return to practice on Wednesday, which would seemingly mean Bam Knight 's time in the sun is over… Samaje Perine did not get a bump in usage coming out of the bye, putting him back in that handcuff group. I like Emmett Johnson and Ray Davis more as pure handcuff stashes. I could also get on board with Chris Rodriguez as a handcuff if something happens to Bhayshul Tuten , given how good Jacksonville's offense is. We need to see Brian Robinson back healthy before he gets back on that list…I would imagine Kyle Monangai returns this week, which puts Roschon Johnson back on the wire.\nDeep Cuts\nWe will see how the Chargers split the backfield coming out of the bye, but Kimani Vidal needs to really own the usage to be a fantasy asset… Ty Johnson should continue to have a defined passing-game role in a very good offense… Corey Kiner did get nearly 31% of the running back carries in Week 7, though that was only 4 attempts. He is more likely to be a thorn for the fantasy value of the other two backs rather than a real fantasy factor himself…With Tyrone Tracy heading to injured reserve, Devin Singletary 's role in the offense is more secure.\nWeek 8 Wide Receiver Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\n1. Makai Lemon, Eagles – Available in 62.5% of ESPN leagues\nIt makes sense that Lemon was dropped in many leagues given his start to the season, but he was always running routes. He finally converted the targets on Monday night, going for 67 yards and a touchdown. Staying away from this crumbling offense the rest of the way might be the answer, but I am interested in adding Lemon because of the conversations we saw last week about shutting down DeVonta Smith so he can get healthy. There is a real scenario where Lemon is the WR1 for an offense that has to throw a lot the rest of the way.\n2. Omar Cooper Jr, Jets – Available in 65.3% of ESPN leagues\nWe invested in Cooper last week, despite concerns about Adonai Mitchell 's potential return, because he was a young player who flashed. Mitchell did eat into some of Cooper's usage, with the rookie's route rate falling to a disappointing 69.7%. Still, Cooper received 17.2% of the team's targets and 35% of the air yards. Most importantly, he continued to make plays. I will always bet on young players who flash, but I would like to see that route rate pick back up.\n3. Antonio Williams, Commanders – Available in 92.9% of ESPN leagues\nI assume Lemon and Cooper are already rostered in most competitive leagues, and Williams should have been added last week even with the Commanders on bye. Even so, he is available in a lot more places. The Commanders have said Stefon Diggs ' role will not expand with Terry McLaurin out for the season. That could just mean a lot more Treylon Burks (assuming his health; he left the game late before the bye) and Dyami Brown , but as is the theme of this article, I am willing to bet on youth. Williams is a third-round rookie who has made plays with the ball in his hands this year, even if some of those have been called back. He was already running a route on 75% of the dropbacks before McLaurin was hurt, so we have a good idea he will be on the field.\n4. Troy Franklin, Broncos – Available in 99.6% of ESPN leagues\nI would much rather stash Tyson or some of the names on the watch list, but if you need someone for this week, Franklin could be an option. Jaylen Waddle left late in Denver's Week 7 win with what appeared to be a significant shoulder or chest injury. Sean Payton gave his yearly speech about getting Marvin Mims more involved, something that never happens, but with Pat Bryant on injured reserve, Franklin is more likely to get snaps and targets if Waddle has to miss time. Franklin was already in that role last year, and there was a long stretch where he out-targeted Courtland Sutton .\n5. Jordyn Tyson, Saints – Available in 65.7% of ESPN leagues\nTyson was never expected to play last week, but it was a bit disappointing that he did not return to practice. Either way, he appears to have a real chance of returning to the field after the Saints' Week 8 bye. It has been up and down, but we have seen the Saints offense support multiple pass catchers already this season, and Tyson is a first-round rookie who matches the upside archetype we are looking for in bench stashes.\nWatch List\nAs with Malik Willis , I would like to see the Dolphins offense be functional for another game before I dive in on any of the pass catchers. Caleb Douglas had a big game, but he ran fewer routes than Malik Washington and saw fewer targets than Chris Bell …I expect D.J. Moore to return following the bye, which sends Keon Coleman back to the waiver wire… Travis Hunter 's role is growing, but he still ran just 7 routes before the bye…The argument for Makai Lemon could be made for Dontayvion Wicks , though we need to see how his injury situation shakes out, and Darius Cooper . I would just rather bet on the first-round rookie…We don't know exactly when De'Zhaun Stribling will return, but he is eligible…I would like to see him running more routes, but Ja'Kobi Lane is second on the Ravens in targets over the last two games…The concerns I raised about Konata Mumpfield last week came true. Even with Davante Adams out, he ran a route on just 60% of the dropbacks with 2 targets.\nDeep Cuts\nMalachi Fields keeps making plays, though his ultimate target upside is questionable behind Malik Nabers and Isaiah Likely …It seems like Amon-Ra St. Brown is fine, but stashing Isaac TeSlaa in deeper leagues makes some sense… Mike Evans could be back after the bye, so it might not matter, but Jordan Watkins finally turned his routes into some targets against the Falcons… Emeka Egbuka will probably be back this week, but Tez Johnson benefited big from his absence… Elic Ayomanor ran a route on nearly 91% of the dropbacks in Week 7. Unfortunately, he plays for the Titans.\nWeek 8 Tight End Fantasy Football Waiver Targets\n1. Chig Okonkwo, Commanders – Available in 95.1% of ESPN leagues\nI am buying in on Antonio Williams , but the answer to the Terry McLaurin question could end up being Okonkwo. The tight end set a season high in route participation before the bye (88.9%) and was targeted 7 times. Okonkwo has been a low air yard target throughout his career and has just 11 end-zone targets in 72 career games, so he is a better bet in PPR formats. That said, he has been good after the catch in his career, and we have seen players like Evan Engram get there on volume alone as a primary target in a passing game.\n2. AJ Barner, Seahawks – Available in 93.8% of ESPN leagues\nI don't want to chase Barner every week because, despite his high route rate, he is a secondary option in a low-volume passing attack. That said, the game environment this week against the Bears could lead to more attempts, and the Seahawks have some receiver injuries. Barner has a 15.8% team target share over his last five games.\n3. Mason Taylor, Jets – Available in 99.7% of ESPN leagues\nThis could be point-chasing after he scored twice in Week 7, but Taylor has had a consistent role in the passing game since returning from injury. His 66.3% route rate over the last three games leaves something to be desired, but he has 17.2% of the team's targets over that span. This week, the Jets get a Raiders defense that has struggled against tight ends. Las Vegas is fourth in fantasy points per game allowed to the position and sixth in expected fantasy points allowed.\nWatch List\nI lost out in my game of Rams TE roulette last week, and now Terrance Ferguson is eligible to return from injured reserve. That will make it tough to project Ferguson, Davis Allen , Colby Parkinson , and Tyler Higbee each week… Mike Gesicki has scored a touchdown in four straight games, but that touchdown has been his only catch in each of the last two. He is running a route on fewer than 50% of the dropbacks… Darren Waller scored a 50-yard touchdown against the Bucs, but he remains a part-time player… Greg Dulcich is a part-time player on a low-volume passing offense, which is a hard way to live as a fantasy asset… Eli Raridon continues to produce when given the opportunity, but he is just not running enough routes right now to be a fantasy asset.","revision_hash":null},{"source":"VSiN","source_type":"betting","url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/panthers-vs-packers-week-8-picks-and-betting-systems/","canonical_url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/panthers-vs-packers-week-8-picks-and-betting-systems/","url_hash":"65d6b9c720dc06cb4ab1bf2f6cd77ccf0ca7cc2f0482cd04d3001edb766e0675","content_hash":"521fb741cc2a76d9c82d0f6b0056b0c1d643c04412bd1d55de4ee86577541a92","title":"Panthers vs. Packers Week 8 Picks and Betting Systems","summary":"🏀 The VSiN College Basketball Betting Guide Is Here! Our 80-page guide features conference previews, team breakdowns and Best Bets from VSiN&#8217;s experts to get you ready for the season. &#62;&#62; Download Your College Basketball Betting Guide 🏈 Are the Packers Really the Better Team? &#8220;Over the last four weeks, the Packers have looked like [&#8230;] The post Panthers vs. Packers Week 8 Picks and Betting Systems appeared first on VSiN .","published_at":"2026-10-29T04:33:02.000Z","confidence":0.71,"author":"Bill Adee","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Home NFL Panthers vs. Packers Week 8 Picks and Betting Systems\nGreen Bay Packers defensive end Micah Parsons (1) celebrates after sacking Minnesota Vikings quarterback J.J. McCarthy (9) on Sunday, November 23, 2025, at Lambeau Field in Green Bay, Wis.\nX\nFacebook\nEmail\n🏀 The VSiN College Basketball Betting Guide Is Here!\nOur 80-page guide features conference previews, team breakdowns and Best Bets from VSiN's experts to get you ready for the season.\nDownload Your College Basketball Betting Guide\n🏈 Are the Packers Really the Better Team?\n\"Over the last four weeks, the Packers have looked like one of the best teams in football.\"\nThat's VSiN.com senior editor Zach Cohen, citing Expected Points Added (EPA) numbers in his preview of tonight's Panthers-Packers game at Lambeau Field.\nGreen Bay has gone 3-1 over that stretch and is a 3.5-point favorite over Carolina to kick off Week 8.\nBut before you assume Zach's pick, consider what else he discovered:\n\"When looking up all of these numbers for the Packers, do you know what stood out the most? The Panthers have a better statistical profile over the course of the entire season. Carolina also matches up well with Green Bay in several ways.\"\nGreen Bay is a 3.5-point favorite at Circa, but Zach's analysis suggests this matchup may be closer than the spread indicates.\nSo which matters more — Green Bay's recent improvement or Carolina's stronger full-season numbers?\nZach breaks down the matchup and has two Best Bets: a side and a player prop.\nZach Cohen's Panthers-Packers Best Bets\nDave Tuley sees an opportunity, too. He likes the idea of backing a team coming off an embarrassing defeat and believes Carolina has reasons to respond after Sunday's 43-13 loss to Tampa Bay.\nTuley's Takes on Every Week 8 Game\nMakinen's Numbers Disagree\nSteve Makinen's Power Ratings make Green Bay a 5.6-point favorite. But several of his betting systems point toward Carolina.\nCarolina is coming off an ugly 43-13 loss to Tampa Bay. In the last 34 qualifying games, NFL teams that have missed covering the spread by 30 points or more have bounced back as road underdogs of at least three points, going 23-10-1 ATS (69.7%).\nAnother Thursday Night Football system favors road teams coming off home losses. Those teams are 32-18-1 ATS (64%) over the last four-plus seasons.\nAnd Green Bay qualifies for a play-against system that has seen favorites coming off a straight-up loss in which they covered the spread go just 34-63 ATS (35.1%) since 2019.\nSteve's Week 8 Best Bets will be posted later today, but his Analytics Report is already available.\nMakinen's Week 8 NFL Betting Systems and Trends\nLooking for a Player Prop?\nVSiN has three tools to help you find an edge for tonight's Panthers-Packers game:\nBOLT Prop Picks — Find player prop selections.\nVSiN Player Prop Analyzer — Compare available player props and betting numbers.\nOpta AI Projections — See how statistical projections stack up against the market.\nAround the NFL\nLamar Jackson returned to full practice Wednesday ahead of Baltimore's matchup at Buffalo. The Bills opened as 3.5-point favorites, and the line is now Buffalo -3.\nNFL Week 8 Betting Hub: Picks, Odds and Previews\n🏈 How High Is Too High?\nOddsmakers are expecting fireworks in Thursday night's Florida Atlantic-North Texas game.\nThe total has reached 77 at Circa , the highest college football total of the season.\nThe game kicks off at 7:30 p.m. ET on ESPN, and Adam Burke breaks down the matchup, along with Troy at James Madison.\nIs a total this high justified by the offenses involved, or have bettors pushed the number too far?\nAdam's Thursday College Football Picks\nWeek 9 Betting Systems, Splits and Trends\nCollege Football Week 9 Betting Hub\nShare your picks. Got an opinion on a pro or college football game this weekend? Post it in the\nVSiN Community .\n⚾ Roll Out the Barrel\nMilwaukee finally got to celebrate Wednesday night.\nAfter Tampa Bay extended the World Series with a 12-inning comeback Tuesday, the Brewers finished the job with a 4-1 victory in Game 5 to capture their first World Series championship.\nMilwaukee entered the series as a -160 favorite.\nWilliam Contreras, who was +175 to win World Series MVP heading into Game 5, took home the award.\nAnother championship could be decided today. The Golden State Valkyries lead the Atlanta Dream 3-2 and can clinch the title on the road at 12:30 p.m. ET. Golden State is a 4.5-point underdog.\n🏇 A Familiar Horse, an Unfinished Grudge\nThe Breeders' Cup is Friday and Saturday at Keeneland, bringing 14 races that are frustratingly difficult to handicap.\nBut we're still going to give it our best shot over the next few days.\nSaturday's Classic features defending champion Forever Young, the 2-1 favorite in an eight-horse field.\nI still haven't recovered from loading up on Forever Young in the 2024 Kentucky Derby, only to watch him get knocked around in the stretch and finish third.\nOur horse racing handicapper, \"Mr. Ed\" Sehon, has studied the Classic field. And spoiler alert: He's not taking the chalk.\nMr. Ed's Breeders' Cup Classic Preview\nEd also has previews of Friday's Juvenile and Juvenile Fillies races.\nComplete Breeders' Cup Coverage\n📊 All of Makinen's Power Ratings in One Place\nWe've made it easier to find Steve Makinen's ratings across every sport.\nThe new VSiN Power Ratings Hub brings his sport-by-sport ratings together in one place, with links to the complete ratings and daily or weekly head-to-head matchups.\nYou can even sort the matchups to find the ones marked with stars, indicating potential value against the actual betting line.\nExplore the New Power Ratings Hub\n📘 DonBest College Basketball Rotation Book\nThe DonBest College Basketball Rotation Book is now available for just $4.99 .\nGet Your College Basketball Rotation Book\nSPONSORED\nDoc's Sports: Mr. Saturday Keeps Winning\nSTRIKE POINT SPORTS did it again last week, scoring a 7-Unit winner with West Virginia (+10.5) winning outright!\n\"Mr. Saturday\" went 3-1, +970 in college football last week, making it six winning college football weeks in the last eight.\nGet Your Free Trial With Strike Point Sports\nSPONSORED\n🏈 Why the Owner of Wunderdog Sports Turned Down Six Figures\nWhen I told Hewlett-Packard I was leaving, they offered me six figures to stay. I said no, and I've been making sports picks for a living since 2001.\nEvery one of the more than 89,000 picks I've released is still on my site, losses included.\nVSiN readers get a $50 credit toward my Pro Picks with just an email address.\nClaim Your $50 Credit\nRELATED ARTICLES MORE FROM AUTHOR\nPanthers vs. Packers Predictions: Week 8 Thursday Night Football odds, picks, and player props\nTuley's Takes: NFL Week 8\nNFL Top Plays Based on Betting Splits, Power Ratings and Trends – Week 8","revision_hash":null},{"source":"VSiN","source_type":"betting","url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/panthers-vs-packers-predictions-week-8-thursday-night-football-odds-picks-and-player-props/","canonical_url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/panthers-vs-packers-predictions-week-8-thursday-night-football-odds-picks-and-player-props/","url_hash":"4c5562a58c27f45ea3904324c46ba26a44852339166fc0a58f78610d8506a57e","content_hash":"ce53abb309863a53c1a18c7dd244651c4c9373f9485a3a472a4caf3e7a890bc5","title":"Panthers vs. Packers Predictions: Week 8 Thursday Night Football odds, picks, and player props","summary":"Week 8 begins with the Green Bay Packers hosting the Carolina Panthers for some Thursday Night Football. Keep reading for betting odds, picks, and player props for this exciting showdown. Also, make sure you head over to our Week 8 NFL Betting Hub for a look at all of our NFL betting content. MORE: Head [&#8230;] The post Panthers vs. Packers Predictions: Week 8 Thursday Night Football odds, picks, and player props appeared first on VSiN .","published_at":"2026-10-29T02:25:10.000Z","confidence":0.71,"author":"Zachary Cohen","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Home NFL Panthers vs. Packers Predictions: Week 8 Thursday Night Football odds, picks, and...\nAug 8, 2025; Charlotte, North Carolina, USA; Carolina Panthers quarterback Bryce Young (9) looks to pass in the first quarter at Bank of America Stadium. Mandatory Credit: Bob Donnan-Imagn Images\nX\nFacebook\nEmail\nWeek 8 begins with the Green Bay Packers hosting the Carolina Panthers for some Thursday Night Football. Keep reading for betting odds, picks, and player props for this exciting showdown. Also, make sure you head over to our Week 8 NFL Betting Hub for a look at all of our NFL betting content.\nMORE: Head to the Pro Picks page for best bets from all of our VSiN hosts and analysts!\nHow To Watch Panthers vs. Packers\nWhen: Thursday, October 29 at 8:20 pm ET\nWhere: Lambeau Field in Green Bay, Wisconsin\nChannel: Prime Video\nPanthers vs. Packers Odds\nOdds from DraftKings Sportsbook accurate as of Tuesday, October 27. Look around for the best prices!\nMoneyline: Packers -185, Panthers +154\nSpread: Packers -3.5 (-112), Panthers +3.5 (-108)\nTotal: Over 47.5 (-112), Under 47.5 (-108)\nPanthers vs. Packers Analysis\nIf not for a bad day at the office for kicker Trey Smack, Green Bay would likely be entering this week on a four-game winning streak. Instead, Detroit was able to snap the team's three-game winning streak, earning a 20-17 win as a 3.5-point home home favorite. The Packers will now look to rebound with a home game against the Panthers, and it's pretty clear that there's a strong expectation they will. Green Bay is a very popular bet to take care of business, according to our DraftKings betting splits , and it's pretty easy to see why.\nOver the last four weeks, the Packers have looked like one of the best teams in football. In that span, they're No. 2 in EPA/Play Allowed (-0.118), and it's their passing defense (-0.099 Dropback EPA/Play Allowed) setting the tone. Only four teams have been better against the pass than Green Bay over the last four weeks, and making opposing quarterbacks uncomfortable is huge given the pass-first nature of today's NFL.\nThe Packers are also playing well offensively, with their Dropback EPA/Play (0.217) being No. 7 in the league in this recent four-game stretch. Jordan Love has his inconsistencies, but he has done a good job spearheading this Los Angeles attack.\nThere's just a lot that Green Bay is doing well right now, and the public always takes notice when this iconic franchise is running good. However, when looking up all of these numbers for the Packers, do you know what stood out the most? The Panthers have a better statistical profile over the course of the entire season. Carolina also matches up well with Green Bay in several ways.\nOne thing that should help the Panthers is that the Packers are only 26th in the NFL in Pass Rush Win Rate (26). Well, Carolina is 31st in the NFL in Pass Block Win Rate (70%), meaning the team can struggle to keep Bryce Young upright. Well, perhaps that won't be a massive concern if the Packers defensive ends can't consistently get in the backfield.\nI'm also not sure Green Bay will be able to keep Chuba Hubbard from picking up big yards on early downs. He has been tough after contact this season, and there's a good chance he'll find some success in this game. We just saw Jahmyr Gibbs run 29 times against the Packers, wearing down their defensive line. Hubbard should now be able to pick on what's left.\nOn the other side of the ball, Carolina struggles against the run. But will that be a problem against a Green Bay team that hasn't gotten the ground game going? Also, how will a recently reshuffled Green Bay offensive line look against a Carolina defense which is eighth in the NFL in Pass Rush Win Rate (54%)?\nI just don't think this game will feature one-way traffic, and I like the way the Panthers have responded to home losses under Dave Canales. They're 8-2 against the spread when coming off a loss in Carolina under Canales, and they're also 4-0 both straight-up and ATS when coming off a loss as a favorite in that span.\nPanthers vs. Packers Player Props\nLEAN: Hubbard Anytime Touchdown (-120)\nI'm already playing quite a bit in this game, so I won't personally be adding anything on the player prop market. However, if you're looking for action there, I'd go with Hubbard to find the end zone. Only the Saints have given up more touchdowns to opposing running backs than the nine that the Packers have allowed. Hubbard had also scored three touchdowns in the previous two weeks before being held scoreless last week. Our OptaAI player prop projections also happen to have Hubbard rushing for 81.36 yards in this game. So, going Over 68.5 rushing yards is definitely a route you can go. However, if Hubbard does rush for at least 80 yards here, you can probably count on him to add a touchdown to that.\nPanthers vs. Packers Pick\nFading the Packers at Lambeau Field is always a bit risky, but most of the important numbers that are made available to the public suggest that there isn't a big gap between these teams. That makes it hard to pass on the points, and that's especially true with +4 available at one prominent book — and I wouldn't hesitate to grab the +3.5 either. I'm also going to sprinkle the moneyline, as Young has been a top-tier quarterback this year (fifth in PFF grade at 82.4). I'll take my chances with him late in a close game.\nBet: Panthers +4 (-110 - 1.5 units) & Panthers ML (+170 - 0.5 units)\nRELATED ARTICLES MORE FROM AUTHOR\nPanthers vs. Packers Week 8 Picks and Betting Systems\nTuley's Takes: NFL Week 8\nNFL Top Plays Based on Betting Splits, Power Ratings and Trends – Week 8","revision_hash":null},{"source":"VSiN","source_type":"betting","url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/tuleys-takes-for-nfl-week-8/","canonical_url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/tuleys-takes-for-nfl-week-8/","url_hash":"019651c03acb2a5681b7bea578dec94f0b7de8c4f109e49dc9a87ea608013ff6","content_hash":"b3bad8c891592605d94d446202a4b9482b39542791142bb9b8eaea4f67f31757","title":"Tuley&#8217;s Takes: NFL Week 8","summary":"Tuley&#8217;s Takes &#8211; NFL Week 8: This is one of the busiest weeks of the year in the Tuley’s Takes home office, with our regular NFL and CFB columns on Wednesday and Thursday, respectively, plus our annual horse racing columns on the two-day Breeders’ Cup Friday and Saturday. And longtime readers know our plate is [&#8230;] The post Tuley&#8217;s Takes: NFL Week 8 appeared first on VSiN .","published_at":"2026-10-29T02:20:00.000Z","confidence":0.71,"author":"Dave Tuley","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Home NFL Tuley's Takes: NFL Week 8\nCincinnati Bengals quarterback Joe Burrow (9) warms up before the first quarter of the NFL Week 7 game between the Baltimore Ravens and the Cincinnati Bengals at M&T Bank Stadium in Baltimore on Sunday, Oct. 25, 2026. The Ravens led 13-0 at halftime.\nX\nFacebook\nEmail\nTuley's Takes - NFL Week 8:\nThis is one of the busiest weeks of the year in the Tuley’s Takes home office, with our regular NFL and CFB columns on Wednesday and Thursday, respectively, plus our annual horse racing columns on the two-day Breeders’ Cup Friday and Saturday.\nAnd longtime readers know our plate is also full, as Halloween is a big deal at the Tuley Haunted Mansion, with annual traditions like decorations, pumpkin patches, haunted houses/mazes (Moapa Haunted Corn Maze was Tuesday night), parties, trick-or-treating, etc. Don’t get me started on how busy I used to be when the World Series of Poker held its “November Nine” Main Event final table that same week, but thankfully I’m not juggling that at this time of year anymore.\nAnyway, all of this monthly madness hasn’t hurt our handicapping as we went 3-2 ATS again with our NFL Best Bets here in Week 7 (and 3-1 ATS in CFB Week 8) to sit right around 60% for the season at 22-15-3 ATS (technically 59.5%) after a slow start.\nIn Week 7, we won with the Giants +10.5 in their 27-21 OT win at the Texans, Colts +6.5 in their 16-10 loss at the Vikings, and Packers +3.5 in their 20-17 loss at the Lions, with losses on the Saints +3.5 in their 16-10 loss to the Steelers in Paris and Eagles +4.5 in their 38-21 home loss to the Cowboys on Monday Night Football.\nEven though our 3-2 ATS mark wasn’t as good as in other recent weeks, we felt just as good about it, as favorites led 8-6 ATS in Week 8, so we outperformed the market and found the right plays with our “dog or pass” approach. On the season, my ViewFromVegas Consensus Closing Lines (tracked on Twitter/X at @ViewFromVegas ) have dogs leading 54-45-6 ATS (54.5%), so we’re also beating dogs in general by being selective.\nAs for our Tuley’s Teaser Portfolio, we had another winning week as our recommended plays (all advantage teasers including the key numbers of 3 and 7, aka “Wong Teasers” for the old-timers) went 3-1 with the Patriots +9, Buccaneers +9, and Titans +8 all winning their legs but unfortunately lost our anchor play on Sunday night with the Chiefs +9. As I wrote the last two weeks: Because of this success, we’ll keep pointing out our teaser plays, though we always stress to not only shop around for the best lines to tease (through the key numbers of 3 and 7) but also the lowest juice.\nEnough looking back (except to learn from our mistakes), let’s get to my “takes” on the full NFL Week 8 schedule, which again has just 14 games this weekend with the Giants, 49ers, Texans and Saints having their bye week. For the uninitiated here at Tuley’s Takes, I give my “take” on each game from my “dog or pass” point of view, trying to determine if the underdog is getting enough points to make them a play – or if I recommend passing on the game. I’ll also give my patent-pending Tuley’s Pool Play Percentages for those in contests where you have to pick every game (or just as another helpful handicapping point).\nCarolina at Green Bay (-3.5)\nBefore the season, this didn’t look like an attractive Thursday Night Football matchup, but the Panthers are in first place in the NFC South (albeit with a 3-3 record while the Packers are still in the Wild Card hunt at 4-3. The advance line for this game was Packers -3.5 and reopened at -4.5 on Sunday afternoon after the Panthers were blown out 43-13 by the Buccaneers and the Packers lost 20-17 at Detroit. However, the line has since been bet back down to 3.5, and I feel the money is on the right side. I like betting teams off a blowout loss as they’re obviously embarrassed and will make necessary adjustments on both sides of the ball. In addition, the Panthers have covered the last 13 times after an outright loss, so they’re used to bouncing back. It should be noted that primetime favorites went 3-0 ATS this past weekend after an underdog run of 12-0 ATS the prior four weeks, but hopefully the primetime dogs are barking again in Week 8.\nBest Bet: Panthers +3.5 (Pool Play Percentages: Panthers 67/33 in ATS contests, but Packers still 67/33 in SU pools; note: as I’ve written several times the last few weeks, these percentages basically meant that if these two teams were to play three times, the dog would win once and the fave would win twice but only cover once, hence the 67/33 splits).\nMinnesota at Detroit (-3.5)\nMoving to Sunday (and no early international games, hurray!), the advance line for this NFC North matchup was Lions -2.5 -120. After the Vikings beat the Colts 16-10 as 6.5-point favorites and the Lions beat the Packers 20-17 as 3.5-point favorites (both failed to cover by half a point), the Lions reopened -3 and have since been up to a consensus -3.5. Did bettors see Detroit RB Jahmyr Gibbs intentionally go down when the Packers were trying to let him score a TD and feel the Lions could have or should have covered? Personally, I see it the opposite way, in that it shows the Lions only care about winning and would do it again (note: this is another unspoken additional reason why I see more value in betting dogs overall). In addition, the Vikings are undefeated and mostly winning with their defense, but the offense might step up this week against the Lions’ No. 32-ranked defense (391 yards per game!).\nBest Bet: Vikings +3.5 (Pool Play Percentages: Vikings 67/33 in ATS contests, but Lion still 67/33 in SU pools – see TNF).\nLas Vegas at New York Jets (-1.5)\nThe Raiders started 3-0 but have come back to reality with four straight losses, and the countdown has started on when No. 1 overall draft pick Fernando Mendoza will take over at QB. For now, the Raiders believe Kirk Cousins gives them the best chance, so they’re sticking with him. They’re definitely taking a step down in class (to steal a horse racing phrase since it’s Breeders’ Cup Week) here after losing to the Chiefs, Patriots, Bills and Rams. Still, I’m not confident of a minor upset, so we’ll start our Tuley’s Teaser Portfolio here by moving the Raiders up to +7.5 with 6-point teasers and through the key numbers of 3 and 7.\nBest Bet: Raiders +7.5 in teasers (Pool Play Percentages: Raiders 55/45 in ATS contests, but Jets 60/40 in SU pools).\nArizona at Dallas (-6.5)\nI wrote about “Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde teams” last week (since I’ve been watching the classic story on Turner Classic Movies, including Bugs Bunny and Sylvester/Tweety versions, with Halloween approaching) and these two teams fit the bill. The line opened at Cowboys -5.5 last week before the Cardinals were blown out 30-16 by the Broncos and the Cowboys pulled away to beat the Eagles 38-21 on Monday night. However, the line has only increased to -6.5, which is too short for me to trust the Cardinals with a wager.\nBest Bet: Pass (Pool Play Percentages: Cardinals 55/45 in ATS contests on principle, but Cowboys 70/30 in SU pools).\nAtlanta at Tampa Bay (-2.5)\nThe Buccaneers lost their first five games but have to feel they’re back in the hunt in the weak NFC South after winning two straight and getting QB Baker Mayfield back. And I get why this line has gone from pick-’em to Bucs -2.5 as the Falcons have the fourth-worst pass defense. So, I can’t take the short number on Atlanta. However, the Falcons’ offense has shown signs of competence since Michael Penix Jr’s return, and this should be a one-score game as both teams try to catch the Panthers in the division, so we’ll add it to the Tuley’s Teaser Portfolio.\nBest Bet: Falcons +8.5 in teasers (Pool Play Percentages: Falcons 55/45 in ATS contests, but Buccaneers still 60/40 in SU pools).\nBaltimore at Buffalo (-3 -120)\nThis is one of Week 8's marquee games: the AFC East-leading Bills (5-1) host the Ravens (4-3), who are last in the AFC North but are expecting to get back QB Lamar Jackson, who practiced Wednesday. The advance line was Bills -3 but was raised to -3.5 on Sunday afternoon after the Ravens lost 35-13 to the Bengals, but that was with Tyler Huntley, and most reports were that Jackson would be back for this battle. The line has since dipped back to -3 at most books, though most are attaching -115 or -120. That’s too short for me to fade the Bills fresh off their bye, especially since I thought the line wasn’t high enough at 3.5 and didn’t bet it then either.\nBest Bet: Pass (Pool Play Percentages: Ravens 55/45 in ATS contests on principle, but Bills still 65/35 in SU pools).\nIndianapolis at Jacksonville (-10)\nThe advance line for this AFC South matchup was Jaguars -7.5. While the Jags were on a bye, the Colts lost 16-10 at the undefeated Vikings and covered as 6.5-point road dogs, and the line reopened at the same -7.5. However, in the last few days, there have been reports of a “fire sale” by the Colts (after firing GM Chris Ballard and trading G Quenton Nelson and DT DeForest Buckner with RB Jonathan Taylor, WR Josh Downs and WR Keenan Allen also being rumored on the trading block), and this line has steamed to double digits. I hear all that news, but I still believe the line has been overinflated and will gladly fade it with the remaining Colts players, as they still gave the Vikings a game and covered for us.\nBest Bet: Colts +10 (Pool Play Percentages: Colts 67/33 in ATS contests, but Jaguars still 80/20 in SU pools).\nTennessee at Cincinnati (-10.5)\nAnother double-digit dog, which plays right into our hands, as we’ve done well with dogs getting more than a TD all season. The advance line was Bengals -9.5, then moved to -10.5 after the Bengals routed the Ravens 35-13 and the Titans lost 27-24 to the Browns. Joe Burrow looked great in the second half with four TD passes, but let’s not forget the Bengals looked terrible in the first half as they trailed 13-0, and the Titans, despite winning only one game, have been competitive in most of their games and should be able to keep within one score to get us the cover.\nBest Bet: Titans +10.5 (Pool Play Percentages: Titans 67/33 in ATS contests, but Bengals still 90/10 in SU pools).\nCleveland at Pittsburgh (-3.5)\nHey, this game is for first place in the AFC North between the Browns (5-2) and Steelers (5-2), just like everyone expected at the start of the season, right? Well, we’re not even halfway through the regular season, so it’s no guarantee the winner will win the division come the New Year, but they’ll be in the driver’s seat. The Steelers are favored, but let’s remind everyone that teams coming off an international game in Europe without a bye week are 0-4 SU and ATS this season and 1-7 SU and 0-8 ATS since the start of last season (note: to be fair, the 49ers and Rams both won and covered in Week 2 after playing in Australia in their season-opener, but this is still a lot to overcome). Let’s also not forget that the Browns already beat the 27-24 in Week 4, so we know they can play with them. I’m not a big “revenge” handicapper, as I prefer to have the team that proved they could beat the other team, especially when we’re getting points in the rematch and, in this case, more than a FG.\nBest Bet: Browns +3.5 (Pool Play Percentages: Browns 67/33 in ATS contests, but Steelers 67/33 in SU pools).\nLos Angeles Chargers at Los Angeles Rams (-6.5)\nIt’s the battle of Los Angeles, though we all know who L.A.’s team is, even before the Chargers got off to an 0-6 start before their bye week. The Rams, the preseason Super Bowl favorites, have also been underperforming at 3-4, but they are coming off a convincing 35-21 win over the Raiders and trying to get back in the playoff hunt. This line was as high as Rams -7, but I wasn’t tempted to take the Chargers at that number and definitely dipping to 6.5 has me running away. Hard pass.\nBest Bet: Pass (Pool Play Percentages: Chargers 55/45 in ATS contests on principle, but Rams 75/25 in SU pools).\nKansas City (-1) at Denver\nThis is definitely the best game in Sunday’s afternoon slate with the AFC West-leading Chiefs (5-1) visiting the Broncos (5-2), and it’s a coin-flip in every way as the Chiefs were -1.5 on the advance line and it only got closer to pick-’em at -1 after the Broncos beat the Cardinals 20-16 and the Chiefs lost 20-3 to the Seahawks. I lean to the Chiefs here off the loss, but not going to lay even one point as it’s “dog or pass” and not “dog or make an exception for small chalk or pass.” This should be a one-score game, so I would consider teasing the Broncos up to +7.5 if the line goes back to 1.5, but otherwise pass.\nBest Bet: Pass (Pool Play Percentages: Chiefs 55/45 in all SU and ATS contests).\nNew England (-7) at Miami\nHere’s another underdog where I just couldn’t pull the trigger this week. The advance line was Patriots -7.5 and reopened there even though the Pats lost 30-24 at the Bears last Thursday and the Dolphins upset the Jets 28-25 on Sunday for their first win of the season. The spread has since been bet down to 7, but I wasn’t one of the early bettors as I felt the line was too short. And it doesn’t look like it’ll get back to 7.5 as several books are attaching -115 to the Dolphins at +7. Instead, I might add the Pats -1 to our Tuley’s Teaser Portfolio to mix a favorite in there.\nBest Bet: Pass, though maybe Patriots -1 in teasers (Pool Play Percentages: Dolphins 55/45 in ATS contests, higher at +7.5, but Patriots still 70/30 in SU pools).\nPhiladelphia at Washington (-6)\nWe usually get a good matchup on Sunday Night Football (helped by the fact the league flexes out late-season duds), but it’s too early for that, and we’re stuck with Eagles (2-5) at Commanders (1-4-1). My one regret last weekend was betting the Eagles +4.5 against the Cowboys on Monday Night Football, even with seeing their loooong injury report. The line for this game was Commanders -3.5 with them on a bye in Week 7 and has steamed to -6 after the Eagles blowout and further injury woes. I hope I don’t regret this, but I’m fading the move again with the Eagles as I don’t see how the Commanders should be favored by this much over anyone. It’s still a division rivalry, and I expect the Eagles to step up and at least get the cover. I keep going back to their leading the Cowboys 7-3 and 14-10 on MNF before the game got away from them in the second half.\nBest Bet: Eagles +6 (Pool Play Percentages: Eagles 60/40 in ATS contests, but Commanders still 67/33 in SU pools).\nChicago at Seattle (-3 -120)\nThe Bears come into this appealing MNF matchup at 5-2 and chasing the undefeated Vikings (6-0) in the NFC North, while the defending Super Bowl champion Seahawks are 4-3 and chasing the 49ers (6-1), who lost their first game on Sunday to leave the NFC West door open. This should be a primetime game with playoff-type intensity as both teams want to stay in their divisional races, plus this could be a wild-card tiebreaker. I lean toward the Bears plus the points, but +3 is too short for my liking. Several books have gone to -3 -120, so we might see a move to 3.5, which would probably get me to bet on the Bears, though I’m expecting to pass in the Circa Sports Million and the Westgate SuperContest if the contest lines are only 3. The stronger play to me looks to be to anchor my Tuley’s Teaser Portfolio with Bears +9, as this should be a one-score game with so much on the line.\nBest Bet: Bears +9 in teasers (Pool Play Percentages: Bears 55/45 in ATS contests, higher at +3.5, but Seahawks still 65/35 in SU pools).\nFor more Week 8 NFL best bets, visit the Week 8 NFL Betting Hub , exclusively on VSiN.com.\nRELATED ARTICLES MORE FROM AUTHOR\nPanthers vs. Packers Week 8 Picks and Betting Systems\nPanthers vs. Packers Predictions: Week 8 Thursday Night Football odds, picks, and player props\nNFL Top Plays Based on Betting Splits, Power Ratings and Trends – Week 8","revision_hash":null},{"source":"VSiN","source_type":"betting","url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/nfl-top-plays-based-on-betting-splits-power-ratings-and-trends-for-week-8/","canonical_url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/nfl-top-plays-based-on-betting-splits-power-ratings-and-trends-for-week-8/","url_hash":"d619c62b51c24aeba8aff82bf315e05a2cad6980ca51c0add7ad54b5971bc9a1","content_hash":"d5af40efa352ba7d69dc5d85e2ff3cf8330212d0ba934efbf6d2358ba72399bf","title":"NFL Top Plays Based on Betting Splits, Power Ratings and Trends – Week 8","summary":"Week 8 NFL Betting Trends: The following NFL betting trends are a collection of analytical data, betting systems and strength ratings featured on VSiN and qualified for the NFL games of Week 8. This report is meant to emulate the process that Steve Makinen and other members of the VSiN Analytics team undergo when handicapping [&#8230;] The post NFL Top Plays Based on Betting Splits, Power Ratings and Trends – Week 8 appeared first on VSiN .","published_at":"2026-10-29T02:16:00.000Z","confidence":0.71,"author":"Steve Makinen","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Home NFL NFL Top Plays Based on Betting Splits, Power Ratings and Trends –...\nOct 15, 2026; Denver, Colorado, USA; Denver Broncos quarterback Bo Nix (10) looks to throw in the second half against the Seattle Seahawks at Empower Field at Mile High. Mandatory Credit: Ron Chenoy-Imagn Images\nX\nFacebook\nEmail\nWeek 8 NFL Betting Trends:\nThe following NFL betting trends are a collection of analytical data, betting systems and strength ratings featured on VSiN and qualified for the NFL games of Week 8. This report is meant to emulate the process that Steve Makinen and other members of the VSiN Analytics team undergo when handicapping each week’s NFL board.\nAJ’s Angles\nThese are the top NFL betting trends and systems for this week’s NFL games, handpicked by VSiN Analyst AJ Makinen.\n* Play on any team heading into their bye week when facing a divisional opponent, assuming the opponent is not in the same situation. (Record: 58-28-1 ATS since 2013, 67.4%, +27.3 Units, 31.7% ROI, Grade 72)\nSystem Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH (-3.5 vs CLE)\n* Teams that lost their last game SU but covered ATS have not been good bets as favorites in their next contest, going just 50-47 SU and 34-63 ATS (35.1%) since the start of the 2019 season (including 20-19 SU but 9-30 ATS (23.1%) in divisional play in that same time frame).\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR), WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\n* Home teams have dominated in the Ravens-Bills series, going 11-3 SU and 12-2 ATS since 1999\nTrend Match (PLAY): BUFFALO (-3 vs BAL)\n* Teams that scored poorly ( = 10 points) in their previous game loss have been phenomenal as divisional underdogs in the next contest, going 38-67 SU but 67-35-3 ATS (65.7%) since the start of the 2020 season.\nSystem Match (PLAY): INDIANAPOLIS (+10 at JAX)\nNFL Streaks Betting System #18: Low-scoring ( 22 PPG) NFL teams coming off back-to-back SU wins have been terrible as small underdogs (+3 or less) in the next game, going 15-46-1 SU and 16-43-3 ATS (27.1%) since the start of the 2015 season.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): MINNESOTA (+3 at DET), DENVER (+1.5 vs KC)\n* TAMPA BAY's Baker Mayfield is 17-14 SU but 7-24 ATS as a home favorite since 2020\nTrend Match (FADE): TAMPA BAY (-2.5 vs ATL)\n* Won/lost records have mattered on Monday Night Football, as teams with the better record are 53-45 SU but just 39-57-2 ATS (40.6%) in the last 98 MNF games not matching teams with identical records.\nSystem Match (FADE): CHICAGO (+3 at SEA)\n#1 UNDERPRICED FAVORITE according to the MAKINEN POWER RATINGS: CINCINNATI -10 vs TEN (projections have line at CIN -14.9)\nTeam/Coach/QB Specific Situational NFL Betting Trends\nThese are some of the top situational NFL betting trends that have developed with teams in recent years of action:\n(109) CAROLINA (3-3) at (110) GREEN BAY (4-3)\n* CAROLINA is 27-36 ATS (42.9%) in non-divisional conference games since 2018\nTrend Match (FADE): CAROLINA (+3.5 at GB)\n* GREEN BAY is 96-24 SU and 74-44 ATS as a home favorite since 2009\n* GREEN BAY's Matt Lafleur is 27-19-1 SU but 17-30 ATS as a single-digit favorite since 2021\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY, 1 FADE of GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR)\n(239) MINNESOTA (6-0) at (240) DETROIT (4-2)\n* MINNESOTA boasts an impressive 90-62 SU and 95-56-1 ATS record when playing on normal rest (7 days) since 2011\n* MINNESOTA is 6-24 SU and 10-21 ATS as a divisional road underdog since 2010\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY, 1 FADE of MINNESOTA (+3 at DET)\n* MINNESOTA's Kevin O’Connell is 18-13 Over the total vs. teams with a winning record since 2022\nTrend Match (PLAY OVER): MIN-DET (o/u at 46.5)\n* DETROIT is 27-16-2 ATS (62.8%) at home since 2021\n* DETROIT is on a 23-16 SU and 24-14-1 ATS run vs. teams with a winning record\n* DETROIT's Jared Goff is 19-9 SU and 18-9-1 ATS in divisional games since 2021\nTrends Match (PLAY): DETROIT (-3 vs MIN)\n(241) LAS VEGAS (3-4) at (242) NY JETS (2-5)\n* LAS VEGAS is 42-58 ATS (42%) when coming off a SU loss since 2015\n* LAS VEGAS is 41-56 ATS (42.3%) in road/neutral games since 2015\nTrends Match (FADE): LAS VEGAS (+1.5 at NYJ)\n* NY JETS are on a 9-24 SU and 9-23 ATS skid when coming off an upset loss since 2011\n* NY JETS are 13-29 ATS (31%) as a favorite since 2017\nTrends Match (FADE): NY JETS (-1.5 vs LVR)\n(243) ARIZONA (2-5) at (244) DALLAS (3-4)\n* ARIZONA is 38-27 ATS (58.5%) in road/neutral games since 2019\n* ARIZONA is 38-30 ATS (55.9%) as an underdog since 2021\nTrends Match (PLAY): ARIZONA (+7 at DAL)\n* DALLAS is 32-14 SU and 28-18 ATS vs. teams with a losing record since 2020\n* DALLAS is 23-19 SU and 15-26 ATS when playing on short rest ( 7 days) since 2010\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY, 1 FADE of DALLAS (-7 vs ARI)\n(245) ATLANTA (3-4) at (246) TAMPA BAY (2-5)\n* ATLANTA is on 14-28 SU and 12-30 ATS skid on normal rest (7 days)\n* ATLANTA’s Kevin Stefanski is on 9-23 SU and 8-22 ATS slide when coming off an outright win\nTrends Match (FADE): ATLANTA (+2.5 at TB)\n* TAMPA BAY's Baker Mayfield is 17-14 SU but 7-24 ATS as a home favorite since 2020\n* TAMPA BAY is 39-62 ATS (38.6%) at home since 2014\n* TAMPA BAY is 39-60 ATS (39.4%) as a favorite since 2014\nTrends Match (FADE): TAMPA BAY (-2.5 vs ATL)\n* ATLANTA’s Kevin Stefanski is 20-13 Under the total vs. teams with a losing record since 2020\n* TAMPA BAY's Todd Bowles is 16-11 Over the total vs. teams with a better record since 2017\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY OVER, 1 PLAY UNDER in ATL-TB (o/u at 44.5)\n(247) BALTIMORE (4-3) at (248) BUFFALO (5-1)\n* BALTIMORE is 15-14 SU and 20-8 ATS vs. elite teams with winning percentages >=66.7% since 2020\n* BALTIMORE is 15-17 SU but 23-9 ATS as an underdog since 2018\n* BALTIMORE's Lamar Jackson is on runs of 9-5 SU and 8-4-1 ATS vs. elite offenses scoring >=27 PPG\n* BALTIMORE is 50-28-1 ATS (64.1%) in road/neutral games since 2017\nTrends Match (PLAY): BALTIMORE (+3 at BUF)\n* BUFFALO is 46-34 ATS (57.5%) in non-divisional conference games since 2017\nTrend Match (PLAY): BUFFALO (-3 vs BAL)\n(249) INDIANAPOLIS (2-5) at (250) JACKSONVILLE (4-2)\n* INDIANAPOLIS is 17-25 SU but 29-13 ATS vs. elite teams with point differentials of >=+4.5 PPG since 2015\n* INDIANAPOLIS is 26-27 SU and 38-14 ATS vs. elite defenses allowing 19 PPG since 2010\n* INDIANAPOLIS’s Daniel Jones is 18-23 SU but 24-18 ATS with his team coming off an outright loss since 2020\n* INDIANAPOLIS’s Daniel Jones is 1-6 SU and 0-7 ATS in the last seven following up a game in which his team scored =14 points\nTrends Match: 3 PLAYS, 1 FADE of INDIANAPOLIS (+10 at JAX)\n* JACKSONVILLE is 34-44 ATS (43.6%) when coming off SU loss since 2018\nTrend Match (FADE): JACKSONVILLE (-10 vs IND)\n* INDIANAPOLIS’s Daniel Jones is 36-18 Under the total as an underdog since 2020\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): JAX-IND (o/u at 46.5)\n(253) TENNESSEE (1-6) at (254) CINCINNATI (4-2)\n* TENNESSEE is 38-53-1 ATS (41.8%) in non-divisional conference games since 2014\n* TENNESSEE is on 11-48 SU and 17-41-1 ATS skid in Sunday games\n* TENNESSEE is 23-21 SU and 26-17 ATS when coming off a home loss since 2015\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY, 2 FADES of TENNESSEE (+10 at CIN)\n* CINCINNATI is 77-64 SU and 84-57 ATS when playing on normal rest (7 days) since 2012\n* CINCINNATI’s Joe Burrow is 23-12 SU and 24-11 ATS (68.6%) vs. non-divisional AFC foes. The average line was -1.1, Team average PF: 26.5\nTrends Match (PLAY): CINCINNATI (-10 vs TEN)\n* CINCINNATI's Joe Burrow is 15-10 Under the total versus non-divisional AFC foes since 2022\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): TEN-CIN (o/u at 46.5)\n(255) CLEVELAND (5-2) at (256) PITTSBURGH (5-2)\n* CLEVELAND is 27-41 ATS (39.7%) vs. divisional opponents since 2015\n* PITTSBURGH’s Aaron Rodgers is on a 10-1 SU and ATS run as a divisional home favorite\nTrends Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH (-3.5 vs CLE)\n* PITTSBURGH is 113-83 Under the total (57.7%) since 2015\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): CLE-PIT (o/u at 39.5)\n(257) LA CHARGERS (0-6) at (258) LA RAMS (3-4)\n* LA CHARGERS' Justin Herbert is 10-4 SU and 9-4-1 ATS with his team coming off a double-digit loss since 2021\n* LA RAMS' Sean McVay is just 13-16 SU and 9-18 ATS in its last 28 November games\nTrends Match (PLAY): LA CHARGERS (+6.5 at LAR)\n* LA CHARGERS are on 37-16 Under the total surge in Sunday games\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): LAC-LAR (o/u at 45.5)\n(259) KANSAS CITY (5-1) at (260) DENVER (5-2)\n* KANSAS CITY is 14-23-1 ATS (37.8%) vs. divisional opponents since 2020\n* KANSAS CITY is 58-47-1 ATS (55.2%) in road/neutral games since 2014\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY, 1 FADE of KANSAS CITY (-1.5 at DEN)\n* DENVER is 20-7 Under the total when coming off a double-digit victory since 2017\n* DENVER is 114-77 Under the total (59.7%) since 2015\nTrends Match (PLAY UNDER): KC-DEN (o/u at 40.5)\n(261) NEW ENGLAND (4-3) at (262) MIAMI (1-5)\n* MIAMI is 65-36 ATS (64.4%) at home since 2014\n* MIAMI is 41-25 ATS (62.1%) vs. divisional opponents since 2015\n* MIAMI is 59-48 ATS (55.1%) as an underdog since 2014\nTrends Match (PLAY): MIAMI (+7 vs NE)\n(263) PHILADELPHIA (2-5) at (264) WASHINGTON (1-4)\n* PHILADELPHIA is 15-21 SU and 9-25 ATS when coming off a divisional loss since 2012\n* PHILADELPHIA's Nick Sirianni is 16-5 SU but 6-14 ATS vs. poor teams, being outscored by 4.5 PPG or more since 2022\nTrends Match (FADE): PHILADELPHIA (+6 at WSH)\n* WASHINGTON is 26-42 ATS (38.2%) when coming off a SU loss since 2019\n* WASHINGTON is 21-36 ATS (36.8%) vs. divisional opponents since 2017\n* WASHINGTON's Dan Quinn is 13-9 SU and ATS vs. teams with a losing record since 2019\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY, 2 FADES of WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\n* PHILADELPHIA's Nick Sirianni is 17-6 Under the total in the last 23 games when coming off an outright loss\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): PHI-WSH (o/u at 40.5)\n(265) CHICAGO (5-2) at (266) SEATTLE (4-3)\n* CHICAGO is 36-50 ATS (41.9%) in road/neutral games since 2016\n* CHICAGO is 37-46-1 ATS (44.6%) as an underdog since 2019\nTrends Match (FADE): CHICAGO (+3 at SEA)\n* SEATTLE is 23-12 Over the total vs. teams with a better record since 2011\nTrend Match (PLAY OVER): CHI-SEA (o/u at 46.5)\nNFL Extreme Stats Next Game Systems\nThese systems search for extreme statistical performances in NFL games and detail the results of the follow-up game for these teams.\nBLOWOUT GAMES ARE RED FLAGS\nNFL teams that beat a point spread by 32 points or more in any given game have gone just 17-16 SU and 10-23 ATS (30.3%) when playing at home the next week since 2012.\nSystem Match (FADE): TAMPA BAY (-2.5 vs ATL)\nNFL teams that lose on a point spread by 30 points or more in any given game have rebounded nicely the next week when playing as road underdogs of 3 points or more, going 9-23-2 SU but 23-10-1 ATS (69.7%) in their last 34 tries.\nSystem Match (PLAY): CAROLINA (+3.5 at GB)\nCRAZY LOW-SCORING GAMES COMMAND ATTENTION\nTeams that scored poorly ( = 10 points) in their previous game loss have been phenomenal as divisional underdogs in the next contest, going 38-67 SU but 67-35-3 ATS (65.7%) since the start of the 2020 season.\nSystem Match (PLAY): INDIANAPOLIS (+10 at JAX)\n*WATCH FOR KANSAS CITY at DEN (-1.5 CURRENTLY)*\nCLOSE GAMES\nTeams that lost their last game SU but covered ATS have not been good bets as favorites in their next contest, going just 50-47 SU and 34-63 ATS (35.1%) since the start of the 2019 season (including 20-19 SU but 9-30 ATS (23.1%) in divisional play in that same time frame).\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR), WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\nTeams that just lost a heartbreaker ( = 3 points) to a divisional rival and are now playing in a less competitive game (>= +7 underdog or = -7 favorite) have had totals go Over at a 34-15 (69.4%) rate since the start of the 2017 season.\nSystem Match (PLAY OVER): IND-JAX (o/u at 46.5)\nHome teams coming off a high-scoring close win (>= 27 PF, =3 point differential) have been a strong fade candidate recently, going 79-66-1 SU but 54-86-6 ATS (38.6%) since 2016.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): BUFFALO (-3 vs BAL), MIAMI (+7 vs NE)\nNFL Team Strength Systems\nThe following handicapping information details betting systems for NFL teams based on various team strength indicators or line scenarios.\nNFL Team Strength Betting System #3:\nIn games between two teams with 35% or less winning percentages, and totals = 41, underdogs are 36-31 SU and 45-21-1 ATS (68.2%) since the start of the 2015 season.\nSystem Match (PLAY): PHILADELPHIA (+6 at WSH)\nNFL Team Strength Betting System #5:\nWith at least four games under their belt, favorites with a win percentage at least 25% worse than their opponent have a 36-43-2 SU and 28-51-2 ATS (35.4%) record since the start of the 2015 season.\nSystem Match (FADE): DETROIT (-3 vs MIN)\nNFL Team Strength Betting System #8:\nDefensively dominant road teams allowing less than 15 PPG have gone just 50-66-1 SU and 43-74 ATS (36.8%) since 2015.\nSystem Match (FADE): MINNESOTA (+3 at DET)\nNFL Team Strength Betting System #12:\nTeams that struggle to run the ball and are averaging 60 RYPG are 18-34 SU and 16-36 ATS (30.8%) at home since 2015.\nSystem Match (FADE): GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR)\nNFL Team Strength Betting System #13:\nRoad teams averaging 8.0 or more yards per pass attempt have been dangerous, 155-106 SU and 146-111-4 ATS (56.8%) since 2015.\nSystem Matches (PLAY ALL): BALTIMORE (+3 at BUF), NEW ENGLAND (-7 at MIA)\nNFL Team Strength Betting System #14:\nTeams playing with a point differential of 7 points or worse on the season as home favorites are 62-62-1 SU and 48-74-3 ATS (39.3%) since 2016.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): NY JETS (-1.5 vs LVR), WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\nNFL Team Strength Betting System #17:\nOddsmakers set a pretty good path for whether real bad teams have a chance to compete: those with -10 PPG differentials are 117-121 SU but 143-91-4 ATS (61.1%) as long as they are not a TD underdog or bigger (+7 or more) in the last 238 games.\nSystem Match (PLAY): LA CHARGERS (+6.5 at LAR)\nTNF, SNF, and MNF Team Trends and Systems for the NFL\nThe following trends and systems come from a log of all the Thursday night (TNF), Sunday night (SNF), and Monday night (MNF) games since the start of the 2019 season. Only Thursday night games were included in the TNF study, not the day games played on Thanksgiving. The Sunday night games only included those games played on Sunday night, not all of the games covered by the NBC SNF crew, which also included some Wednesday and Saturday contests. The games analyzed were only regular season games.\nTHURSDAY NIGHT FOOTBALL\n- There has been some interesting data regarding the first and second half of the season in terms of Thursday night games. In the first half of the season, or Weeks 1-8, home teams have gone 34-26 SU but 23-35-2 ATS (39.7%) in the last 60. Going back even further, since 2016, TNF home teams in Weeks 9 and later are 49-31 SU and 46-31-3 ATS (59.7%).\nSystem Match (FADE): GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR)\n- There has been a wild trend that has developed over the last 4+ seasons regarding TNF road teams coming off a home loss the prior Sunday, as they have rebounded incredibly with a 26-25 SU and 32-18-1 ATS (64%) record.\nSystem Match (PLAY): CAROLINA (+3.5 at GB)\n- Unfortunately, home cooking has not solved the ills for Thursday home teams coming off a loss in their most recent game, as they have been a brutal bet over the last five seasons, going 31-36 SU and 28-38-1 ATS (42.4%).\nSystem Match (FADE): GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR)\nTNF Team Trends\nCarolina 3-7 SU and ATS since 2014\nGreen Bay 8-6 SU and 8-4-2 ATS in the last 14\nTrends Match (PLAY): GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR)\nSUNDAY NIGHT FOOTBALL\n- Home favorites of less than a TD on SNF have historically been solid, going 63-46-2 ATS (57.8%) in their last 111.\nSystem Match (PLAY): WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\n- Home field advantage has been big in divisional SNF games of late, with hosts owning a 22-13 SU and 20-14-1 ATS (58.8%) record since 2019.\nSystem Match (PLAY): WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\n-  Momentum has been big for hosts overall, as home teams on SNF coming off a loss in their last games are just 19-27-1 SU and 21-25-1 ATS (45.7%) in their last 47, but those coming off a win are on a current 35-12 SU and 27-20 ATS (57.4%) surge.\nSystem Match (FADE): WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\nSNF Team Trend\nPhiladelphia 7-2 SU and 7-1-1 ATS in the last nine\nTrend Match (PLAY): PHILADELPHIA (+6 at WSH)\nMONDAY NIGHT FOOTBALL\n- In non-divisional conference matchups on MNF, hosts are on an 29-23 SU and 32-20 ATS (61.5%) surge since 2019.\nSystem Match (PLAY): SEATTLE (-3 vs CHI)\n- Won/lost records have mattered on MNF, as teams with the better record are 53-45 SU but just 39-57-2 ATS (40.6%) in the L98 MNF games not matching teams with identical records.\nSystem Match (FADE): CHICAGO (+3 at SEA)\nMNF Team Trend\nChicago 11-5-1 Under in the last 17\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): CHI-SEA (o/u at 46.5)\nIf you’ve picked up from each of the team trends sections that certain teams are consistently doing well or poorly, or are going Over or Under regularly, you’re right. Here are some overall primetime game trends that you’re going to want to consider:\nGood PRIMETIME (TNF, SNF, and MNF) Team Trend\nGreen Bay 21-10-1 SU and 22-9-1 ATS in the last 32\nTrend Match (PLAY): GREEN BAY (-3.5 vs CAR)\nBad PRIMETIME (TNF, SNF, and MNF) Team Trends\nCarolina 8-15 SU and 8-14-1 ATS in the last 23 primetime games\nTrend Match (FADE): CAROLINA (+3.5 at GB)\nChicago 7-15 SU and 10-12 ATS in the last 22\nTrend Match (FADE): CHICAGO (+3 at SEA)\nWashington 14-28 SU and 15-26-1 ATS in primetime since 2013\nTrend Match (FADE): WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\nUnder the total PRIMETIME (TNF, SNF, and MNF) Team Trend\nSeattle 14-8 Under in the last 22\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): CHI-SEA (o/u at 46.5)\nNFL Streaks Provide Some Advantages for Bettors\nThe following betting systems focus on winning and losing streaks. Below are the ones that have qualifying plays for this week’s action.\nNFL Streaks Betting System #4: NFL teams that have won their last three games ATS with a point margin of +10 or less in that stretch have gone just 18-51 SU and 19-46-4 ATS (29.2%) in game #4 since 2003.\nSystem Match (FADE): MIAMI (+7 vs NE)\nNFL Streaks Betting System #18: Low-scoring ( 22 PPG) NFL teams coming off back-to-back SU wins have been terrible as small underdogs (+3 or less) in the next game, going 15-46-1 SU and 16-43-3 ATS (27.1%) since the start of the 2015 season.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): MINNESOTA (+3 at DET), DENVER (+1.5 vs KC)\n*WATCH FOR CLEVELAND at PIT (+3.5 CURRENTLY)*\nPre-Bye-Week Systems and Trends\nThe following systems and trends are from the long-running article series detailing pre-bye week performance in the NFL. These records are from only in-season bye weeks and do not include playoffs or preseason.\nPre-bye week system #1:\nPlay on any team heading into their bye week when facing a divisional opponent, assuming the opponent is not in the same situation. (Record: 58-28-1 ATS since 2013, 67.4%, +27.3 Units, 31.7% ROI, Grade 72)\nSystem Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH (-3.5 vs CLE)\nPre-bye week system #2:\nPlay Under the total on any team heading into their bye week when facing a divisional opponent, assuming opponent is not in the same situation. (Record: 41-18-2 since 2013, 69.5%, +21.2 Units, 35.9% ROI, Grade 72)\nSystem Match (PLAY UNDER): CLE-PIT (o/u at 39.5)\nPre-bye week system #4\nPlay on home teams in their pre-bye week game when it comes Week 8 or later on the NFL annual schedule. (Record: 79-41-2 ATS since 2010, 65.8%, +33.9 Units, 28.3% ROI, Grade 68)\nSystem Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH (-3.5 vs CLE)\nPre-bye week system #9\nPlay against any teams heading into their bye week and playing as underdogs of more than 7 points (Record: 48-9 SU and 37-19-1 ATS since 2008, 66.1%, +16.1 Units, 28.8% ROI, Grade 67)\nSystem Match (FADE): TENNESSEE (+10 at CIN)\n* Please note that the systems above and all of the following trends only include bye week games from the regular season schedule, not playoffs.\nPittsburgh Steelers Pre-Bye week game: 11/1 vs. CLEVELAND\n· Pittsburgh is on an 8-1 SU and 7-2 ATS run overall in pre-bye week games\n·The Steelers have won their L4 pre-bye week divisional games SU and ATS\nTrends Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH (-3.5 vs CLE)\nTennessee Titans Pre-Bye week game: 11/1 at CINCINNATI\n· Titans are 6-2 ATS in L8 pre-bye week games as underdogs\n· Tennessee has gone 4-8 ATS in its L12 pre-bye week road/neutral contests\nTrends Match: 1 PLAY, 1 FADE of TENNESSEE (+10 at CIN)\nPost Bye-Week Trends and Systems\nThe following systems and trends are from the long-running article series detailing pre- and post-bye week performance in the NFL. These records are from only in-season bye weeks and do not include playoffs or preseason.\nPost-bye week system #5:\nPlay against double-digit favorites coming off their bye week. (Record: 19-10-1 ATS since 2014, 65.5%, +8.1 Units, 27.9% ROI, Grade 60)\nSystem Match (FADE): JACKSONVILLE (-10 vs IND)\nPost-bye week system #7:\nPlay Under the total with road teams coming off their bye week (Record: 47-28-1 since 2021, 62.7%, +16.2 Units, 21.6% ROI, Grade 60)\nSystem Match (PLAY UNDER): LAC-LAR (o/u at 45.5)\nPost-bye week system #8:\nPlay against teams coming off their bye week after a loss to a divisional opponent prior to the bye. (Record: 26-19 SU and 28-14-3 ATS since 2008, 66.7%, +12.6 Units, 30% ROI, Grade 62)\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): JACKSONVILLE (-10 vs IND), LA CHARGERS (+6.5 at LAR)\nPost-bye week system #9:\nPlay Under the total in games where a team is coming out of its bye week after losing in upset fashion before the bye. (Record: 34-19-1 Under since 1992, 64.1%, +13.2 Units, 24.9% ROI, Grade 60)\nSystem Match (PLAY UNDER): IND-JAX (o/u at 46.5)\n** Please note that the systems above and all of the following trends only include bye week games from the regular season schedule, not playoffs.\nBuffalo Bills Post-Bye week game: 11/1 vs. BALTIMORE\n·  Buffalo is on a 11-0 SU and 8-2-1 ATS run in post-bye week games, and is 22-10-2 ATS dating back to 1993\nTrend Match (PLAY): BUFFALO (-3 vs BAL)\n· The Bills are on a 4-0 Under the total run in post-bye week home games, allowing just 13.8 PPG\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): BAL-BUF (o/u at 54.5)\nJacksonville Jaguars Post-Bye week game: 11/1 vs. INDIANAPOLIS\n· Jacksonville has lost its last five post-bye week divisional games, going 2-2-1 ATS\n· The Jaguars are 5-1 ATS in their last six post-bye week home games T\nrends Match: 1 PLAY, 1 FADE of JACKSONVILLE (-10 vs IND)\nLos Angeles Chargers Post-Bye week game: 11/1 at LA RAMS\n·  The Chargers have gone 4-2 SU and 5-1 ATS in their last six post-bye week road contests\nTrend Match (PLAY): LA CHARGERS (+6.5 at LAR)\n·  The Chargers on 3-0 Under the total streak in post-bye week games versus NFC foes\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): LAC-LAR (o/u at 45.5)\nWashington Commanders Post-Bye week game: 11/1 vs. PHILADELPHIA\n·  Washington is just 5-13 SU and 4-14 ATS in its last 18 post-bye week games\nTrend Match (FADE): WASHINGTON (-6 vs PHI)\n·  The Commanders are on 1-6 SU and ATS skid in post-bye week divisional games, and 4-0-1 Under the total run in such games as well\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): PHI-WSH (o/u at 40.5)\nHandicapping NFL Rematch Games\nThe following trends and betting systems come from the same-season rematch data over the last 15 seasons\nWorst NFL rematch teams lately\n-  Cleveland: lengthy 12-30-1 ATS rematch skid L43\nTrend Match (FADE): CLEVELAND (+3.5 at PIT)\n-  Denver: 10-17 SU and 11-16 ATS L27 tries\nTrend Match (FADE): DENVER (+1.5 vs KC)\n-  Philadelphia: just 11-14 SU and 8-16-1 ATS L25 rematch games\nTrend Match (FADE): PHILADELPHIA (+5.5 at WSH)\nWorst NFL home rematch teams lately\nWashington: 2-12 SU and 4-10 ATS L14 at home\nTrend Match (FADE): WASHINGTON (-5.5 vs PHI)\nRematch Betting System\nTeams that won by 21 or more points in the opening game between teams are 93-29 SU and 75-47 ATS (61.5%) in the rematch\nSystem Match (PLAY): KANSAS CITY (-1.5 at DEN)\nTop Head-to-Head Series NFL Betting Trends\nThese are the top head-to-head series NFL betting trends between teams from recent years’ action:\n(109) CAROLINA at (110) GREEN BAY\n* CAROLINA is 4-5 SU but 7-2 ATS in the last nine meetings with Green Bay\nTrend Match (PLAY): CAROLINA (+3.5 at GB)\n(239) MINNESOTA at (240) DETROIT\n* Over the total is 6-1 in the last seven of the Vikings-Lions divisional rivalry at Ford Field\nTrend Match (PLAY OVER): MIN-DET (o/u at 46.5)\n(241) LAS VEGAS at (242) NY JETS\n* Home teams are 11-3 SU and 11-2-1 ATS in the Raiders-Jets set since 2003\nTrend Match (PLAY): NY JETS (-1.5 vs LVR)\n(243) ARIZONA at (244) DALLAS\n* ARIZONA is 8-1 SU and ATS in their last nine matchups with Dallas, including three outright wins as +6.5 or longer underdogs\nTrend Match (PLAY): ARIZONA (+7 at DAL)\n(245) ATLANTA at (246) TAMPA BAY\n* ATLANTA is 5-3 SU and 6-2 ATS versus divisional foe Tampa Bay in the last four seasons\nTrend Match (PLAY): ATLANTA (+2.5 at TB)\n(247) BALTIMORE at (248) BUFFALO\n* Home teams have controlled in Ravens-Bills series, going 11-3 SU and 12-2 ATS since 1999\nTrend Match (PLAY): BUFFALO (-3 vs BAL)\n(249) INDIANAPOLIS at (250) JACKSONVILLE\n* JACKSONVILLE has dominated Indianapolis historically, sporting a 14-8 SU and 18-3-1 ATS record in their last 22 meetings\nTrend Match (PLAY): JACKSONVILLE (-10 vs IND)\n(253) TENNESSEE at (254) CINCINNATI\n* CINCINNATI is 8-3 SU and 9-2 ATS in the last 11 games versus Tennessee\nTrend Match (PLAY): CINCINNATI (-10 vs TEN)\n(255) CLEVELAND at (256) PITTSBURGH\n* Home teams are 15-2-1 SU and 15-3 ATS in the Browns-Steelers AFC North rivalry since the start of the 2018 season\nTrend Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH (-3.5 vs CLE)\n(257) LA CHARGERS at (258) LA RAMS\n* Over the total is 6-2 in the Chargers-Rams set since 1994\nTrend Match (PLAY OVER): LAC-LAR (o/u at 45.5)\n(259) KANSAS CITY at (260) DENVER\n* Home teams are 8-3 SU and 9-2 ATS in the last 11 of the Chiefs-Broncos divisional rivalry\nTrend Match (PLAY): DENVER (+1.5 vs KC)\n* Under the total has converted in seven straight of the series as well\nTrend Match (PLAY UNDER): KC-DEN (o/u at 40.5)\n(261) NEW ENGLAND at (262) MIAMI\n* Favorites are on 7-1 SU and 6-2 ATS surge in the Patriots-Dolphins set\nTrend Match (PLAY): NEW ENGLAND (-7 at MIA)\n(263) PHILADELPHIA at (264) WASHINGTON\n* Over the total is 8-1 in the last nine of the Eagles-Commanders divisional rivalry\nTrend Match (PLAY OVER): PHI-WSH (o/u at 40.5)\n(265) CHICAGO at (266) SEATTLE\n* CHICAGO is 2-1 SU and 3-0 ATS in the last three of the series with Seattle\nTrend Match (PLAY): CHICAGO (+3 at SEA)\nNFL Rookie/Retread Coaching Systems\nThis material is from the VSiN piece entitled Analyzing the New NFL Head Coaches for 2026 detailing systems that apply to rookie coaches Mike LaFleur (Arizona), Jesse Minter (Baltimore), Joe Brady (Buffalo), Todd Monken (Cleveland), Klint Kubiak (Las Vegas), and Jeff Hafley (Miami) as well as re-tread coaches Kevin Stefanski (Atlanta), Mike McCarthy (Pittsburgh), and Robert Saleh (Tennessee).\nRookie Coach Systems\n( Games this week: BAL(+3)-BUF(-3), ARI(+7)-DAL, CLE(+3.5)-PIT, LVR(+1.5)-NYJ, NE-MIA(+7))\n-   Rookie head coaches have been far more proficient at covering point spreads on the road over the last decade. Here is the breakdown: Home games – 175-195-10 ATS (47.3%). Road/Neutral games – 202-181-7 ATS (52.7%).\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): BUFFALO, MIAMI\n-  As smaller favorites of -4 or fewer, rookie head coaches have gone 102-75 SU but 75-90-11 ATS (45.5%) over the last decade.\nSystem Match (FADE): BUFFALO\n-   Ironically, it's in the games where coaching figures to matter most (+1 to +3 small underdog lines) where rookie head coaches are able to hold their own best against the point spread. Their record in this line window over the last decade is 76-83-2 SU and 88-71-2 ATS (55.3%).\nSystem Matches (PLAY ALL): BALTIMORE, LAS VEGAS\n-  Since 2016, in games #1-#9 of their first seasons, they’ve combined to go 204-217-15 ATS, good for 48.5%. In games #10 and later, they’ve gone 173-159-2 ATS (52.1%). One special angle on this we find that rookie head coaches as small home favorites of -1 to -4 points in games #1-#9 are on a 15-25-2 ATS (37.5%) skid.\nSystem Match (FADE): BUFFALO\n-   Among the key challenges new head coaches face is stringing wins together and keeping the team galvanized after losses. Rookie head coaches have been better at the latter. When coming off of losses, rookie head coaches own a record of 108-117-2 ATS (48%) since December 2020. After wins, they’ve done reasonably worse in that same time frame, 76-91-6 ATS (45.5%).\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): BUFFALO, CLEVELAND, MIAMI\nRetread Coach Systems\n( Games this week: ATL(+2.5)-TB, TEN(+10)-CIN, CLE-PIT(-3.5) )\n-   Unlike the rookie head coaches, retread head coaches have been more proficient at covering point spreads at home since 2020. Here is the breakdown: Home games – 67-59 ATS (53.2%). Road/Neutral games – 65-65 ATS (50%).\nSystem Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH\n-  Retread head coaches have been brutal bets as favorites but respectable in the underdog role in their first seasons with new franchise. As favorites since 2015, they’ve gone 110-72 SU but just 74-97-11 ATS, for 43.3%! As dogs (or pick em), 93-191-1 SU and 142-137-6 ATS (50.9%).\nSystem Match (FADE): PITTSBURGH\n-  Since 2016, in games #1-#8 of their first seasons, they’ve combined to go 78-112 ATS (41.1%), while in weeks #9 and later, they’ve gone 97-86 ATS (53%).\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): ATLANTA, TENNESSEE, PITTSBURGH\n-  Since 2015, when coming off a win or tie, these coaches have posted a respectable 95-87 ATS (52.2%) record in their first seasons, including 45-36 ATS (55.6%) since mid-2022. When coming off a loss, the record has been an ugly 153-185 ATS (45.3%) in that same time span.\nSystem Match (FADE): TENNESSEE\n-  Retread coaches have been solid in revenge scenarios over the last decade, going 27-19 ATS (58.7%) when having lost an earlier season game against an opponent. This trend is on a 16-5 ATS run heading into 2026.\nSystem Match (PLAY): PITTSBURGH\nNFL Veteran Quarterback Leading New Team Systems\nThese systems take into account veteran quarterback records in their first season with a new team. They include game logs of different veteran QBs since 2004 who have played at least eight years in the NFL and started extensively on a previous team. This week, there are three different QBs finding themselves in a new place: Kirk Cousins (Las Vegas), Geno Smith (NY Jets), and Kyler Murray (Minnesota).\nNFL Veteran Quarterbacks Stats Betting System #5 – Veteran quarterbacks are trending extremely negatively on the road\nThe results since 2021 of veteran quarterbacks playing with their new teams on the road have been brutal, as they are just 32-58 SU and 37-52-1 ATS (41.6%).\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): LAS VEGAS (+1.5 at NYJ), MINNESOTA (+3 at DET)\nNFL Veteran Quarterbacks Stats Betting System #6 – By type of opponent, non-divisional conference matchups have been best for veteran starting quarterbacks in their first season with new teams\nSince 2005, veteran QBs in their first season with new teams have fared well against non-divisional conference opponents, going 95-82 SU and 98-77-2 ATS (56%).\nSystem Matches (PLAY ALL): LAS VEGAS (+1.5 at NYJ), NY JETS (-1.5 vs LVR)\nNFL Veteran Quarterbacks Stats Betting System #8 –Veteran QBs have shown an inability to strong win streaks together recently\nIn their last 76 starts with their new teams coming off outright victories, new incoming veteran QBs have gone just 38-38 SU and 33-42-1 ATS (44%). This trend dates back to 2021.\nSystem Match (FADE): MINNESOTA (+3 at DET)\nNFL Veteran Quarterbacks Stats Betting System #11 – Veteran quarterbacks are consistent bets as smaller road underdogs with new teams\nDating back to 2006, veteran starting quarterbacks in their first seasons with new teams have gone 41-36 SU and 51-26 ATS (66.2%) when playing as road underdogs of +5.5-points or fewer. The last 29 such games are 19-10 Under the total (65.5%) as well.\nSystem Match (PLAY): MINNESOTA (+3 at DET)\nSystem Match (PLAY UNDER): MIN-DET (o/u at 46.5)\nStrategies Using NFL DraftKings Betting Splits Data\nOne of the most touted features on the VSiN.com website, and a feature that we believe to be a fantastic resource for bettors, is the betting splits pages. These are the pages that we have built utilizing the data that DraftKings so graciously provides to us, detailing the breakdowns of the money and ticket splits for point spreads, money lines, and totals. In an article published in the 2026 VSiN NFL Betting Guide, Steve Makinen outlined 12 different systematic strategies for successfully using the DK Betting Splits Data that developed in the last three seasons. Here are the systems and qualifying plays for this week’s games as of 4:30 p.m. ET on Wednesday. These can and will change, so continue to track and qualify the systems up until kickoff for best usage.\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #1: Over the past two seasons, when more than 68% of the handle has been on a road side of an ATS wager, this majority group boasts a 74-52 ATS (58.7%) record for +16.8 units and an ROI of +13.3%!\nSystem Matches (PLAY ALL): CLEVELAND, LA CHARGERS\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #2: In NFL divisional games since the start of the 2022 season, DK majority handle bettors have been awful, as this majority group is just 225-274 ATS (45.1%) for -76.4 units.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): CLEVELAND, JACKSONVILLE, DETROIT, TAMPA BAY, NEW ENGLAND, KANSAS CITY, WASHINGTON\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #3: Similar to #2 above, in that same time span, when the majority number of bets staked its side in an NFL divisional game, this majority group is just 225-277 ATS (44.8%) for -79.7 units.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): CLEVELAND, DETROIT, ATLANTA, NEW ENGLAND, KANSAS CITY\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #4: In NFL non-conference games since the start of the 2023 season, DK majority handle groups have been quite sharp, going 139-113 ATS (55.2%) for +14.7 units.\nSystem Match (PLAY): LA RAMS\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #5: Since the start of the 2023 season, when the majority number of bets has backed a team in non-divisional conference tilts with smaller lines (6.5 points favorites or less), these groups have produced an outstanding 147-123 ATS (54.4%) record for +11.7 units.\nSystem Matches (PLAY ALL): GREEN BAY, BUFFALO, LAS VEGAS, SEATTLE\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #6: What is the definition of a “big public favorite” that savvy bettors should be willing to fade? Well, over the last three years, when a “supermajority” handle of 77% or higher got behind an NFL favored team of 6.5 points or more, these groups have gone just 15-28 ATS (34.9%) for -15.7 units and an ROI of -36.5%.\nSystem Match (FADE): JACKSONVILLE\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #7: When the majority handle and number of BETS have backed a team in an ATS wager in the higher-profile, non-Sunday afternoon games over the last three seasons, these majority groups are just 144-164 ATS (46.8%) and 142-163 ATS (46.6%), respectively. This set of games includes all the Wednesday, Thursday, Saturday, Sunday night (SNF), and Monday night contests.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): GREEN BAY, WASHINGTON, SEATTLE\nNFL DK Betting Splits system #8: Number of bets majority groups have been very sharp judging games when there is an exact one-game win difference between two teams in a matchup. The teams they have gotten behind boast an amazing 159-123 ATS (56.4%) record for +23.7 units over the last three seasons. The highlight of the one-win separation games has been when bettors back the road team, as these majority groups have gone 92-64 ATS for 59% and +21.6 units of profit.\nSystem Matches (PLAY ALL): GREEN BAY, ARIZONA, ATLANTA, BUFFALO, LAS VEGAS, SEATTLE\nAlternatively, when there is a difference of two or more wins in the standings, these majority number of bets groups have struggled to a 193-218 ATS (47%) mark.\nSystem Matches (FADE ALL): DETROIT, CINCINNATI, LA RAMS, NEW ENGLAND\nDK Betting Splits system #9: The average NFL total in 2023 was 43.0. Over the last two years, it ballooned back up to 44.8. In games where the totals reached 46.5 or higher and oddsmakers thus expected them to be a little more explosive, majority number of bettors have gauged these games incredibly well the last three years, going 179-137 ATS (56.6%)!\nSystem Matches (PLAY ALL): OVER – CAR-GB, BAL-BUF, TEN-CIN, ARI-DAL, MIN-DET, CHI-SEA\nUNDER – IND-JAX\nDK Betting Splits system #10: When 56% or more of the number of bets has been on the Under in an NFL game total over the last three seasons, this majority group has been quite sharp, 66-57 ATS (53.7%). This number for a “supermajority” in the NFL is quite low, evidence of how rarely the betting public bets the low side of a total.\nSystem Matches (PLAY UNDER ALL): IND-JAX, LAC-LAR, KC-DEN\nDK Betting Splits system #11: The magic mark for super majority on handle for betting Overs was 74% or higher, and this group performed miserably in 2023 and 2024 with a record of 84-107 (43.9%) for -33.7 units (20-18 for +0.2 units in 2026). To me, this has been a long-standing belief, but when the Oer looks too obvious, it usually loses.\nSystem Matches (PLAY UNDER ALL INSTEAD): BAL-BUF, LVR-NYJ, NE-MIA, CHI-SEA\nDK Betting Splits system #12 : Call this one the Over trap, but when a super-majority (>=64%) of handle has been on the Over, but DraftKings moved the opening total lower throughout the week, this majority group has lost regularly, going just 117-135 (46.4%) for -31.5 units over the past three seasons. Almost as if they were trying to bait more people into taking the Over.\nSystem Matches (PLAY UNDER ALL INSTEAD): TEN-CIN, ATL-TB, NE-MIA, CHI-SEA\nThis Week’s NFL Strength Ratings\nThe following NFL betting trends are taken from today’s MAKINEN DAILY RATINGS page under the NFL tab on VSiN.com. Listed by team, current line, and difference between rating and current line (in parentheses).\nThis week’s Top 5 UNDERPRICED UNDERDOGS according to the Makinen POWER RATINGS projections:\nRatings Matches: 1. DENVER +1.5 (+1.9)\n2(tie). LAS VEGAS +1.5 (+1.6)\nATLANTA +2.5 (+1.6)\n4(tie). INDIANAPOLIS +10 (+1.1)\nPHILADELPHIA +6 (+1.1)\nThis week’s Top 5 UNDERPRICED FAVORITES according to the Makinen POWER RATINGS projections :\nRatings Matches: 1. CINCINNATI -10 (+4.9)\n2. DALLAS -7 (+3.1)\n3(tie). GREEN BAY -3.5 (+2.1)\nPITTSBURGH -3.5 (+2.1)\n5. NEW ENGLAND -7 (+1.3)\nThis week’s Top 5 UNDERPRICED UNDERDOGS according to the Makinen EFFECTIVE STRENGTH RATINGS projections:\nRatings Matches: 1. MIAMI +7 (+2.0)\n2. CHICAGO +3 (+1.7)\n3. INDIANAPOLIS +10 (+1.0)\n4. LA CHARGERS +6.5 (+0.9)\n5. LAS VEGAS +1.5 (+0.8)\nThis week’s UNDERPRICED FAVORITES according to the Makinen EFFECTIVE STRENGTH RATINGS projections :\nRatings Matches: 1. BUFFALO -3 (+1.3)\n2. CINCINNATI -10 (+1.1)\n3. TAMPA BAY -2.5 (+0.6)\n4. WASHINGTON -6 (+0.5)\nThis week’s Top 5 BIGGEST TOTAL PROJECTIONS FAVORING OVER according to the Makinen EFFECTIVE STRENGTH RATINGS projections:\nRatings Matches: 1. PHI-WSH OVER 40.5 (+2.7)\n2. TEN-CIN OVER 46.5 (+1.6)\n3(tie). LVR-NYJ OVER 45.5 (+1.2)\nLAC-LAR OVER 45.5 (+1.2)\n5. KC-DEN OVER 40.5 (+1.1)\nThis week’s Top 5 BIGGEST TOTAL PROJECTIONS FAVORING UNDER according to the Makinen EFFECTIVE STRENGTH RATINGS projections:\nRatings Matches: 1. MIN-DET UNDER 46.5 (-2.7)\n2. ARI-DAL UNDER 54.5 (-2.6)\n3. ATL-TB UNDER 44.5 (-1.4)\n4. NE-MIA UNDER 43.5 (-1.0)\n5. CLE-PIT UNDER 39.5 (-0.9)\nThis week’s Top 5 UNDERPRICED UNDERDOGS according to the Makinen BETTORS RATINGS projections:\nRatings Matches: 1. INDIANAPOLIS +10 (+2.5)\n2. ATLANTA +2.5 (+2.0)\n3. DENVER +1.5 (+1.4)\n4(tie). CAROLINA +3.5 (+1.2)\nPHILADELPHIA +6 (+1.2)\nThis week’s Top 5 UNDERPRICED FAVORITES according to the Makinen BETTORS RATINGS projections :\nRatings Matches: 1. PITTSBURGH -3.5 (+4.1)\n2. CINCINNATI -10 (+3.5)\n3. DALLAS -7 (+3.1)\n4. NEW ENGLAND -7 (+1.0)\n5. LA RAMS -6.5 (+0.6)\nThis week’s Top 5 BIGGEST TOTAL PROJECTIONS FAVORING OVER according to the Makinen BETTORS RATINGS projections:\nRatings Matches: 1. KC-DEN OVER 40.5 (+1.4)\n2. CAR-GB OVER 47.5 (+1.0)\n3(tie). LVR-NYJ OVER 45.5 (+0.8)\nATL-TB OVER 44.5 (+0.8)\nCHI-SEA OVER 46.5 (+0.8)\nThis week’s TOTAL PROJECTIONS FAVORING UNDER according to the Makinen BETTORS RATINGS projections:\nRatings Matches: 1. MIN-DET UNDER 46.5 (-2.6)\n2. TEN-CIN UNDER 46.5 (-1.8)\n3. CLE-PIT UNDER 39.5 (-1.1)\n4. LAC-LAR UNDER 45.5 (-0.2)\nRELATED ARTICLES MORE FROM AUTHOR\nPanthers vs. Packers Week 8 Picks and Betting Systems\nPanthers vs. Packers Predictions: Week 8 Thursday Night Football odds, picks, and player props\nTuley's Takes: NFL Week 8","revision_hash":null},{"source":"VSiN","source_type":"betting","url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/expert-nfl-picks-week-8-best-bets-predictions-and-player-props-from-zachary-cohen/","canonical_url":"https://vsin.com/nfl/expert-nfl-picks-week-8-best-bets-predictions-and-player-props-from-zachary-cohen/","url_hash":"11b28f45f4c20ebf5983828d49631e71189c47952f11be9694f9871fb3d938fd","content_hash":"800fd9b1dc555346f2409809d76301246c75ec532ed97c4e1ab984e1fd86a083","title":"Expert NFL Picks: Week 8 best bets, predictions, and player props from Zachary Cohen","summary":"It&#8217;s time for Week 8 of the 2026 NFL season. I strongly suggest you check out the Week 8 NFL Betting Hub, where you&#8217;ll find all of the features and picks from my talented co-workers. On top of that, we never stop pumping out good NFL content on our live shows. That&#8217;s the beauty of [&#8230;] The post Expert NFL Picks: Week 8 best bets, predictions, and player props from Zachary Cohen appeared first on VSiN .","published_at":"2026-10-29T02:15:00.000Z","confidence":0.71,"author":"Zachary Cohen","captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":"Home NFL Expert NFL Picks: Week 8 best bets, predictions, and player props from...\nNov 2, 2025; Paradise, Nevada, USA; Las Vegas Raiders tight end Brock Bowers (89) celebrates after scoring a touchdown during the second half against the Jacksonville Jaguars at Allegiant Stadium. Mandatory Credit: Stephen R. Sylvanie-Imagn Images\nX\nFacebook\nEmail\nIt's time for Week 8 of the 2026 NFL season. I strongly suggest you check out the Week 8 NFL Betting Hub , where you'll find all of the features and picks from my talented co-workers. On top of that, we never stop pumping out good NFL content on our live shows . That's the beauty of being a subscriber. As a company, we're relentless in our effort to get you prepared for these games. With that out of the way, let's get into the fun stuff. Keep reading for my Week 8 NFL best bets and Week 8 NFL player props.\nMORE: Check out our Pro Picks page for NFL best bets from all of our analysts\nLas Vegas Raiders at New York Jets - 1:00 pm ET\nDidn't last week show us that New York probably shouldn't be favored against anyone? The Jets had a golden opportunity to pick up another win, as they were hosting a winless Dolphins team at MetLife Stadium. Miami ended up moving the ball at will in that game, scoring 28 points and picking up its first win of the year.\nThe Jets will now be hoping to turn things around against a cold Raiders team, but it's a Vegas squad which really isn't that bad. In fact, the Raiders are No. 15 in the NFL in EPA/Play (0.019) this season, Kirk Cousins is Pro Football Focus' 14th-ranked starter, and the team has the sport's ultimate weapon in Brock Bowers. Perhaps I'm oversimplifying things, but are we sure New York can be trusted to slow the passing game down? The Jets are 24th in the NFL in Dropback EPA/Play Allowed (0.141) this season.\nNaturally, a lot of what I just wrote can be applied to the Raiders. Las Vegas has been absolutely awful defensively this season. However, it's pretty clear that Klint Kubiak is a better head coach than Aaron Glenn. I also have way more faith in Cousins than I do Geno Smith. In what could be a close game, that's enough for me to take the plus-money odds.\nBet: Raiders ML (+105)\nMinnesota Vikings at Detroit Lions - 1:00 pm ET\nThis feels like an ideal matchup for T.J. Hockenson. I know the Vikings passing game has been miserable this season, but playing the Lions brings \"The Greatest Show on Turf\" out of everyone. Detroit is also especially bad against tight ends, ranking 32nd in TDs allowed, 32nd in receptions allowed, and 31st in aDOT allowed to the position. With that in mind, if Kyler Murray can comfortably see over the line in this game, he should see Hockenson with a whole lot of green around him. That said, I'm taking Hockenson to finish with at least 38 receiving yards, and I'm also playing him to score a touchdown.\nBet: Hockenson Over 37.5 Receiving Yards (-117) & Hockenson Anytime TD (+285 - 0.5 units)\nAdditional Week 8 Best Bets\nPanthers +4 (-110 - 1.5 unit) & Panthers ML (+170 - 0.5 units) vs. Packers - Check out my Thursday Night Football Preview !\nPARLAY: Browns Alt +8.5 vs. Steelers & Falcons Alt +8.5 vs. Buccaneers (-116 - 1.5 units)\nGunnar Helm Over 15.5 Receiving Yards (-114) vs. Bengals\nWeek 7 Picks\nTexans -9.5 (-122) vs. Giants\nBrowns ML (-120 - 2 units) vs. Titans\nBucky Irving Over 59.5 Rushing Yards (-122 - 1.5 units) & Anytime TD (+110 - 0.5 units)\nPatriots +3 (-105 - 1.5 units), Patriots ML (+138 - 0.5 units), Drake Maye Over 1.5 Passing TDs (-115) vs. Bears\nPARLAY: Vikings ML vs. Colts & Packers Alt +8.5 vs. Lions (-103 - 1.5 units)\nSeahawks -2.5 (-115) vs. Chiefs\nEagles +5 (-110) & Eagles ML (+190 - 0.5 units) vs. Cowboys\n2026 NFL Record: 40-39 (+9.20 units)\nRELATED ARTICLES MORE FROM AUTHOR\nPanthers vs. Packers Week 8 Picks and Betting Systems\nPanthers vs. Packers Predictions: Week 8 Thursday Night Football odds, picks, and player props\nTuley's Takes: NFL Week 8","revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/nflpicks2026_08early.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/nflpicks2026_08early.php","url_hash":"8e1fffa93ac21075ae3930af14b0b22d7b77b9bff08e43b5e010c9d9acfce465","content_hash":"b4472c65404c3c4760b91803c604b4abb8a71b1a6fcf3d90c937643b8c89bd96","title":"NFL Picks","summary":"Week 8 NFL Picks posted.","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:50:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/fantasyweeklyrankingsQB.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/fantasyweeklyrankingsQB.php","url_hash":"aa06ced2e7af4a7dfd243ead7a670392ceb5d880e3c56e237a8e86f09ab0b231","content_hash":"20b9203b6adeb142cf1639dddc6f67897b393dd29c9d24cd38bc02747db13170","title":"Week 8 Fantasy Football Rankings","summary":"Check out our Weekly Fantasy Football Rankings to see who you should start.","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:50:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/fantasy2026startsit.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/fantasy2026startsit.php","url_hash":"9731820214fd3a3d8299931bd608f02d3ae4c705646a708e35bc84f54824a2ea","content_hash":"a216b04212da293f1aa25d86440b7339918a0ce9935e5fae56e495554b50aa0e","title":"Fantasy Football: Start Em/Sit Em: Week 8","summary":"Fantasy Football Start Em/Sit Em for the upcoming week.","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:50:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/nfl-news","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/nfl-news","url_hash":"e8d0f5dd6d6fdf1dbe2b1028eaa7cdbaa646d47e75b11b17d744ee3da4bc9537","content_hash":"dd4fc395bf80965bf0338ed809fbd32c1b2795a6cd1503121a8b73468f27847a","title":"NFL News","summary":"The latest NFL news with our take on some of the news items.","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:50:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/confidencepool.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/confidencepool.php","url_hash":"6c0e132d7a655a524a52225f6aa5ccb02b98c3fb66d91ef1689d86e06d6d4558","content_hash":"035f4a7ec6dc441d6a5bcd5e49794353dcbe700db7ef861a5346ed403a984cb8","title":"NFL Confidence Pool Picks","summary":"NFL Confidence Pool picks for this week posted.","published_at":"2026-10-29T10:50:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/draft2027.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/draft2027.php","url_hash":"60ee12fd834d1b2c641e59f581245a9dc851ddfaad7909f4e5e4e2436d3cebf7","content_hash":"212a0b82dc6e3b9f88dc228ffeef9282b4efab49d4e07cab4804f34d061bdc21","title":"2027 NFL Mock Draft","summary":"2027 NFL Mock Draft updated today.","published_at":"2026-10-28T10:42:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/fantasyadddrop.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/fantasyadddrop.php","url_hash":"72682b7f51adf972de029e596ec8f5e1c4341e9952b9efb9dd35e7893b102cbf","content_hash":"ffff7bdbf7d0b5d8d0beb76dd4acb0542e42e85b4afce2ccd854e6c5ff942644","title":"Fantasy Football Add/Drop","summary":"Whom you should add or drop on your fantasy team after Week 7 of the NFL season.","published_at":"2026-10-27T10:48:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/nflreview.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/nflreview.php","url_hash":"dbc6522298f37589254bdd964ab262f4a4c792fe1d45558f98de17e49f06905c","content_hash":"7f0099019973e739e01c12b2d7b593ec97aba4509fe9a833762ad9024c718e66","title":"NFL Game Recaps: Week 7","summary":"Recap of the Week 7 NFL games here with fantasy football notes.","published_at":"2026-10-27T10:48:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Walter Football","source_type":"analytical","url":"http://walterfootball.com/nflpowerrankings.php","canonical_url":"http://walterfootball.com/nflpowerrankings.php","url_hash":"2440c823e269f714949ad11d9c769cfc73463f138d5b12227ae2ad15aa65d1b0","content_hash":"a48b5180e046af74680cb1900325babf0d61cd334b348f965d3965cbccc2b264","title":"NFL Power Rankings","summary":"NFL Power Rankings updated.","published_at":"2026-10-27T10:48:00.000Z","confidence":0.5,"author":null,"captured_at":"2026-10-29T14:59:12.476Z","body":null,"revision_hash":null},{"source":"Action Network","source_type":"betting","url":"https://www.actionnetwork.com/nfl/nfl-playoff-picture-week-8-afc-division-odds-futures-reset","canonical_url":"https://www.actionnetwork.com/nfl/nfl-playoff-picture-week-8-afc-division-odds-futures-reset","url_hash":"5f3d4cdd36022e1e1445b49d01e98ae55bc09d6b993e406f68a51bdef345ca37","content_hash":"ae60486dada73a0544996e1b0f15b9540238556a636aad7d4ca280e566fea133","title":"NFL Playoff Picture: Week 8 AFC Division Odds & Futures Reset","summary":"Turn your sports knowledge into winning\npredictions\n21+ or 18+ in Certain Locations. 19+ in ON. Please Play Responsibly. Gambling Problem? Call 1-800-GAMBLER. Visit connexontario.ca or Call 1-866-531-2600 in ON.\nNo Code Needed\nHome NFL\nNFL Playoff Picture: Week 8 AFC Division Odds & Futures Reset\nBrandon Anderson\nStaff Writer\nDownload App\nUpdated:\nOct 28, 2026, 12:00 PM EDT\nUpdated:\nOct 28, 2026, 12:00 PM EDT\n13 min read\nCredit: IMAGN IMAGES via Reuters Connect. Pictured: Zay Flowers.\nWe are seven weeks into the NFL season, and if the postseason started today, it would be quite the shocking playoff picture.\nLooking at the big picture in the AFC, you can cross out the Jets, Dolphins, Colts, Texans, Chargers, and Raiders from the contenders. That leaves 10 teams fighting for seven playoff sp","published_at":"2026-10-28T15:59:01.000Z","confidence":0.74,"author":"Brandon Anderson","captured_at":"2026-10-29T15:02:04.040Z","body":"Turn your sports knowledge into winning\npredictions\n21+ or 18+ in Certain Locations. 19+ in ON. Please Play Responsibly. Gambling Problem? Call 1-800-GAMBLER. Visit connexontario.ca or Call 1-866-531-2600 in ON.\nNo Code Needed\nHome NFL\nNFL Playoff Picture: Week 8 AFC Division Odds & Futures Reset\nBrandon Anderson\nStaff Writer\nDownload App\nUpdated:\nOct 28, 2026, 12:00 PM EDT\nUpdated:\nOct 28, 2026, 12:00 PM EDT\n13 min read\nCredit: IMAGN IMAGES via Reuters Connect. Pictured: Zay Flowers.\nWe are seven weeks into the NFL season, and if the postseason started today, it would be quite the shocking playoff picture.\nLooking at the big picture in the AFC, you can cross out the Jets, Dolphins, Colts, Texans, Chargers, and Raiders from the contenders. That leaves 10 teams fighting for seven playoff spots. Three of the divisions have clear favorites, but then there is the loaded AFC North.\nLet's reset the AFC playoff picture, division by division, and find the best futures value on the board.\nDownload the Action Network app now for more NBA picks and analysis! If you want more Action Network content, be sure to add us as a preferred source on Google .\nAFC Division & NFL Playoff Picture Reset\nPicks\nAFC North\nAFC West\nAFC South\nAFC East\nGive the Man His Flowers\nAFC North Deep Dive\nThe AFC North is the most competitive and interesting division in football right now. All four teams are over .500 for a second straight week, so let's dive into the deep end on all four teams.\nI'll make the case for how to invest in each of the four teams if you're looking for a ticket — even if it's not my preferred bet — and then give my final verdict on the division at the end, before we get to the other AFC divisions.\nBaltimore Ravens\nFor the second straight week, the Ravens blew a double-digit lead against a division rival and went completely scoreless in the second half.  They were up 13-0 at halftime against the Bengals , and it easily could have been 21-0 if they hadn't settled for field goals on 4th-and-1 at the 11-yard line and 4th-and-3 at the 6-yard line.\nInstead, Baltimore collapsed, going 0-for-2 on fourth downs, 0-for-3 in the red zone, and committing 10 penalties as the Bengals scored 35 unanswered to win with ease. The Ravens are the first team since 1950 to lose by 20+ points after leading by 13+ at halftime.\nThe Ravens now have a +65 point differential in the first half this season and a -70 differential in the second half. That 135-point swing is the largest through seven games this century. At this point, this is in their DNA. The coaching change didn't fix the constant wilting.\nRight now, this is not a playoff defense. Marlon Humphrey was embarrassed Sunday, the linebackers looked lost, and Baltimore can't generate any pressure.\nOn offense, the line had a rough day with Cam Jurgens at center, and I am starting to get genuinely concerned about Derrick Henry . He is getting hit in the backfield by run blitzes and lacks his usual acceleration.\nThe Ravens are now in last place in the division. They play in Buffalo on Sunday and then play Jacksonville on a short week for Thursday Night Football, and we don't even know if Lamar Jackson is playing this week, or what version we'll get.\nFTN has Baltimore's division odds down to 9%, but it is still priced at +225 (a 31% implied probability). That price is way off.\nThis team is far from a lock to even be a playoff team at this point.\nHow to bet Baltimore: Ravens to Miss the Playoffs at +198 (FanDuel)\nCincinnati Bengals\nThe Bengals were on the other side of that Baltimore collapse, rattling off 35 straight points.\nIn the first half, Cincinnati managed just 13 plays for 60 yards. In the second half? Five consecutive touchdown drives — 35 plays, 291 yards, and 8.3 yards per play. Joe Burrow went from -0.60 EPA/play and a 23% success rate in the first half to 1.18 EPA/play and an 89% success rate in the second half.\nWhile it still feels like the same old Bengals — relying on Burrow, Ja'Marr Chase , and Tee Higgins to overcome coaching flaws — the offensive line and defense have improved exactly like we hoped.\nThe Bengals are No. 2 in overall DVOA and rank in the top 10 across all three phases of the game. This is the first time they have been top three in DVOA for a full decade.\nLooking ahead, the Bengals likely only have two games left against playoff opponents. Their upcoming schedule features the Titans , Falcons , Steelers , Commanders , Saints , and Browns . There is a very real path to 9-3 or 10-2.\nFTN has them at an 88% probability to make the playoffs and 58% to win the division.\nI'm still not sold on the Bengals defense enough to need playoff futures, but I'm seeing value on Cincinnati to make the playoffs, win the division, and most other futures — but I prefer the high-end outcome.\nThis team has a real path to the 1- or 2-seed, which would put a Joe Burrow MVP ticket in play (+600) but I'll just bet the 1-seed outright.\nHow to bet Cincinnati: Bengals to be the AFC 1-Seed at 8% (+1150 at Polymarket)\nCleveland Browns\nHear me out: Cleveland's win on Sunday was actually pretty impressive.\nYes, the Browns only beat the terrible Titans by three, but Cleveland fell behind 14-3, suffered weird turnovers, doinked a late field goal, and still found a way to win the exact sort of game we'd typically expect a team like this to lose. The Browns dominated the underlying metrics, posting a 56% to 40% success rate advantage while holding Tennessee to 181 total yards.\nThe Browns are 5-2, despite their wins coming by margins of 4, 3, 3, 3, and 3 points. Could they be this year's version of last year's Broncos ?\nThe schedule gives them a massive opportunity. Up next for Cleveland is an older Pittsburgh team coming off a trip to France, and they still have winnable games against the Saints, Raiders , Falcons, Giants , and Colts . With five wins already, even winning four of those six puts Cleveland squarely in the playoff mix.\nMike Rutenberg's defense is the real deal, and Deshaun Watson keeps making just enough plays late.\nWatson just threw for his first 300-yard game in 2,120 days — he leads the NFL with five game-winning drives and three fourth-quarter comebacks. It's a gross pick, but if Watson is going to keep coming back, you might want to bet it.\nHow to bet Cleveland: Deshaun Watson for Comeback Player of the Year (+3000 at BetRivers)\nPittsburgh Steelers\nI'm not sold on this team at all.\nPittsburgh barely beat Cooper Rush and Jalon Daniels, and its only \"good\" win was a goofy turnover-luck game against Cincinnati.\nI do not buy the Steelers at all — they are totally fraudulent. Their top-10 DVOA rating is inflated by the terrible backup quarterbacks they've been fortunate to face.\nThis is not a top-10 team. Not even close.\nThe numbers, however, tell you to bet on them — DVOA gives them 25% division odds and a 67% chance to make the playoffs, which would mean serious value on their current market prices.\nBut I want nothing to do with it.\nThe Steelers' schedule is about to turn incredibly sour: home for Cleveland with no rest after France, then at Cincinnati, at Philadelphia, Denver, Houston, at Jacksonville, and Baltimore.\nIf you trust the metrics, Pittsburgh futures are a no brainer. I can't do it.\nHow to bet Pittsburgh: Steelers to Make Playoffs at 47% (Polymarket) or Division (+475 at Caesars)\nBrandon's AFC North Verdict\nBengals for AFC 1-Seed at 8% (+1150 at Polymarket)\nClick here to return to the table of contents.\nAFC West\nThe Chiefs finally took their first loss of the and looked completely lifeless in Seattle on Sunday Night Football. They put up three points, made no trips to the red zone, and barely scraped together 200 yards.\nHonestly, a loss that bad might have actually been a good thing — it highlights this offense has no weapons outside of Kenneth Walker . They need to get serious and trade for a wide receiver right now.\nMeanwhile the Broncos won, but I'm still not buying it. They looked ugly even in an easy win against the Cardinals , posting just a 37% success rate and relying on two fluky, long plays but otherwise managed just 263 yards on 54 plays.\nThe Broncos are 5-2 with four one-score wins. They profile more like a 3-4 or even 2-5 team… but those wins count either way.\nThis week is the big one: Chiefs -1.5 at Denver.\nRight now, this division is about 60-40 in favor of Kansas City. If the Chiefs win, it's over — they secure the sweep.\nBut if you like Denver to steal this game, its +170 division odds at DraftKings are a nice play as the upcoming schedule features a super soft stretch ( Panthers , Raiders, Steelers, Dolphins , Jets , Raiders).\nI am passing on the division, but I love a rookie angle here.\nYou immediately noticed the difference when Broncos running back Jonah Coleman checked into the game over J.K. Dobbins and RJ Harvey on Sunday. Coleman shows real burst and gives this team the explosive ability it sorely lacks.\nReturning from a short-term IR stint, Coleman immediately led the backfield in carry share (50%) and snaps on early downs, third downs, and short yardage. He led the team in RB snaps his last game in Week 2 as well.\nThe Offensive Rookie of the Year race is wide open, and 60-1 is an absurd number for a starting running back getting this kind of opportunity behind a great offensive line.\nVerdict: Jonah Coleman for Offensive Rookie of the Year (+6000 at BetMGM)\nClick here to return to the table of contents.\nAFC South\nThe Texans losing to the Giants in overtime was one of the most frustrating and shocking results of the entire year.\nYou let J.J. McCarthy come in for his first career road start and dice you up right after you had just righted your season against the Jaguars? An absolutely disgusting result across the board.\nHouston's offense managed just 237 yards and a 39% success rate. Finally armed with wide receivers, the Texans have no cohesive plan. Nico Collins has seen his target rate plummet from 29% in the first two games down to 19% over the last three. What are we doing?!\nDefensively was even worse. The Texans allowed 420 yards, 6.5 yards per play, and a 50% rushing success rate. The Giants hadn't ripped off a 20-yard run all season, then did so on back-to-back plays in overtime to win it. This was the third-worst EPA/play allowed in the DeMeco Ryans era, and four of the worst nine have all happened this season.\nIt's time to accept that this simply is not an elite defense right now.\nI downgraded Houston by a full win in my projections, dropping them from 55% to 34% to make the playoffs. This was a completely unacceptable performance by a team that should be in the top 10.\nWith the Colts and Titans DOA, this might just be a one-team division for the Jaguars.\nStill, Houston heads into a badly needed bye week and then faces the Chargers , Browns, and Colts. That soft stretch should get them to 5-5.\nThe Texans have the second-easiest remaining schedule by DVOA and can still win any game left on their slate.\nEven if you want to get back out later, this soft stretch leaves a chance to buy low on a team that should still win football games.\nVerdict: Texans Over 8.5 Wins (+134 at DraftKings)\nClick here to return to the table of contents.\nAFC East\nThere is not a ton of new information on this division entering Week 8.\nThe Bills were on bye and watched their odds increase thanks to the Patriots losing a winnable Thursday night game in Chicago.\nBuffalo is still over 50% for a top-two seed, a good setup for a Josh Allen MVP ticket, but I still don't believe in the defense enough to invest in playoff futures . New England looks a likely playoff team.\nBut the real value in this division might actually be on the Jets.\nYes, it was an ugly loss to Miami, but New York actually outperformed the Dolphins across the board. The Jets had more yards (377), better yards per play (7.1), a better success rate (52%), and a better explosive rate. Miami was rested off its bye and went 3-for-3 on fourth downs and 3-for-3 in the red zone to squeak out a 3-point win. It happens.\nThe Jets aren't a great team, but they aren't terrible. They rank between 19th and 22nd in DVOA across offense, defense, special teams, and overall. That is perfectly fine, reminiscent of the Steelers over the last few years. They have four one-score losses this year, and playing tight games against the Packers , Lions , and Patriots are actually good outcomes.\nThe Jets' remaining schedule is a favorable one. They host a reeling Raiders team this week, and they still play the Chargers, Dolphins, Cardinals, Broncos, and Vikings , plus a Week 18 matchup against a Buffalo team that could be resting starters.\nI have the Jets projected for 6.3 wins, so it's time to take advantage of a market overreaction.\nVerdict: Jets Over 5.5 Wins at 46% (+117 at Kalshi) | Jets Escalator Over 6.5 Wins at 27% (+270 at Polymarket)\nClick here to return to the table of contents.\nBonus: Zay Flowers Futures\nI have to include this before we wrap up: few players have impressed me more this season than Zay Flowers . New offensive coordinator Declan Doyle has unlocked an entirely new, insane version of this dude.\nFlowers is fifth in the NFL with 608 receiving yards  despite missing one full game and two halves due to injury ! For context, the four guys clustered around Flowers in yardage at 605-636 yards have played seven full games compared to his five. Only Jaxon Smith-Njigba is well out ahead of that group, but he can't perform like this all year.\nFlowers has actually played only 257 of the Ravens' 452 snaps this season (57%).\nEven more ridiculous, Flowers has only played 67 snaps with Lamar Jackson on the field, basically one game's worth. In those 67 snaps, Flowers has 16 catches for 353 yards and two touchdowns. That is a pace of about 235 yards per game. He is averaging an astronomical 9.1 yards per route run when sharing the field with Jackson.\nIf Flowers maintained that pace with Jackson over the remaining 10 games, he would put up another 2,350 yards and finish over 3,000 for the season. Ridiculous! That obviously isn't going to happen, but it highlights just how unbelievable his production has been.\nI have been looking for a way to invest in Flowers since Week 1, and this is a guy you want to find any way to snag in fantasy football. I'm buying low now before Jackson gets fully integrated back into the lineup.\nBET: Zay Flowers Receiving Yards Leader at 2% (+4900 at Kalshi/Polymarket) | Zay Flowers Offensive Player of the Year at 1% (+9900 at Kalshi/Polymarket)\nClick here to return to the table of contents.\nBrandon Anderson's Futures Bets Placed This Week\nBengals AFC 1-Seed at 8%: +1150 (Polymarket)\nTexans Over 8.5 Wins: +134 (DraftKings)\nJets Over 5.5 Wins at 46%: +117 (Kalshi)\nJets Over 6.5 Wins at 27%: +270 (Polymarket)\nJonah Coleman Offensive Rookie of the Year: +6000 (BetMGM)\nZay Flowers Receiving Yards Leader at 2%: +4900 (Kalshi/Polymarket)\nZay Flowers Offensive Player of the Year at 1%: +9900 (Kalshi/Polymarket)\nFree Guide: 10 Tips to Hit Bigger Same Game Parlays More Often\n10 real, data-backed strategies for SGP bettors. Just enter your email and we'll send it.\nAbout the Author\nBrandon Anderson is a staff writer at the Action Network, specializing in NFL and NBA coverage. He provides weekly NFL power rankings and picks for every game, as well as contributing to NBA analysis, regularly appearing on the BUCKETS Podcast. With a deep background in sports betting and fantasy football, Brandon is known for spotting long-shot futures and writing for various outlets like Sports Illustrated, BetMGM, and more befor