ic Betting Database for QBs, Coaches & Teams","summary":"Turn your sports knowledge into winning\npredictions\n21+ or 18+ in Certain Locations. 19+ in ON. Please Play Responsibly. Gambling Problem? Call 1-800-GAMBLER. Visit connexontario.ca or Call 1-866-531-2600 in ON.\nNo Code Needed\nHome NFL\nBookBias: The NFL Public Betting Database for QBs, Coaches & Teams\nEvan Abrams\nDirector of Research\nDownload App\nUpdated:\nOct 27, 2026, 05:31 PM EDT\nUpdated:\nOct 27, 2026, 05:31 PM EDT\n1 min read\nPRO\nCredit: Action Network.\nEvery NFL bet comes down to a side, and every side has a crowd. So who do bettors love most, and does it actually pay to ride with them?\nBookBias answers that for every NFL quarterback, head coach and team. It tracks against-the- spread results for 250+ QBs, 150+ coaches and all 32 teams, split two ways: betting with the public (the major","published_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:19.000Z","confidence":0.74,"author":"Evan Abrams","captured_at":"2026-10-29T15:02:04.040Z","body":"Turn your sports knowledge into winning\npredictions\n21+ or 18+ in Certain Locations. 19+ in ON. Please Play Responsibly. Gambling Problem? Call 1-800-GAMBLER. Visit connexontario.ca or Call 1-866-531-2600 in ON.\nNo Code Needed\nHome NFL\nBookBias: The NFL Public Betting Database for QBs, Coaches & Teams\nEvan Abrams\nDirector of Research\nDownload App\nUpdated:\nOct 27, 2026, 05:31 PM EDT\nUpdated:\nOct 27, 2026, 05:31 PM EDT\n1 min read\nPRO\nCredit: Action Network.\nEvery NFL bet comes down to a side, and every side has a crowd. So who do bettors love most, and does it actually pay to ride with them?\nBookBias answers that for every NFL quarterback, head coach and team. It tracks against-the- spread results for 250+ QBs, 150+ coaches and all 32 teams, split two ways: betting with the public (the majority side) or with the minority. And you can see it over five different windows.\nMajority ticket count is the QB, coach or team receiving 51% or more of the betting support against the spread. The minority count would be the flip side, receiving 49% or less. In BookBias, Public is the majority side.\nAn example: Cowboys at Chiefs with the Chiefs -3. The Chiefs are receiving 58% of the total tickets/bets on them to cover the spread. The Cowboys have 42%. Kansas City would be the public/majority side.\nStart with One Tab to see a single list, like QBs betting with the public since 2018, ranked by money won. Then sort by record, win rate, ROI or units to answer the question you're actually asking.\nCompare Tabs is where the tool earns its keep. Every name gets all four lists side by side, plus the gap between minority and public results in each window. That shows you exactly who the market overrates when everyone piles on, and who quietly cashes when nobody wants him.\nWant to settle a debate? Head to Head stacks any QBs, coaches or teams across all four lists so you can compare them line by line. Tap any name in any table to add it.\nDive into BookBias below.\nNFL Public Betting: BookBias\nTop Stories\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Prediction, Pick, Odds for NFL Thursday Night Football on October 29\nSean Koerner\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Anytime Touchdown Props for NFL Thursday Night Football\nGilles Gallant\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Player Props for Josh Jacobs and Savion Williams\nSam Farley\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Spread Prediction: Pros Betting This 57% ATS System\nPJ Walsh\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Playoff Picture: Week 8 AFC Division Odds & Futures Reset\nBrandon Anderson\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Week 8 Pick’em, Confidence Pool Picks, Projections, Ratings\nSean Koerner\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Betting Primer: Trends, Stats, Systems for Every Game\nEvan Abrams\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Power Rankings Week 8: Dolphins Move Up in Luck Rankings\nNick Giffen\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Week 8 Luck Rankings Picks: The First Luck-Free Slate In 5 Years\nNick Gi