 Pictured: Malik Willis.\nNFL Luck Rankings — a betting-focused version of NFL Power Rankings — are out for Week 8 of the 2026 season.\nThese NFL rankings are designed to help you identify which teams’ results have been luckier — or unluckier — than their on-field performance indicates. When there is a large difference in luck","published_at":"2026-10-27T19:13:21.000Z","confidence":0.74,"author":"Nick Giffen","captured_at":"2026-10-29T15:02:04.040Z","body":"Turn your sports knowledge into winning\npredictions\n21+ or 18+ in Certain Locations. 19+ in ON. Please Play Responsibly. Gambling Problem? Call 1-800-GAMBLER. Visit connexontario.ca or Call 1-866-531-2600 in ON.\nNo Code Needed\nHome NFL\nNFL Power Rankings Week 8: Dolphins Move Up in Luck Rankings\nNick Giffen\nPredictive Analyst\nDownload App\nUpdated:\nOct 27, 2026, 03:14 PM EDT\nUpdated:\nOct 27, 2026, 03:14 PM EDT\n1 min read\nPRO\nCredit: USA TODAY Network via Reuters Connect. Pictured: Malik Willis.\nNFL Luck Rankings — a betting-focused version of NFL Power Rankings — are out for Week 8 of the 2026 season.\nThese NFL rankings are designed to help you identify which teams’ results have been luckier — or unluckier — than their on-field performance indicates. When there is a large difference in luck between two teams, there has been proven success in betting on the unlucky team.\nThis season, we've introduced Luck Rankings Version 3.1, which is just a slight modification to last year's methodology. For more on the changes, check out our  season primer to understand what's different and how to use it to bet on the NFL.\nFor Version 3.1, when the Luck Score is 1.9 or higher, unlucky teams are 87-45 against the closing spread — the hardest lines to beat.\nThat equates to a 65.9% cover rate when pushes are removed over a sample size of 131 games. This season, unlucky sides are 5-2 against the closing spread (71.4%).\nHere's how our NFL Luck Rankings shake out before Week 8. Be sure to check back on Wednesday when I break down the Week 8 luck-based sides and totals.\nNFL Week 8 Luck Rankings\nNote:  Luck % represents the win probability swing between a team’s expected winning percentage from their on-field performance and their actual winning percentage. Lucky teams may regress and could be overvalued by betting markets, while the opposite may be true for unlucky teams.\nTop Stories\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Prediction, Pick, Odds for NFL Thursday Night Football on October 29\nSean Koerner\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Anytime Touchdown Props for NFL Thursday Night Football\nGilles Gallant\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Player Props for Josh Jacobs and Savion Williams\nSam Farley\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nPanthers vs Packers Spread Prediction: Pros Betting This 57% ATS System\nPJ Walsh\nOct 29, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Playoff Picture: Week 8 AFC Division Odds & Futures Reset\nBrandon Anderson\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Week 8 Pick’em, Confidence Pool Picks, Projections, Ratings\nSean Koerner\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nNFL\nNFL Betting Primer: Trends, Stats, Systems for Every Game\nEvan Abrams\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Week 8 Luck Rankings Picks: The First Luck-Free Slate In 5 Years\nNick Giffen\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\n2026 Live NFL Quarterback Power Rankings: Every QB’s Value Against the Spread\nEvan Abrams\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nBookBias: The NFL Public Betting Database for QBs, Coaches & Teams\nEvan Abrams\nOct 27, 2026 UTC\nPRO\nNFL\nNFL Anytime Touchdown Machine: Live TD Odds, Trends and More\nEvan Abrams\nOct 28, 2026 UTC\nFree Guide: 10 Tips to Hit Bigger Same Game Parlays More Often\n10 real, data-backed strategies for SGP bettors. Just enter your email and we'll send it.\nFollow Us On Social","revision_hash":"e010b028953203ff761e3506ad2612c870d1a6b21195b9ce7a541f6af25d4a85"}]$nfl_articles_fc9b12c2cf17dc51$::jsonb) AS x(
